x_comment('x_rateOfFire-Cyclic',"(#$rateOfFire-Cyclic GUN RATE) indicates the number of rounds per minute that can be fired. The unit of RATE to use is #$TimesPerMinute. This predicate can be used for most #$ProjectileLaunchers that have a store of projectiles. The obvious examples are the instances of #$MachineGun that have a large store of bullets that can be fired at a rapid rate. Less obvious examples include the #$Pistols that can fire six bullets at the #$rateOfFire-Cyclic, after which one must pause for the #$reloadTime of that pistol. For certain instances of #$MissileLauncher the #$rateOfFire-Cyclic is determined by the #$reloadTime: the time it takes to reload the launcher after firing a missile, determines the rate at which one can fire missiles.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6b56).
