x_comment('x_off-UnderspecifiedSurface',"(#$off-UnderspecifiedSurface ACT LOC) states that an abstract\nlocational relation holds between ACT and LOC, where LOC is an\n#$SurfaceRegion-Underspecified and ACT is some action requiring an ablative\nrole.  Only things which can be conceptualized as surfaces are thus\nallowable as the second argument to an 'off' relation. 'Off' is thus\nsemantically more restrictive than 'from', and implies a touching of\nsurfaces. Probably because of the strong relation to writing, the\nnotion of a topic in English is conceived of as a\n#$SurfaceRegion-Underspecified (that is, one can write 'on a topic', the\ndebate can move 'off a topic', etc.).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6b64).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a6b64,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
