x_comment(x_cityBlockBoundedBy,"(#$cityBlockBoundedBy BLOCK ST1 ST2 ST3 ST4) means that BLOCK is bounded by streets ST1 - ST4 such that if one starts on ST1 (where it borders BLOCK) and circles around BLOCK making  only right-hand turns one will travel along ST1, ST2, ST3, and ST4, in that order.  The region immediately surrounding the  block must be an #$UrbanArea that has a #$GridStreetSystem running through it.  To have this predicate correctly relate a given city block BLOCK to its bordering streets, one can fill its arg2 position with any  of the four streets that borders BLOCK, and then continue to fill in the remaining argument-places according to the order in which one would travel along the other three streets if one were circling BLOCK in a clockwise fashion (i.e. by  making only right-hand turns).  See also #$CityBlockFn and #$CityGridSectionFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6bb9).
