x_comment('x_Label-IBO',"The collection of all labels, namely those #$InformationBearingObjects that serve to identify the object to which they are attached.  This is the most general form of such things and includes a wide range of examples.  Easily identified subsets include #$ProductLabels and #$AddressLabels.  Other, not so obvious examples include a radio isotope that serves to identify a particular gene.  Thus an intangible projection of light onto a wall cannot serve as a label although it may contain information about something (see #$containsInformationAbout).  A borderline positive example is a magnetic strip containing information about the object to which it is attached.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6be2).
