x_comment('x_SurfaceArea-WholeSurfaceFn',"This function denotes the surface area of the entire surface of an object; it applies to 3-D objects and to 2-D objects.  If a 2-D object is deemed to have a front and back side we may want to define its surface area as twice its area.  However, if it does not, the surface area of a 2-D object and its area may be equal. The surface area of an object is the sum of the areas of all of the surfaces that define the boundary of the object on all sides, including undersides.  See also #$SurfaceArea-TopSurfaceFn, to use with lakes, tabletops, etc.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6be7).
