x_comment('x_enables-RemovesIncapacitatingFactors',"#$enables-RemovesIncapacitatingFactors expresses the notion that\nan agent is 'enabled' by an event in the following sense: the event removes\nall factors that are 'incapacitating', i.e., that would render the agent\ncertainly incapable of performing the action in question. More accurately,\n(#$enables-RemovesIncapacitatingFactors SIT AGENT ACT_TYPE) is true iff,\nin the given circumstances, SIT obtains, there are no factors\nthat would make AGENT certainly incapable of performing an instance of\nACT_TYPE, and SIT is the cause of there being no such incapacitating\nfactors. Hence #$enables-RemovesIncapacitatingFactors does not imply that\nthe agent is capable of doing ACT_TYPE_TOKEN: it merely entails that the\nprobability of the agent's succeeding at tokens of ACT_TYPE is\nnon-zero. Example: snow plowing enables people to drive after a snowstorm\nin this sense -- since a heavy snow cover on roadways #$incapacitates\ndriving.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6c22).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a6c22,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a6c22,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
