x_comment(x_ReverseMortgage,"The collection of #$MortgageAgreements in which the owner of a #$HumanResidence recieves money or a #$SecuredLineOfCredit (or some combination of these) taken from the equity the owner has amassed by paying a previous #$MortgageAgreement on that property.  Such mortgages are usually given to senior citizens who have totally or nearly totally repaid any existing mortgage on their residences.  The #$MortgageAccount is typically settled when the #$borrower no longer occupies that residence.  The #$borrower on a #$ReverseMortgage cannot be forced to sell the residence to repay it as long as the #$borrower occupies that residence, even if the value of the loan exceeds the value of the residence.  The #$ReverseMortgage is usually easier to obtain than other #$HomeEquityLoans.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6c4a).
