x_comment(x_actionInapplicabilityConditions,"(#$actionInapplicabilityConditions GENERICPURPOSEFULACTION CYCFORMULA) asserts that an instance of the\nGENERICPURPOSEFULACTION is reasonable to plan to do within a particular #$Situation if only CYCFORMULA is NOT known to\nbe true. Note that for some action class like ACT, it is NOT the same to assert (#$actionApplicabilityConditions ACT (not\n(P ?x))) vs.  (#$actionInapplicabilityConditions ACT (P ?x)), because the former says that we must be able to PROVE (not\n(P ?x)), while the latter is weaker - we should only not know that (P ?x) holds. That is, we are allowed to create plans\nthat have an execution of ACT if we don't know that (P ?x), but we could discover ourselves to be uninformed. Using\n#$actionApplicabilityConditions, however, we could not create such plans unless we were certain that (not (P ?x)). Note\nalso that applicability conditions differ from preconditions - we can't try to plan to achive an applicability\ncondition.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6c5d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a6c5d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a6c5d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
