x_comment(x_distalToFrom,"(#$distalToFrom PART-1 PART-2 REF-POINT) means that the #$PartiallyTangible (often an #$AnimalBodyRegion) PART-1 lies in a #$DistalDirection of PART-2, from the point of reference REF-POINT (an #$AnimalBodyPart -- generally, of a #$Person).  PART-1 and PART-2 are parts of the same body.  For example, (#$distalToFrom FredsThumb FredsElbow FredsTorso) expresses the fact that Fred's thumb is further away from his torso than his elbow is.  Note that PART-2 is therefore proximal to PART-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `proximal to'") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6c5f).
