x_comment(x_MtOfIndustryTypeFn,"The term (#$MtOfIndustryTypeFn INDUSTRYTYPE) denotes the\n\n#$Microtheory containing the assertions pertaining primarily to the collection\n\nINDUSTRYTYPE of all localized industries of a certain kind.  This function can be used for any industry type; it is not\n\n necessary to create a new, named \n\n'industry Microtheory' for an industry type when the industry type is already in the\n\nknowledge base.  For example, (#$MtOfIndustryTypeFn\n\n#$MetallurgyIndustry) would be the #$Microtheory for assertions relating\n\nprimarily to metallurgy, i.e. to the collection of all metallurgy industries\n\n worldwide.  (#$MetallurgyIndustry is the collection of all metallurgy industries, each of which is an instance of #$Industry-Localized; it is not itself an individual instance of #$Industry-Localized.)  Note that each\n\n instance of #$IndustryType,\n\n or value of the function #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn, is a collection of individual,\n\n regionally defined industries.  To generate the #$Microtheory for a specific individual regional industry,\n\n use #$MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6cd1).
