x_comment(x_OrganicFn,"The term `(#$OrganicFn THING-TYPE)' denotes the collection of instances of \n\nthe type THING-TYPE which are properly called `organic'. For example, \n\n`(#$OrganicFn (#$FruitFn #$TomatoPlant))' denotes the collection of organic\n\ntomatoes. Note that this function need not only take as arguments terms denoting\n\nfoodstuffs. For example, #$WoolStuff, would be an appropriate argument. Note also\n\nthat, while every product raised according to (#$OrganicMethodFn ACTIVITY), for some\n\nACTIVITY, will be an instance of (#$OrganicFn THING-TYPE) for some THING-TYPE, the reverse\n\nwill not be the case. Wild mushrooms, for examples, will typically be instances of\n\n(#$OrganicFn Mushroom).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6cf0).
