x_comment(x_GramPositiveBacterium,"The collection of all instances of #$Bacterium that are not decolorized after the process known as 'Gram Staining'. In this process the bacterial cells are rinsed with ethyl alcohol after being stained with a crystal violet dye. That the #$GramPositiveBacterium retain the stain indicates that the cells lack an outer membrane. Another feature that distinguishes them from the #$GramNegativeBacterium is that their cell walls have molecules on them known as teichoic acids which regulate the growth of the cell wall. Antibiotics to work against the #$GramPositiveBacterium are engineered to interfere with these molecules.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6cf7).
