x_comment(x_cityGridSectionBoundedBy,"(#$cityGridSectionBoundedBy SECTION ST1 ST2 ST3 ST4) means that SECTION is a roughly rectangular urban region that is completely bounded by segments of each of the streets ST1 - ST4.  The relative order (but not the absolute positions) of the 2nd - 5th arguments here is  important: it should be physically possible to circle completely  SECTION once by starting along ST1 and making successive right-hand turns on ST2, ST3, ST4, and back onto ST1.  SECTION must be part of a region that has a #$GridStreetSystem running through it.  To have this predicate correctly relate a given street-bounded rectangular city section SECTION to the four streets that border it, one can fill its arg2 position with  any of the four streets, and then continue to fill in the remaining argument-places according to the order in which one would travel along the other three streets if one were circling SECTION in a clockwise fashion (i.e. by making only right-hand turns). See also #$CityGridSectionFn, #$citySectionBoundedBy, and #$cityBlockBoundedBy.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6d0a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a6d0a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a6d0a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
