x_comment(x_ParodyMovie,"A collection of #$ComedyMovies which spoofs traditional genres or a specific film, poking fun at its conventions or plotlines. The makers of these film types expect audiences to understand the well-established cliches and archetypes that are therein ridiculed with inside jokes and broad strokes. Often using slapstick techniques, parodies offer a lowbrow, tongue-in-cheek counterpoint to the more serious revisionist approach used by movements like the French New Wave and genres like Spaghetti westerns which favor subversive tactics.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6d46).
