x_comment(x_infoStructureOfCW,"(#$infoStructureOfCW CONCEPTUALWORK STRUCTURE) means that INFOSTRUCTURE is an #$AbstractInformationStructure corresponding to the whole of CONCEPTUALWORK. For example, #$MobyDickNovel is expressed by one #$AbstractInformationStructure which is the complete sequence of words which Melville penned as well as by another #$AbstractInformationStructure which is the #$TextString of the sequence of characters with which those words were written.  Similarly, a song [#$Song-CW] may have one structure which is its lyrics [#$Lyric-WordsToSong], another being a normal musical score including notes & text, and a third being an instance of #$GuitarTablatureText.  This predicate allows us to make assertions about information structures used in a particular work without reference to any instantiation of that work.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6d7a).
