x_comment(x_MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn,"The term\n\n (#$MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn REGIONINDUSTRY) denotes the\n\n#$Microtheory or 'context' containing the assertions pertaining primarily to the the\n\n specific individual regional #$Industry-Localized \n\nREGIONINDUSTRY.  This function can be used for any regional #$Industry-Localized; it is not\n\n necessary to create a new, named \n\n'industry Microtheory' for a regional industry when the instance of #$Industry-Localized is already in the knowledge base.  For example, (#$MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn\n\nGermanMetallurgyIndustry) would be the #$Microtheory for assertions relating\n\nprimarily to the German  metallurgy industry.  Note \n\nthat each value of the function #$MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn\n\n is the Microtheory for an individual regionally defined #$Industry-Localized.  This is in contrast to the function #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn, which applies to collections of individual, regionally defined industries.  To generate the microtheory for all of the industry type, i.e. the collection of all individual regional industries of a certain kind, use #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6d7e).
