x_comment(x_termCreationTime,"(#$termCreationTime TERM TIME) means that TERM was ``first used'' at TIME (TIME specifies a particular day in YYYYMMDD syntax.). For example, if TERM is an #$CycLAssertion which first appeared  in the KB due to a #$HumanCyclist directly (aka ``locally'') asserting it, then the #$termCreationTime is the same as the #$assertionAssertTime for that assertion.  However, if TERM is an #$CycLAssertion which was only deduced and not directly asserted, then #$termCreationTime is when the assertion was deduced.  If TERM were *both* directly asserted and deduced, then #$termCreationTime is the time of earliest assertion or deduction.  The analogous is true for NATs (see #$CycLNonAtomicTerm); the #$termCreationTime of a NAT is the earliest date on which it was referenced in a local or deduced #$CycLAssertion.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6d86).
