x_comment(x_CityGridSectionFn,"(#$CityGridSectionFn ST1 ST2 ST3 ST4) denotes the unique, roughly rectangular urban region (if any) that is completely  bounded by segments of each of the streets ST1 - ST4.  The relative order (but not the absolute positions) of the arguments here is  important: it should be physically possible to circle completely  the bounded area once by starting along ST1 and making successive  right-hand turns on ST2, ST3, ST4, and back onto ST1.  The bounded  area must be part of a region that has a #$GridStreetSystem running  through it.  To have this function return a given street-bounded  rectangular city section SECTION, one can fill its arg1 position with  any of the four streets that borders SECTION, and then continue to  fill in the remaining argument-places according to the order in which  one would travel along the other three streets if one were circling  SECTION in a clockwise fashion (i.e. by making only right-hand turns). See also #$CitySectionFn and #$CityBlockFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6db0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a6db0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
