x_comment(x_negotiators,"(#$negotiators NEGOTIATION AGENT) means that AGENT participates, deliberately, as a negotiating party, in the negotiating event (instance of #$Negotiating) NEGOTIATION. The intent is that #$negotiators be broad in some respects, yet narrow in others. Consider the negotiations that occurred in the Spring of 1998 with the goal of producing an agreement between Unionist and Republican factions in Northern Ireland. Assuming the existence of appropriate constants, these would be correct assertions: (#$negotiators <the negotiation> <the Unionist faction>), (#$negotiators <the negotiation> <the Republican faction>), since the two mentioned factions were the parties seeking to reach an agreement in the negotiations. It would also be correct to say (#$negotiators <the negotiations> MartinMcGuinness), since McGuinness acted as a representative of one of the negotiating factions. However, although in an informal sense the United States and its representative, George Mitchell, acted as 'negotiators', by playing the role of promoting progress in the negotiations, both the following would be incorrect assertions: (#$negotiators <the negotiations> #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica), (#$negotiators <the negotiations> GeorgeMitchell). To describe the role the US and Sen. Mitchell played in the negotiations, use #$mediators.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6dbd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a6dbd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a6dbd,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
