x_comment(x_WhiteMagic,"#$WhiteMagic is a kind of #$Magic such that the effects of elements of #$WhiteMagic are generally believed to be beneficial or at least to have a beneficial purpose.  Who is it that generally believes this?  This is a function of the current #$Microtheory.  In some #$Microtheorys, most people may believe in the possibility of #$Magic, but it is generally believed that no magic can have beneficial effects.  In such a #$Microtheory, the extent of #$WhiteMagic would be the empty set.  In other #$Microtheorys, general belief may be that some people perform #$WhiteMagic with beneficial intent but that these actions have no effects.  Of course, there are numerous possibilities about what 'general belief' about #$WhiteMagic would entail, and thus many correspondingly different possible #$Microtheorys. Alchemists in the european tradition were often considered capable of performing #$WhiteMagic.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6e23).
