x_comment(x_salientURL,"(#$salientURL THING URL) means that the information contained at the #$UniformResourceLocator URL, is salient to #$Thing.  Salience is a function of the microtheory that the #$salientURL assertion is placed in.  For example, in the #$WebSearchEnhancementMt, an eCyc search which returned URL would count as a good hit for a query that disambiguates to THING.  If URL points to something which most internet saavy people would refer to as ``the homepage for'' THING, then #$homepage is a more appropriate predicate to use.  Note that URL is assumed to be a publicly accessible entity on the #$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource.  Thus, pointers to documents on the cycorp internal filesystem are not legitimate values for URL.  For such documents #$salientCycorpPathname is appropriate.  Where possible please use the more descriptive predicate #$salientURLPrintString rather than #$salientURL. (#$BillJ 1/20/2000)") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6e85).
