x_comment(x_complementaryNucleicAcidSequences,"(#$complementaryNucleicAcidSequences SEQ1 SEQ2) means that that SEQ1\n\nand SEQ2 are lists of nucleotides such that the nucleotides that\n\ncompose SEQ2 complement the nucleotides that compose SEQ1, and vice\n\nversa.  Another way to think of this: given that\n\n(#$complementaryNucleicAcidSequences SEQ1 SEQ2), if someone were to replace every\n\nnucleotide in SEQ1 with its complementary nucleotide (i.e., the nucleotide with which it forms a complementary base pair), the result would\n\nbe SEQ2, and if someone were to replace every nucleotide in SEQ2 with\n\nits complementary nucleotide, the result would be SEQ1.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6e9e).
