x_comment(x_distanceInBlocksOfStreet,"This predicate relates two things located in a \ncity or town in terms of the number of blocks away they \nare from each other.  (#$distanceInBlocksOfStreet OBJ1 OBJ2 N)\nmeans that in order to get from OBJ1 to OBJ2 by the shortest\nroute using city streets, one must travel a total of N \ninstances of #$BlockOfStreet.  OBJ1 and OBJ2 must each be\n#$onPath some instance or other of #$Street-Generic, and if\nthey are on different streets, those streets must be (directly\nor indirectly) connected to each other within the same \n#$StreetSystem.  Since the lengths of street blocks vary \nconsiderably, a given distance in street blocks cannot be \ngenerally associated with any specific absolute distance.  \nStill, this predicate is useful for rough estimates of, and \ncomparisons between, distances.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6ed7).
