x_comment(x_nearestGenlMt,"A specialization of #$genlMt.  (#$nearestGenlMt MT NEAR-MT) means that NEAR-MT is a \"nearest\" microtheory of which MT is a specialization.  That is, (#$genlMt MT NEAR-MT) holds, MT is not identical to NEAR-MT, and there is no reified #$Microtheory NEARER-MT distinct from MT and NEAR-MT such that both (#$genlMt MT NEARER-MT) and (#$genlMt NEARER-MT NEAR-MT) hold.  Note that #$nearestGenlMt is non-assertible (see #$notAssertible), since its extension at any given time depends upon (and so must be recomputed from) the current state of the #$genlMt hierarchy in the Cyc Knowledge Base.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6f1a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a6f1a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
