x_comment(x_SpecifiedGameType,"Instances of #$SpecifiedGameType are types of games, specific as to the name and the rules used.  Each instance is a collection, a spec of #$GameEvent, whose instances are particular events in which the game is played from beginning to end.  For example, #$IndivPentathlonEvent is an instance of #$SpecifiedGameType, because all instances use the same set of rules, and consist of all the moves of a game until one of the players wins.  Not every instance of #$SpecifiedGameType has to consist of instances where there is a winner, because there might be games that don't have winners; the important thing is that the instances are by default played to completion (whatever that means for the particular type of game).  Also, not every spec of #$GameEvent is a #$SpecifiedGameType.  E.g., 'SolitaryGameEvent' (the class of games played by one person) would not be a #$SpecifiedGameType since that class isn't specific as to the name of the game and the rules used.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6f6d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a6f6d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
