x_comment(x_valueEquals,"(#$valueEquals X Y) means nothing more than X = Y, except that a\n#$valueEquals assertion also #$evaluates NATs formed with an\n#$EvaluatableFunction expression. This is not the intended behavior of\n#$equals. Thus, the proper way to state that two #$Lists L001 and L002\nhave the same length would be\n(#$valueEquals (#$LengthOfListFn L001) (#$LengthOfListFn L002)). If\n#$valueEquals is replaced with #$equals in the previous assertion, one will\nnot get the correct inferential results, since #$equals will not evaluate\nthe denotation of the 2 NATs in argument position.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6f74).
