x_comment(x_holdsReciprocallyOf,"#$holdsReciprocallyOf ?SET ?PRED means that for any two distinct elements of ?SET, ?PRED holds of them.  For example, the statement 'Todd and Erik are friends' can be represented as (#$holdsReciprocallyOf (#$TheSet #$ToddHughes #$ErikLarson) #$friends). This implies both (#$friends #$ToddHughes #$ErikLarson) and (#$friends #$ErikLarson #$ToddHughes).  If the example set contained a third member, then there would be 3!=6 total implications of that type, and so on.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6f84).
