x_comment(x_argAndRestGenl,"A ternary #$ArgGenlPredicate (q.v.) used to \n\nplace a specified #$genls based argument-type constraint on a given \n\n#$VariableArityRelation (q.v.) with respect to any of its argument-places \n\nwhose ordinal position is greater than or equal to a specified number.\n\n(#$argAndRestGenl RELN N COL) means that, as a necessary condition for \n\nsemantic well-formedness, anything given as the Nth or greater argument \n\nto RELN must be an specialization of COL.  Thus a closed formula \n\n(RELN ARG1..ARG(N)..ARG(N+1)..) is well-formed only if each of ARG(N)..ARG(N+1).. is an instance of COL.  See also #$argsGenl and #$argAndRestIsa.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a6fad).
