x_comment(x_interArgReln,"A quaternary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln RELN M N BINPRED) means that a ground atomic formula (or \"GAF\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence) or closed non-atomic term (or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) built from RELN is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the Mth and Nth arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ..ARGM..ARGN..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARGM ARGN) holds.  For further explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.  See also the more specific binary #$InterArgRelnPredicates, each of which is defined for two particular argument-places of RELN (e.g. #$interArgReln1-2 and #$interArgReln4-2).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7021).
