x_comment('x_CharacterToken-Inscribed',"The collection of all inscribed tokens of individual\n  abstract characters.  More precisely, #$CharacterToken-Inscribed\n  is a  specialization of #$CharacterToken each of whose instances \n  is a physical marking, #$Engraving, or character-in-relief that \n  represents or realizes a particular instance of #$Character-Abstract \n  in some writing system.  Instances include character tokens that \n  are written or printed on paper, carved into stone, displayed on \n  computer monitors or LCDs, generated by skywriting, and created \n  by Brailling.  Examples such as these last two demonstrate \n  why #$CharacterToken-Inscribed is a proper generalization \n  of #$WrittenCharacter.  Inscribed characters are \n  identified (both in theory and in practice) as tokens of\n  particular abstract characters largely by their shapes,\n  though context and creator's intention also figure in \n  (see #$tokensCharacter).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7034).
