x_comment(x_EconomicEmbargo,"The collection of events in which one nation, acting as an agent, officially forbids all economic commerce with a particular country, and takes additional steps to prevent and/or intercept all relevant instances of commerce trade.  Often, but not always, embargoes are cases of punishing or imposing sanctions.  An embargo can be thought of as the most extreme possible case of imposing trade restrictions. In CycL, we take an embargo to be the combination of the legal/official edict interdicting commerce and the actual steps taken to enforce the edict, eg, the conducting of additional customs inspections in ports.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7060).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7060,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
