x_comment(x_IrreversibleReformulation,"A property of reformulator rules.  A reformulator rule RULE having\n\nthe property #$IrreversibleReformulation is such that one of the following\n\n4 conditions obtains: (1) If RULE, when \n\napplied in the forward direction to a given \n\nexpression PRE-FORM, yields the expression POST-FORM, then RULE, \n\nwhen applied in the backward direction to POST-FORM, \n\ndoes not yield PRE-FORM.\n\n(2) If RULE, when \n\napplied in the backward direction to a given \n\nexpression PRE-FORM, yields the expression POST-FORM, then RULE, \n\nwhen applied in the forward direction to POST-FORM, \n\ndoes not yield PRE-FORM.\n\n(3) Applying RULE in the forward direction is impossible.\n\n(4) Applying RULE in the backward direction is impossible.\n\nSee also #$OneWayReformulation-Forward and #$OneWayReformulation-Backward") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7067).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7067,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
