x_comment(x_profileDBQueries,"This #$QuaternaryPredicate is used to state the CycL and English (template) versions of queries used by various #$Cyc database applications and prototypes.  ARG1 is the type of object the query is about.  ARG2 is the type of information the query is asking for (the type of information the answer will consist of).  ARG3 is a CycL query expression.  ARG4 is a list consisting of a keyword followed by an English query (template) string.  The keyword may be :text or :tabular.  It indicates how the query answer should be formatted.  If the keyword is :text, the English query string should contain the Cyc variable ?subject, which denotes the object being profiled (the object the query is about).  This object will be an instance of ARG1.  If the keyword is :tabular, the English query string will be followed by two lists: a list of field (column) name strings, and a list of Cyc variables.  Each field name string corresponds to one of the variables.  The corresponding elements must occur in the same positions in their respective lists.  This arcane syntax allows the answer to be formatted as a table, if so desired.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a709a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a709a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a709a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
