x_comment('x_exchangeRateDuring-Market',"(#$exchangeRateDuring-Market UM1 UM2 THING NR) means that NR is the average market exchange rate of the #$UnitOfMoney UM1 for the #$UnitOfMoney UM2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (THING will often be a calendar time period.)  That is, NR UM1's can be traded for 1 UM2, and conversely, in a market that is not controlled by the #$GeopoliticalEntity whose currency UM1 is.  For example, the fact that during October of 1995 the market exchange rate between Liberian and United States dollars was 50 Liberian dollars for 1 US dollar can be expressed as (#$exchangeRateDuring-Market #$Dollar-Liberia #$Dollar-UnitedStates (#$MonthFn #$October (#$YearFn 1995)) 50).  See also #$exchangeRateDuring-Official and #$exchangeRateDuring.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a70a2).
