x_comment(x_JobPosition,"#$JobPosition is the collection of all job positions conceived as #$StaticSituations that exist at an #$Organization. A #$JobPosition can be characterized by a set of #$duties (see also #$dutiesOfAgentInJob) that the person filling the #$JobPosition will be expected to perform. In practice, we often use instances of #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg instead of specializations of #$JobPosition to represent types of job positions. See also #$JobPositionTypeFn. A #$JobPosition can be either open or filled (see #$JobOpen and #$JobFilled). A #$JobPosition is not the same as a #$WorkAgreement or a #$HasPositionRelationship. These latter two exist only when a #$JobPosition is filled by a #$Person who enters into a relation with the #$Organization that has the #$JobPosition. For each #$JobPosition, there can be only a single #$Person who fills it for a given temporal interval, although two different #$Persons may successively fill the same #$JobPosition. Use #$versionOfJobPosition to relate a #$JobPosition to a #$HasPositionRelationship.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7144).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7144,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
