x_comment(x_embeddedCylinderInSheet,"The predicate (#$embeddedCylinderInSheet CYLINDER SHEET) means that the #$SheetOfSomeStuff SHEET surrounds all of the #$LongAndThin object CYLINDER or a section its major axis which extends through the length of SHEET.  The predicate is agnostic as to whether the cylindrical object is part of the sheet.  \n\nIf the #$LongAndThin object is a part of SHEET, it need not be an internal part.\n\nExamples of this predicate include wires in a ribbon cable, #$Threads in a piece of #$Cloth, and lacrimal ducts in an #$Eyelid.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a716b).
