x_comment(x_salaryIncome,"(#$salaryIncome PERSON MONETARY_FLOW_RATE) means that #$Person has an #$occupation as an #$Employee and earns salary from this employment at the specified rate.  The rate is the official rate of payment to the employee.  It includes funds withheld for taxes, union dues, insurance, retirement, and/or other purposes.  Income from sources other than a salary are not included in this rate.  If the rate is expressed in monetary units per hour or per day, that refers to working hours (or days), so that the number is not multiplied by the number of hours (or days) in a year to obtain a monetary rate per year.  In addtion, note that this rate can vary from time to time.  Someone may have a #$salaryIncome during the day of one value, but a different value during the night when working at a second job for a different employer.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a717e).
