x_comment(x_subStringTokens,"This predicate is a specialization of #$subSeries that\n\n  relates a serial string token to other serial string tokens that \n\n  occur within it (see #$CharacterStringToken-Serial).  (#$subStringTokens SERIES SUBSERIES) means that \n\n  SUBSERIES is a sub-token-series of SERIES.  That is, all of the \n\n  members of SUBSERIES are members of SERIES, that SERIES and \n\n  SUBSERIES share the same ordering principle, and that, if the first \n\n  member of SUBSERIES is the Mth member of SERIES, the Nth member of \n\n  SUBSERIES is the (N+M-1)th member of SERIES.  So a #$subStringTokens \n\n  is an uninterrupted \"slice\" of the whole.  Note that any character\n\n  token series is trivially a #$subStringTokens of itself.  See also #$concatenateStringTokens.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7186).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7186,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a7186,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
