x_comment(x_nthStreetOver,"This predicate relates a street to another street that \n\nis a specified number of \"streets over\" from the first.\n\n(#$nthStreetOver STREET1 STREET2 N) means that STREET1 and\n\nSTREET2 run parallel to each other in some #$GridStreetSystem,\n\nand that, for any given perpendicular street XSTREET that \n\nintersects both of them, the distance between the two \n\nintersections is a #$distanceInBlocksOfStreet of N blocks\n\nalong XSTREET.  For example, in a typical grid system, 15th\n\nStreet is five streets over from 10th Street.  Of course, 5th\n\nStreet is also five streets over from 10th Street; so to \n\nidentify a particular street in a given context using this \n\npredicate, it is generally also necessary to specify a \n\ndirection from STREET1 to STREET2.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7194).
