x_comment('x_interArgIsa3-2',"A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).   (#$interArgIsa3-2 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that,  when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the third argument to RELN,  a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the second argument  must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then  (RELN ARG1 ARG2 INST ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed only  if ARG2 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic  well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a71d9).
