x_comment(x_purposeOfSocialEvent,"This predicate can be used to represent the goal in those instances of #$SocialOccurrence that exist so that participants in them can reach some particular goal. (#$purposeOfSocialEvent EVENT FORMULA) means that the goal of EVENT (as determined by at least one participant in EVENT) is represented by FORMULA. When EVENT is an instance of #$CooperationEvent, all  #$cooperatingParticipants in EVENT have the goal represented by FORMULA and are participating in EVENT because they believe doing so will help bring about that goal. This predicate is particularly useful in connection with instances of #$CooperationEvent but can also be relevant for other subcollections of #$SocialOccurrence, such as #$MilitaryExercise,  #$HelpingAnAgent or #$BusinessEvent.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a71fc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a71fc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
