x_comment(x_quantityInfluenceFunctionStrength,"(#$quantityInfluenceFunctionStrength TIME THING QUANTITY-SLOT FUNCTION-TYPE STRENGTH) means that during TIME the value of QUANTITY-SLOT for successive time slices of THING is subjected to some influence.  The strength of this influence is specified by STRENGTH.  The higher the STRENGTH of a given influence, the more likely that the time course of actual changes in QUANTITY-SLOT during TIME will follow the shape that elements of FUNCTION-TYPE have.  If two influences are present, the actual time course of QUANTITY-SLOT follows resembles the shape of its corresponding FUNCTION-TYPE most.  When STRENGTH is unknown or irrelevant use #$quantityInfluenceFunction.  See #$quantityChangeFunction for making statements about the *actual* time course of some quantity.  See also #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for important pointers to related vocabulary.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7236).
