x_comment(x_CollectionTypeTypeByDisjointness,"A collection of instances of #$CollectionTypeType.  #$CollectionTypeTypeByDisjointness is a collection of the three major types of #$CollectionTypes: #$CollectionType is the most general type of #$CollectionType and tells nothing about how the collections in the type are related (no disjointness restrictions).  #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType (a spec of #$CollectionType) gives some disjointness constraints, but with some exceptions.  #$DisjointCollectionType gives the most disjointness constraints--all instances of any instance of #$DisjointCollectionType must by disjoint collections.  #$CollectionTypeTypeByDisjointness is in the KB to explicitly show how #$CollectionType, #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType, and #$DisjointCollectionType are related to anyone dealing with #$CollectionTypes.  The facet assertion (#$facets-Covering #$CollectionType #$CollectionTypeTypeByDisjointness) states that any instance of #$CollectionType should be checked for possible membership in #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType or #$DisjointCollectionType.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a725f).
