x_comment(x_VulnerableToTearDropAttack,"#$VulnerableToTearDropAttack is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has this vulnerability if it is running an operating system that fails to handle a deliberately malformed\n UDP (#$UserDatagramProtocol) packet.  In a Teardrop attack, a remote attacker sends one or multiple fragmented UDP packets to a host, which have the correct (according to the IP header) fragment sizes but false (according to the IP header) fragment offsets.  The result is that the destination host's memory allocation fails and the OS crashes. ") :- x_cid(a65b16526a726b).
