x_comment(x_objectTranslating,"(#$objectTranslating MOVEMENT OBJECT) means that in MOVEMENT, OBJECT undergoes some salient translational or place-to-place motion (see #$Movement-TranslationEvent).  #$objectTranslating is stronger than its generalization #$objectMoving, since the latter is agnostic as to whether  the moving object is rotating or translating.  When considering using #$objectTranslating, one should also consider whether its specialization #$translatesFromTo applies.  If MOVEMENT is a #$Translation-SingleTrajectory,  then any #$objectTranslating in any #$timeSlices of MOVEMENT is #$onPath the #$motionPathway-Complete of MOVEMENT.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a729e).
