x_comment(x_SportsVersionFn,"This function maps from #$ExistingObjectTypes to the versions of those types that are suitable for use in sporting activities.  The sport versions will share many of the same characteristics, but will not share the same purpose.  For example, the purpose of a #$Spear is to help its user kill animals, while a #$Javelin (i.e. (#$SportsVersionFn #$Spear) is used in distance throwing competitions).  Likewise, this function when applied to #$Guns would yield guns that are used for sport, but NOT used for killing, which is the primary purpose of most #$Guns.  Guns that are used for sport hunting (i.e. not subsistence hunting) would not be considered sports versions, because they retain the primary purpose of guns-- killing.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a72a3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a72a3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
