x_comment('x_relativeOrientation-Underspecified',"(#$relativeOrientation-Underspecified OBJ1 OBJ2 ORIENT) states\n\nthat relative to OBJ2, OBJ1 occupies the #$OrientedLocation-Underspecified\n\ndenoted by ORIENT. This predicate allows us to express relativistic notions\n\nof orientation, such as 'sick is better than dead', 'ecstatic' is better than\n\n'happy', etc. More usefully, it allows us to define the lexical semantics of\n\nactions like 'to raise X' (the subabstraction of X after the raise occupies\n\nan upwardly oriented state relative to the subabstraction of X just before\n\nthe raise). Many verbs, such as 'improve', 'increase' and 'enhance' have this\n\ncore meaning.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a730e).
