x_comment(x_ConstrainedRotation,"#$Movement-Rotation constrained by physical contact with a solid or liquid external object along an external or internal boundary of the rotating object.  Physical contact between the rotating body and the external object continues during the rotation, although pairs of points of the two objects in contact may change.  Rigidly connected #$physicalParts of an object undergo #$ConstrainedRotation if the part to which it they are connected also undergo #$ConstrainedRotation.  #$RollingOnASurface, spinning on an axle, #$BeltedMotion, bolt insertion, etc. are all #$ConstrainedRotation s.  A borderline case would be juice whirling within a pitcher just after being stirred.  A maple seed helicoptering in its descent is not an example of #$ConstrainedRotation; neither is a whirlpool in a body of water.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a733c).
