x_comment('x_objectSought-Definite',"The expression `(#$objectSought-Definite SEARCH SEEKER CRITERION\nOBJECT)' means that SEARCH is a #$LookingForSomething-Definite which is\n#$performedBy SEEKER, and that OBJECT is the unique thing which\nsatisfies the #$PossibleIdentificationCondition which is the #$searchCriterion-Definite\nfor the search. This predicate is agent-relative\nin some respects and non-agent-relative in others. Including the searchCriterion-Definite\nmakes is agent-relative in a certain sense. \nOn the other hand, the term used to denote the OBJECT need not\nbe one the agent would use or even recognize as denoting the OBJECT, so\nthat the arg4 position of this predicate is not opaque (see\n#$opaqueArgument). Nor need the SEEKER ever be in a position to recognize\nthat the OBJECT satisfies the CRITERION: in some cases the SEEKER may fail\nto recognize that the OBJECT satisfies the CRITERION even upon coming face\nto face with said object, because of the guise under which OBJECT is\npresented.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7369).
