x_comment('x_enables-RemovesContraryFactors',"#$enables-RemovesContraryFactors expresses the notion that an\nagent may be 'enabled' by an event in the following sense: the event\nremoves all factors that are 'contrary', i.e., that would decrease the\nlikelihood of the agent's success -- put another way: all factors that\nwould make it less likely that the agent would succeed in performing the\naction if she tried. More accurately, (#$enables-RemovesContraryFactors SIT\nAGENT ACT_TYPE) is true iff SIT obtains, there are no contrary factors for\nAGENT to do an instance of ACT_TYPE, and SIT is the cause of there being no\nsuch contrary factors. Hence #$enables-RemovesContraryFactors does not\nimply that the agent is in fact capable of doing an action: rather, it\nentails that, given SIT, the probability of the agent's success is\nincreased. Example: proper bicycle maintenance enables the cyclist to\ncomplete the race.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a73bd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a73bd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a73bd,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
