x_comment(x_LengthOfListFn,"The function #$LengthOfListFn, applied to a list, gives the length of the list, a non-negative integer.  Note that the length of LIST should not in general be considered the same as the cardinality of (#$SetOfListMembersFn LIST).  For example, given that LIST = (#$TheList A B C B D), (#$LengthOfListFn LIST) is 5 while the cardinality of (#$SetOfListMembersFn LIST) is 4.  When LIST is an instance of #$ListWithoutRepetition, nevertheless, the length of LIST is identical to the cardinality of (#$SetOfListMembersFn LIST).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a743f).
