x_comment(x_SecureMailGuard,"A spec of #$SecurityDevice that allows mail to be transferred electronically between the non-classified internet protocol router network (NIPRNET) (see #$NIPRNet-PathSystem) and the secret internet protocol router network (SIPRNET) (see #$SIPRNet-PathSystem). It is designed to allow Coalition users (who do not have access to SIPRNET) to exchange mail with American users (who do have access to SIPRNET) without allowing the Coalition users access to SIPRNET. The mail guard works by examining transmitted data and allowing only that in the right format to be released. It also may do security checks, word checks to look for sensitive information that should not be allowed through, and it supports content scanning, downgrade, releasability review, regrade, and sanitization.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a74a3).
