x_comment(x_ThoughtExperimenting,"This is the collection of instances in which a person does a thought experiment. Carrying out a thought experiment is a technique employed extensively in philosophy but also notably\n\nin relativistic physics and quantum mechanics. The idea is to achieve insight by\n\nimagining a particular sort of scenario and then trying to figure out what would\n\nor should happen or how the scenario should be evaluated. A philosophical example is the Experience\n\nMachine: would a life in which all of your apparent experiences were simulated by\n\na computer hooked up to your brain be as good as one in which you have the same experiences\n\nin the normal way? If not, then hedonism, the theory that the only intrinsically valuable thing is pleasure, is incorrect. Note that there need not\n\nbe a prior conceptual work of which such an activity is an instantiation. Thought experiments can be improvised.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a74af).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a74af,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
