x_comment(x_defaultSpecializedType,"(#$defaultSpecializedType GENERAL SPECIF) means that, in the current context and application, the default (most normal or typical) instances of the collection GENERAL are likely to be member of its intersection with the the Collection SPECIF (which my or may not be a subclass of GENERAL).   This is not a new logical construct (for any kind of default logic); rather it is to be used as a heuristic guide in specific applications.  If no other information about an individual is known other than that it is an instance of GENERAL, then assume tentatively that it is an instance of SPECIF.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a74c2).
