x_comment(x_MountableTransporter,"A #$MountableTransporter is a transporter that one `rides' or `rides on' but does not `ride in'.  This collection was originally created to enable the following sorts of natural language interpretations.  Anyone who is said to `ride' such an object is most likely to be the #$driverActor.  If someone `rides' a non #$MountableTransporter (e.g. a train) is most likely not a #$driverActor but a #$passengers.  Positive exemplars include horses, jet skis, motorcycles, bicycles.  Negative exemplars include cars, trains, planes.  A borderline positive example is a skateboard.  When one `rides' a skateboard one is most likely the #$driverActor, but, unlike typical #$MountableTransporters, one is also most likely not sitting.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a750b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a750b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
