x_comment('x_possessedWeaponRange-Max',"(#$possessedWeaponRange-Max AGENT WEAPON-TYPE RANGE) means that the weapons of type WEAPON-TYPE that AGENT possesses have the maximal range RANGE.  For example, suppose that AGENT possesses TYPE(1)-missiles, ..., TYPE(n)-missiles, whose maximal ranges (see weaponEffectiveRange-Max) are, respectively, RANGE(1), ..., RANGE(n). Then, if these are the only types of missiles that AGENT possesses, we have (#$possessedWeaponRange-Max AGENT #$Missile RANGE) where RANGE is the maximal one among RANGE(1), ..., RANGE(n).  Actually, RANGE is the same as (#$Maximum (#$TheSetOf TYPE (#$and (#$genls TYPE #$Missile) (#$relationInstanceExistsMany #$possesses AGENT TYPE))) (#$FunctionToArg 2 #$weaponEffectiveRange-Max)).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a752b).
