x_comment(x_FluidCirculating,"A #$FluidCirculating is a moving event in which pieces of the #$objectMoving are moving, but the #$objectMoving is not necessarily undergoing rotational (see #$Movement-Rotation) or translational motion (see #$Movement-TranslationEvent) as a whole.  E.g. the parts of a whirlpool are moving with respect to one another but the whirlpool as a whole may or may not be changing its location.  Tornadoes also undergo #$FluidCirculatings.  Note that if the tornado as a whole were undergoing motion it would be necessary to either make the #$FluidCirculating event also an element of some appropriate specialization of #$MovementEvent or to reify another event (which was not a #$FluidCirculating) to describe its motion as a whole.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7548).
