x_comment(x_reformulatorEquals,"A #$CycLReformulationRulePredicate that relates two CycL denotational terms.  When asserted in a #$Microtheory MT, (#$reformulatorEquals TERM-1 TERM-2) means that the #$CycLDenotationalTerm TERM-1 may be reformulated into the #$CycLDenotationalTerm TERM-2, or vice-versa (based on meta-properties of this rule and what mode the reformulator is in), in any #$Microtheory SPEC-MT such that (#$genlMt SPEC-MT MT) holds.  Free variables in TERM-1 and TERM-2 are shared, and may bind with CycL terms which match the template.  Note that (#$reformulatorEquals TERM-1 TERM-2) does _not_ necessarily imply (#$equals TERM-1 TERM-2), although this implication would hold if the reformualtion is a #$TruthPreservingReformulation (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a755d).
