x_comment('x_CharacterStringToken-Inscribed',"A specialization of #$CharacterStringToken    each of whose instances is a specific physical marking,    #$Engraving, or character-string-in-relief that represents or    realizes a particular abstract instance of #$CharacterString    in some writing system.  Most (but not all) inscribed    character-string tokens are serial, i.e. are physical series    consisting of one or more instances of #$CharacterToken-Inscribed   (see #$CharacterStringToken-Serial).  Examples of nonserial inscribed string tokens include those illegible or barely legible instances of    #$Signature that cannot be divided into discrete character    tokens.  #$CharacterStringToken-Inscribed is a proper   generalization of #$WrittenCharacterSequence, as things like    illegible signatures, skywriting, and Brailling are instances   of the former but not the latter.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7589).
