x_comment(x_AscendingEvent,"An event is an #$AscendingEvent if and only if its object (#$objectMoving) has a higher altitude (#$altitudeAboveSeaLevel) at the end of the event than it did at the beginning of the event.  Thus, some descent may occur during the ascent so long as the net affect is to increase altitude.  Climbing stairs, walking down a hill to the top of a higher hill, being lifted, and airplane taking off are exemplars of #$AscendingEvent.  Technically, a standing up or bread rising are not exemplars because the #$altitudeAboveSeaLevel of these objects is not higher at the end of the ascension.  (#$altitudeAboveSeaLevel is based on the distance between the bottom of the object and the mean sea level.)") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7604).
