x_comment('x_objectSought-DefiniteDeRe',"`(#$objectSought-DefiniteDeRe SEARCH SEEKER OBJECT)' means that\nSEARCH is a #$LookingForSomething-Definite which is #$performedBy SEEKER\nand that OBJECT is the (unique) object sought in the sense that it is the\nunique object that satisfies the SEEKER's #$searchCriterion-Definite.\nOften we will not know what this criterion is, so this predicate allows us\nto speak of the relation between the seeker and the object sought in the\nabsence of such knowledge. Note that the arg3 position is not opaque. This\nreflects the fact that this is a \"third-person perspective\"\npredicate. The term used to denote the object sought needn't match the way\nSEEKER conceives of that object.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7607).
