x_comment(x_mtPartonomicAbstractionLevel,"(#$mtPartonomicAbstractionLevel MT COLLECTION) means that when reasoning in (or with) the context MT, (instances of) classes of objects at about the level of partonomic abstraction indicated by COLLECTION should be attended to, or taken into account.  If you consider the knowledge base as a lattice of abstract concepts arranged in a hierarchical structure via the subparts/superparts relation (#$parts), then the further `up' or `down' the hierarchy you go from COLLECTION, the less likely it is that (instances of) these classes should be used in inferencing. Example: the assertions in MT might apply to wheel-and-axle assemblies, but not to bearings (part of a wheel-and-axle assembly), and not to cars (which have wheel-and-axle assemblies as parts).  See also #$mtSubsetAbstractionLevel.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7621).
