x_comment(x_Pony,"#$Pony is a collection, a specialization of #$Horse, each member of which is (thought to be) descended from the primitive pony of the ice age.  Each member of #$Pony is a member of a pony breed, however, only a few representative breeds are in Cyc as collections.  Modern instances of #$Pony are rarely if ever pure bred ponies, but are mixtures of various horse and pony breeds.  While some instances of #$Pony (of a specialization of #$Pony that represents a breed) are larger than some instances of #$Horse, in sports the pony is defined as any horse shorter than about 148 cm (in horse terminology about '14.2 hands').  Ponies are ridden by children or small adults.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7624).
