x_comment('x_consumerPriceIndex-USA',"The #$consumerPriceIndex-USA or 'CPI', is an index that measures the prices of consumer goods and services and is a measure of the pace of the effectsof monetary inflation in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.  The CPI is published by the US Department of Labor once a month (the number is calculated by the #$BureauOfLaborStatistics).  The CPI measures and compares, from month to month, the total cost of a statistically determined 'typical market basket' of goods and services consumed by U.S. households.  (#$consumerPriceIndex-USA DATE NUMBER) means that NUMBER is the CPI on DATE.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a762b).
