x_comment(x_Neutrino,"The collection of all neutrinos.  Neutrinos are #$SubAtomicParticle which are massless (or near massless), have a \"spin\" of +/- 1/2, lack charge, travel at (or near) the speed of light, and have an extremely low reaction cross-section.  There are three kinds of neutrinos, the electron-like, tau-like, and beta-like types, which are created in reactions in which their namesakes are also produced.  There is a theory that a single neutrino may change from one category to another, which would indicate that it must travel slower than the speed of light, and thus must have \"rest mass\".") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7658).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7658,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
