x_comment(x_reformulationOf,"(#$reformulationOf SIMPLE-TERM COMPLEX-TERM) means that SIMPLE-TERM and COMPLEX-TERM are definitionally or intensionally equal.  Also SIMPLE-TERM is a simpler form of COMPLEX-TERM.  That is, SIMPLE-TERM contains fewer nested #$Function-Denotationals than does COMPLEX-TERM.  Unlike #$equals, #$reformulationOf is strictly a #$HumanCyclist asserted form of equality.  #$reformulationOf differs from #$rewriteOf in that its COMPLEX-TERM argument is unreified. This allows us to state equalities between existing Cyc terms and NAUTS so that at dialogue time, a compositionally determined output of one of our parsers can be mapped to Cyc terms.  See #$ncRule for examples of such NAUTS.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7661).
