x_comment(x_decreasesVulnerabilityTo,"(decreasesVulnerabilityTo SITUATION OBJECT RESULT-TYPE) means that being in situation SITUATION decreases OBJECT's vulnerability to RESULT-TYPE.  This predicate is similar to #$makesVulnerableToDegree except that, unlike #$makesVulnerableToDegree, it expresses a relative decrease in OBJECT's vulnerability rather than an absolute degree of vulnerability.  It also resembles #$vulnerableIn, but there is an important difference that must be observed, namely that when using #$decreasesVulnerabilityTo one assumes that certain conditions coming into effect descrease vulnerability.  Therefore, it should not be used to declare vulnerabilities outright; Cyc should have to conlcude that a situation decreases an object's vulnerability to some result.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7683).
