x_comment(x_interArg3ResultIsa,"A ternary #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly #$isa based relationship holds between the third argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (#$interArg3ResultIsa FUNC INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the third argument to FUNC, then -- regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be -- the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG1 ARG2 INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the #$InterArgTypePredicates, #$interArg3ResultIsa _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but more flexible quaternary #$interArgResultIsa.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a76ca).
