x_comment('x_NarrativeTVShow-CW',"#$NarrativeTVShow-CW is the collection of all #$TVShow-CWs that are also #$Narratives. Thus, #$NarrativeTVShow-CWs tell a story and represent a structured sequence of events. Typically, the actors playing roles in a #$NarrativeTVShow-CW follow a script that describes the sequence of action and spoken lines. #$SoapOperas are positive examples of #$NarrativeTVShow-CW, whereas #$TVGameShows and #$LiveSportsTVShows are negative examples. #$NarrativeTVShow-CW can be characterized using the predicate #$hasAttributes and an instance of #$NarrativeGenre. Most #$NarrativeTVShow-CWs are instances of #$FictionalTVShow-CW. However, #$TVDocumentary and #$TVBiography are nonfictional #$NarrativeTVShow-CWs.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a76dd).
