x_comment(x_isAContraryFactorFor,"(#$isAContraryFactorFor FACTOR AGENT ACT_TYPE) means that in the\ngiven circumstances FACTOR would cause AGENT's likelihood of success in\ndoing actions that are tokens of ACT_TYPE to be lower, i.e., the\nconditional probability of AGENT's succeeding at ACT_TYPE given FACTOR is\nless than it would be if FACTOR did not obtain. In other words, FACTOR\nbrings it about that the #$derivedProbability of the proposition expressed\nby 'A would be successful at ACT_TYPE_TOKEN if she tried' is\ndecreased. Note that 'being a contrary factor' in this sense is relative to\nthe given circumstances: in the present, ordinary circumstances not having\ncoffee readily available might be a contrary factor for Julia to make a\nsuccessful presentation, but things might well be different in a state\nof affairs where Julia has slept for 3 straight days and is fully\nrested.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7710).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7710,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
