x_comment(x_accessibleFrom,"This predicate relates pairs of nearby regions or\nobjects that are so situated that an unaided human could \nmove directly to the second from the first.  \n(#$accessibleFrom HERE THERE) means that HERE and THERE \nare places -- i.e. either regions or objects (like rooms\nand rooftops) that are capable of containing or supporting\na human -- such that the average human could, more or less \ndirectly, get from being in/on HERE to being in/on THERE\nwithout excessive difficulty or risk, and without the use \nof special equipment.  For example, one room is accessible \nfrom another if the door between them is unlocked, but not if\nthe door is locked.  This predicate is not symmetric as, for \nexample, it might be possible to jump from one rooftop to a \nlower rooftop yet not possible to climb back.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7751).
