x_comment('x_connectedTo-Directly',"(#$connectedTo-Directly OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are directly attached in a way that allows at most only certain types of relative motion between them.  Adjacent links in a bicycle chain, for example, can only undergo limited rotational motion in relation to each other.  OBJ1 and OBJ2 must both be #$SolidTangibleThings, must be directly touching  each other, and their mutual connectedness must _not_ obtain merely in virtue of some third object's serving as a connector between them.  For a generalization of this \n\nthat does not imply a _direct_ connection between objects, see #$connectedTo\n\n(which is in effect the transitive closure of #$connectedTo-Directly).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a77b3).
