x_comment(x_supplyFromCapacityDuring,"(#$supplyFromCapacityDuring PT1 COL PT2 THING AMOUNT) means that that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the greatest possible amount of instances of the #$Collection COL with which the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 could be supplied from the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$supplyFromCapacityDuring is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and likewise for PT2.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates what would be the average rate of supply of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE to PT1 from PT2 during the temporal extent of THING if PT1 were supplied with PRODUCT-TYPE from PT2 at the limit of its capacity.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7817).
