x_comment(x_versionOfJobPosition,"(#$versionOfJobPosition JOB RELATION) means that the version of #$JobPosition JOB is the #$HasPositionRelationship RELATION. An instance of #$JobPosition can have more than one version because the same #$JobPosition can be filled successively by more than one person. A different #$HasPositionRelationship is created each time a different person fills the same #$JobPosition JOB. Each of these #$HasPositionRelationships bear the relation #$versionOfJobPosition to the same #$JobPosition, although these relations hold at different time intervals. Two different people cannot bear the #$versionOfJobPosition relation to the same #$JobPosition during the same time interval. For example, suppose #$Cycorp has a #$JobPosition, OntologicalEngineer01. At t1, the position is open (see #$JobOpen). At t2, David Smith is hired to fill this position (see #$JobFilled) . At t2, a #$HasPositionRelationship, OntologicalEngineer01DS begins, the relation between David Smith and #$Cycorp. At t2, it's true that (#$versionOfJobPosition OntologicalEngineer01 OntologicalEngineer01DS). At t3, David Smith resigns. At t4, Kevin Jones is hired to fill the #$JobPosition OntologicalEngineer01, and a new #$HasPositionRelationship, OntologicalEngineer01KJ is created. At t4, it's true that (#$versionOfJobPosition OntologicalEngineer01 OntologicalEngineer01KJ). On the other hand, if David Smith and Kevin Jones were each hired by #$Cycorp at the same time as ontological engineers, there would be two #$JobPositions at #$Cycorp, and each person would bear a #$versionOfJobPosition to different instances of #$JobPosition.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a78f9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a78f9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a78f9,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526a78f9,6531).
