x_comment('x_MachineGun-M242',"The 25mm M242 Bushmaster cannon used on the Bradley Fighting  Vehicle and a variety of land and sea vehicles.  The Marine Corps carries  this weapon on the Light Armored Vehicle (LAV) while the Navy carries it on  many of its ocean-going vessels to deal with small attack craft. The M242  25mm Bushmaster Chain Gun, manufactured by McDonnell Douglas, has a single  barrel with an integrated dual-feed mechanism and remote ammunition selection. Either armor piercing (AP) or high explosive (HE) ammunition may be selected  with the flick of a switch. The Gunner may select from single or multiple  shot modes. The standard rate of fire is 200 rounds per minute, and has a range of 2,000 meters (depending on the ammunition used). A wide range of  ammunition has been developed for this weapon, making it capable of defeating  the majority of armored vehicles it is likely to encounter, up to and  including some main battle tanks.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a790e).
