x_comment(x_listwiseArg2Type,"(#$listwiseArg2Type LIST SLOTLIST) is true when for every N, 0 < N\n\n<= (#$LengthOfListFn LIST), if SLOTn is the N-th element of SLOTLIST and\n\n(#$arg2Isa SLOTn COLL), then the N-th element of LIST is an instance of\n\nCOLL. In other words, for every N the N-th element of LIST satisfies the\n\narg2 constraint for the N-th element of SLOTLIST. Example: the pair\n\n(#$TheList #$performedBy) and (#$TheList #$Lehmann) is an element of this\n\nrelation. Note that (#$listwiseArg2Type LIST1 LIST2) presupposes that LIST1\n\nand LIST2 are of the same length.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a791e).
