x_comment(x_AttendingFn,"#$AttendingFn is a collection denoting function which takes as its argument a type of event and returns a collection of events, which collection is itself a collection of subevents of the instances of the subcollection of #$Event entered in the Arg1 position. For example, (#$AttendingFn #$EntertainmentEvent) returns the collection of events which consist of attending some entertainment event or other. Moreover, attending an entertainment event is a subevent of the entertainment event in question, which is itself an instance of #$EntertainmentEvent, so (#$AttendingFn #$EntertainmentEvent) is a collection of subevents of instances of #$EntertainmentEvent.  Another more specific example would be (#$AttendingFn #$BalletDancePerformance), which would be the collection of all instances of attending an instance of ballet. Since attending a ballet is a subevent of an instance of ballet, (#$AttendingFn #$BalletDancePerformance) is a collection of subevents of instances of #$BalletDancePerformance. Yet a third example is as follows: (#$AttendingFn #$SocialGathering) returns the collection of events in which some agent attends some instance of #$SocialGathering. In each case, '#$AttendingFn' is meant to distinguish the spectators from the performers, or the guests from the hosts.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7921).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7921,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
