x_comment(x_visibleParts,"The #$visibleParts of this tangible object.  Since #$colorOfObject, #$textureOfObject transfersThro visiblePartOf it is important to understand the following. Implicit in what is a visible part is a point of view.  This point of view is probably context dependent.  Thus for your average human activities the visible parts of an apple should be its stem and its skin. Or for a House the #$visibleParts would be Shutter, Roof, OutsideWalls.  Note that AppleFlesh, Seeds, and RoomInAHouse are internal parts.  Each of these parts has their own #$visibleParts.  However, internal parts are usually not #$visibleParts from the bigger object that they are part of.  Thus the color of RoomInAHouse's walls will not affect the color of the House.  This gets very complex for containers, or objects with portals in them.  Also transparent parts sometimes allow #$internalParts to be visible.  These two issues are hard and important and need to be dealt with.  For now, this ad hoc solution may deal with a large number of common sense cases.  So just annotate cases where this breaks down.  Sometimes a new microtheory may be necessary.  I.e. there may be some mT where we are constantly opening things up and taking them apart.  What is on #$visibleParts would be completely different then.  Thus for #$HumanActivitiesMt good slot values would be things that would be visible from a reasonable point of view.  We usually don't cut pencils open; it is usual to think of a house's color as being its colors visible from outside etc..") :- x_cid(a65b16526a795d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a795d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
