x_comment(x_CharacterStringMode,"A collection of collections.  A character-string mode is\n\n  a collection of concrete character-string tokens that all represent\n\n  the same abstract character-string in the same way, e.g. by being \n\n  handwritten rather than printed or spoken.  That is, each instance\n\n  MODE-INST of #$CharacterStringMode is a specialization of an \n\n  instance TYPE-INST of #$CharacterStringType that includes all \n\n  elements of TYPE-INST that are realized in a particular way (such \n\n  as by being inscribed, or by being sounded).  For example, if \n\n  TYPE-INST is the collection of all tokens of the string 'cat', \n\n  MODE-INST might be the collection of all _spoken_ tokens of 'cat'.  \n\n  For other examples, see the specializations \n\n  #$CharacterStringMode-Inscribed, \n\n  #$CharacterStringMode-Sounded, and \n\n  #$CharacterStringMode-ElectroMagnetic.  See also #$modeOfStringType for\n\nthe relation between a given string type and each of the various string modes\n\nit subsumes.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7987).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7987,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
