x_comment(x_StreetCornerFn,"(#$StreetCornerFn XING DIRECTION) is the\nlot of land (if any) that lies adjacent to, and generally to \nthe DIRECTION of, XING.  A given intersection will normally \nhave four street corners associated with it, corresponding \nto four directions that are approximately 90 degrees apart \nfrom each other.  For example, if the two streets that \nintersect at XING run north-south and east-west, respectively, \nthen there will be street corners to the #$Northeast-Generally, \n#$Northwest-Generally, #$Southeast-Generally, and \n#$Southwest-Generally of XING.  See also #$streetCornerOf,\n#$atStreetIntersection, and #$directionsOfPath.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a799f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a799f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
