x_comment('x_positiveInterest-Prop',"(#$positiveInterest-Prop AGT PROP) means that AGT has a pro-attitude towards PROP -- i.e., AGT has a positive interest in PROP being or becoming true.  #$positiveInterest-Prop is a generalization of more specific pro-attitude predicates such as #$desires, #$intends, and #$goals.  In contrast with #$desires and #$goals, #$positiveInterest-Prop is not strictly future-directed.  An agent may have a positive interest in a proposition which already holds.  Also, (#$positiveInterest-Prop AGT PROP) does not \n\nentail that AGT intrinsically values PROP.  AGT may only prefer PROP to the available alternatives.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a79b3).
