x_comment(x_kePlausibleConsideration,"(#$kePlausibleConsideration TERM FORMULA) means that FORMULA expresses information that could be useful to the KB if asserted about TERM.  Such judgements are based on generalizations about things of the same type. Note that if FORMULA is salient to term, it may be strongly or weakly suggested that FORMULA be known to be true in the system, see #$keWeakSuggestion, #$keStrongSuggestion.  As an example of how this differs from strong or weak suggestions consider a partition of a collection, call it CollectionA.   It is probably useful to consider whether new specializations of CollectionA should also be made specializations of one of the partition cells.  However, we wouldn't strongly or weakly suggest that it be made such a specialization until after we've considered whether it fits into one of the cells.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a79bc).
