x_comment(x_PresuppositionPredicate,"The collection of predicates  that   enable a basic CycL representation of commonsense knowledge  that \"pack in\" or \"gloss over\" assumptions that, for Cyc to do  interesting reasoning over,  would generally need to be made explicit.  By  definition, instances of  #$PresuppositionPredicate are axiomatically   related to other predicates that make all or most of  the assumptions in such natural language expressions  explicit.  Consider, for example, the Cyc treatment  of statements about evidence, which (appropriately)  involves ascribing an amount of evidence that an   #$IntelligentAgent has in support of some belief (see  #$evidentialSupportForBelief).  However, in ordinary  English, people who make statements about evidence  generally do not make them in terms of agents or beliefs.  Often, they make them in terms of an amount of evidence  and some #$Individual or #$Collection (e.g., \"there  is plenty of evidence for Nessie,\" \"there is no  evidence of UFOs\").  Obviously, parsing such syntactically  and semantically different expressions using  #$evidentialSupportForBelief is problematic.  Thus we  need #$evidentialSupportForPhenomena-AgentUnspecified,  which takes an amount and a collection -- and so   allows for easy parsing of such common English   expressions -- and is understood by Cyc via axioms  to the explicit, or 'longhand' CycL involving  #$evidentialSupportForBelief.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a79c9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a79c9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a79c9,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
