x_comment(x_vulnerableInType,"(#$vulnerableInType SITUATION-TYPE OBJECT RESULT-TYPE) means that when in situations of type SITUATION-TYPE, existing object OBJECT is vulnerable to hardships of type RESULT-TYPE.  The purpose of #$vulnerableInType is to represent knowledge that an object is vulnerable in an entire class of situations.  For restrictions on RESULT-TYPE please see the comment on #$vulnerableIn.  Note that this is a type-level predicate in the first argument place and that care needs to be taken in developing rules that draw #$vulnerableIn conclusions from #$vulnerableInType GAFs so that we do not overpopulate the KB with potentially questionable #$vulnerableIn judgments.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a79cb).
