x_comment(x_AxisConstrainedRotation,"#$Movement-Rotation physically constrained at the axis of rotation.  The object may rotate about an #$Axle, may be attached to a rotating #$Axle which is constrained it its position, or may be rotated by a spinning device which is attached to it along the #$axisOfRotation.  The axis may be through the center of gravity (e.g. #$DrillBit, #$Propeller, #$Wheel, ...) or not (clock hand, pendulum, ...).  A #$Wheel which falls off a car and rolls down the street is NOT axis constrained, and one of two wheels connected by a fixed #$Axle rolling as a unit is a borderline negative example.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a79d7).
