x_comment(x_AsymmetricDigitalSubscriberLine,"A variation of 'Digital Subscriber Line' designed for an upstream data flow (client-to-server) which is a fraction of the downstream data flow (server-to-client).  Typically the upstream data flow is measured in kilobits per second while the downstream data flow is measured in megabits per second (e.g. 6 megabits per second over standard phone lines). ADSL is appropriate for applications such as Video on Demand or World-Wide Web where a request from the user is far less data than the response.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7a48).
