x_comment(x_availableToAgentTypeForEventType,"(#$availableToAgentTypeForEventType AGENT-TYPE OBJECT EVENT-TYPE) means that OBJECT is typically available for agents of type AGENT-TYPE to use in events of type EVENT-TYPE.  If an instance of AGENT-TYPE is capable of using OBJECT in an instance of EVENT-TYPE, nothing prevents that agent from choosing to use OBJECT in that event. Note that if OBJECT is available to an instance of AGENT-TYPE in an instance of EVENT-TYPE, that instance of AGENT-TYPE may still, for other reasons, be incapable of using OBJECT in that instance of EVENT-TYPE. Compare this predicate to #$availableForEvent and #$availableToAgentTypeForEvent.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7a4d).
