x_comment('x_interArgFormat3-3',"An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).\n(#$interArgFormat3-3 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)\nrequirement for the third argument-place of PRED when PRED's third argument\nis an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form \n(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ... ARGN) in which ARG3 is an instance of COL, PRED's arg3\nposition (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG3' in the preceding\nsentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances for\nfurther explanation.  Note that #$interArgFormat3-3 is one of several \n\"degenerate-case\" inter-argument format predicates, in which the \nspecified condition and the corresponding format constraint both have to do \nwith the _same_ argument-place of a given predicate.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7aaa).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7aaa,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
