x_comment(x_negativelyCorrelatedWith,"(#$negativelyCorrelatedWith ?SET ?SLOT1 ?SLOT2) means that the values for ?SLOT1 and the values for ?SLOT2 are negatively correlated, when they are applied to elements of ?SET.  In other words, ?SLOT1 is low when ?SLOT2 is high (and vice versa: high when low) for an arbitrary element of ?SET. High and low are with respect to the range of all values of ?SLOT1 respectively ?SLOT2 for elements of ?SET. \n\nNote that #$negativelyCorrelatedWith and #$positivelyCorrelatedWith don't entail a particular directionality of the causal relationship between ?SLOT1 and ?SLOT2.  It might go either direction, or there may be no direct causal link, with instead values of ?SLOT1 and ?SLOT2 actually being independent but subject to some common causal mechanism.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7adc).
