x_comment(x_orderingRelation,"(#$orderingRelations ORDER PRED) means that, in a #$MathematicalOrdering ORDER, there is an order-predicate PRED that forms an ordering relation on the #$baseSet of ORDER.  The predicate PRED, when restricted to the #$baseSet of the #$MathematicalOrdering ORDER, is transitive on the #$baseSet of ORDER.  Note that the predicate #$orderingRelations is not a functional predicate because we may have both (#$orderingRelations ORDER PRED1) and (#$orderingRelations ORDER PRED2).  (This is true even if, extensionally, the two predicates PRED1 and PRED2 denote only one set-theoretic binary relation associated with ORDER.)  Such an ordering relation is not necessarily a full order or even a partial order; it depends on the kind of #$MathematicalOrdering.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7ae6).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7ae6,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
