x_comment(x_positivelyCorrelatedWith,"(#$positivelyCorrelatedWith ?SET ?DEP-PRED ?INDEP-PRED) means that the second arguments to ?DEP-PRED are positively correlated with those for ?INDEP-PRED, when elements of ?SET appear in the first argument position.  In other words, given the range of bindings for DEP-VAL and INDEP-VAL in (#$and (#$elementOf X ?SET)(?DEP-PRED X DEP-VAL) (?INDEP-PRED X INDEP-VAL)), whenever INDEP-VAL is high for a particular X, DEP-VAL will also be high and whenever INDEP-VAL is low, DEP-VAL will be low.  Note that #$negativelyCorrelatedWith and #$positivelyCorrelatedWith don't entail a particular directionality of the causal relationship between arg2 values for ?DEP-PRED and ?INDEP-PRED.  It might go either direction, or there may be no direct causal link, with instead arg2 values for ?DEP-PRED and ?INDEP-PRED actually being independent but subject to some common causal mechanism. ") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7b8d).
