x_comment(x_RoundClosestFn,"(#$RoundClosestFn QUANTITY) converts QUANTITY into one where the maximum and minimum ranges have been rounded to the closest integer values.  For example,  (#$RoundClosestFn (#$Meter 2.41)) denotes (#$Meter 2),  (#$RoundClosestFn (#$Meter 2.7)) denotes (#$Meter 3), and (#$RoundClosestFn (#$Meter 1.6 4.2)) denotes  (#$Meter 2 4). If QUANTITY is exactly between two integers (that is, in the form integer+0.5), then it is rounded to the one that is even. So, (#$RoundClosestFn (#$Meter 2.5)) denotes (#$Meter 2), and (#$RoundClosestFn (#$Meter 7.5)) denotes (#$Meter 8). See also #$RoundUpFn, #$RoundDownFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7b9b).
