x_comment(x_defaultSuitableProduct,"(#$defaultSuitableProduct PRSN PROD-TYPE) means that any instance of the instance of #$ProductType, PROD-TYPE, is a suitable #$Product to be purchased for the #$Person PRSN, unless PROD-TYPE is known to be not suitable (see #$contraindicatedProduct). For example,(#$defaultSuitableProduct #$TheRecipient #$PersonalDigitalAssistant) means that any instance of #$PersonalDigitalAssistant is a suitable #$Product to be purchased for #$TheRecipient. Assertions using this predicate are the weakest assertions that can be made about the suitability of a #$Product for a recipient. There need be no positive evidence in favor of PROD-TYPE being suitable for a recipient for it to be default suitable. The motivation for creating this predicate is to enable asks of the form (#$defaultSuitableProduct ?PRSN ?PROD-TYPE) to return bindings right at the beginning of a session in which a customer uses the Cyc Product Advisor interface. In the beginning of a session we have no information about the customer, so we can't do any inferencing about which #$Products are indicated.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7ba9).
