x_comment('x_decreases-Generic',"(#$decreases-Generic TEMP-THING THING SLOT)            means the value of the            predicate SLOT applied to THING (in the first argument            position) will decrease over some time period after the start of            TEMP-THING. Compared with            its value immediately before TEMP-THING, the value of            SLOT applied to THING will be lower            immediately following or some time after the start of TEMP-THING.             This is the most generic of the #$SlotTrendPredicates relating to decreasing of a given #$QuantitySlot: the decrease may be causal, or may not be, and may occur immediately, or over a period of time following TEMP-THING. For GAFs, or in the consequents of rules dealing with decreased quantities, use the more specific predicates if possible. See            #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of related            predicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7bac).
