x_comment(x_FunctionValueFn,"(#$FunctionValueFn FUNCTION ARG) is a term \n\ndenoting the resulting value of applying a unary FUNCTION to ARG, whatever \n\nthat value may be. Since #$FunctionValueFn is a #$ReifiableFunction, one can\n\nuse this to refer to and talk about the result of applying a function to \n\nan argument even if the actual resulting value is not known.  For example,\n\n'the diameter of Mars is smaller than the diameter of Earth' can be expressed\n\nas :\n\n(#$followingValue\n\n  (#$FunctionValueFn\n\n     (#$FunctionToArg 2 #$diameterOfObject)\n\n     #$PlanetMars)  \n\n  (#$FunctionValueFn\n\n     (#$FunctionToArg 2 #$diameterOfObject)\n\n     #$PlanetEarth)") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7bb6).
