x_comment('x_typeMakesMoreVulnerableThan-Situation',"(#$typeMakesMoreVulnerableThan-Situation SIT-TYPE1 SIT-TYPE2 ?OBJECT-TYPE ?RESULT-TYPE) means that when existing things of type ?OBJECT-TYPE are involved in situations of type ?SIT-TYPE1 they are more vulnerable to results of type ?RESULT-TYPE than when they are involved in situations of type ?SIT-TYPE2.  The purpose of this predicate is to enable broad, comparative knowledge representations of vulnerabilities.  For a similar, instance level predicate see #$makesMoreVulnerableThan-Situation.  Note that this is predicate is type-level across the board; it is meant to capture very broad generalizations.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7be5).
