x_comment(x_Swinging,"The process of repetitive swinging with either a rigid (e.g. pendulum or metronome) or flexible (e.g. child's swing) connection to an axis not at the center of gravity.  The axis does not have to be horizontal; thus a gate can swing back and forth.  The motion, for a horizontal axis, may be above the axis as well as below.  Both the object attached to the pivot and any object 'riding' on that object are said to swing.  This does not include swinging an axe or a bat as a single swing is not periodic, and the return to the start of the swing for repeated swings is not a temporal reflection of the forward swing.   Swinging a pail around the head while it is attached to a rope is not this kind of #$Swinging since it is not a repetative reversing motion.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7c16).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7c16,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
