x_comment('x_enables-StaticConduciveFactor',"This predicate represents the idea that an agent may be enabled\nto do something not by the occurrence of an event, but simply by finding\nherself, more or less statically, in a certain situation. Example: having\nresidence in midtown Manhattan enables one to attend performances of the\nMetropolitan Opera, in the sense of making it more likely that one would be\ncapable of attending such a performance than if one would be if she were,\nsay, in Austin. Therefore, (#$enables-StaticConduciveFactor SIT AGENT\nACT_TYPE) means that SIT makes it more likely that AGENT would succeed at\nan instance of ACT_TYPE were she to attempt than it would be otherwise --\ni.e., if SIT did not obtain.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a7c7e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a7c7e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
