x_comment(x_AnimalMigration,"The collection of regular, species-linked movements of an animal or group of animals from one place to another, usually with a return to the starting point after a certain period of time.  In some species, the migration cycle occurs once in a lifetime, while others migrate annually on a seasonal basis.   Migration is typically linked with an animal's reproductive cycle (as in salmon), but may also involve seasonal relocation to a more hospitable climate and/or more plentiful food supply. For example, many birds exhibit seasonal migration; e.g., native Northeastern U.S. birds that spend their winters in the Southern U.S.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8033).
