x_comment('x_Horse-WarmBlood',"Members of horse breeds represented by specializations of the collection #$Horse-WarmBlood tend to be more slender than those that are members of breeds represented by specializations of #$Horse-ColdBlood.  In temperament, warm-blood horses are usually more high-strung than cold-blood horses.  They are generally used for sports such as racing, jumping, and dressage.  While the collections #$ThoroughbredHorse and #$ArabianHorse represent 'light breeds,' and have instances sharing many charactersitics with instances of #$Horse-WarmBlood, they are not specializations of #$Horse-WarmBlood because instances are considered pure-bred while warm-blood breeds are of mixed heritage.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8142).
