x_comment(x_HepaticCapillary,"The collection of all hepatic capillaries (or 'sinusoids').  A #$HepaticCapillary releases nutrients and waste products into the #$Liver; it does not supply #$Oxygen.  That function is provided by systemic capillaries which are also in the #$Liver.  Kupffer #$Cells in hepatic capillaries destroy bacteria [see #$Bacterium] in the #$Blood, an important task since bacterial cells may have entered the bloodstream in the #$SmallIntestine.  A #$HepaticCapillary is a filtering pathway for #$Blood which has entered the #$Liver via the #$HepaticPortalVein.  Arterioles from the #$HepaticArtery provide #$OxygenatedBlood to the hepatic capillaries.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8147).
