x_comment(x_learnedCapableOf,"This generalization of #$skillCapableOf can be used to assert that a given individual agent has the ability to play a certain role in a certain type of #$LearnedActivity (q.v.).  (#$learnedCapableOf AGENT ACTTYPE ROLE) means that AGENT has acquired the necessary abilities to act in ROLE in normal instances of ACTTYPE.  For example, that #$Gumby has learned to walk is expressed by (#$learnedCapableOf #$Gumby #$WalkingOnTwoLegs #$performedBy).  #$learnedCapableOf entails that AGENT satisfies any physical or intellectual prerequisites for acquiring, possessing, and exercising the ability; but it is neutral as to whether AGENT has the necessary resources of time, money, opportunity, etc., to exercise the ability in any particular instance of ACTTYPE.  Note that ROLE should normally be a fairly \"central\" one to ACTTYPEs, i.e. a specialization of #$doneBy or #$deliberateActors.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a827c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a827c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
