x_comment(x_differsOnlyInArg,"A ternary predicate that relates an instance of non-negative integer (representing an argument position) to two instances of CycL formula.  (#$differsOnlyInArg FORMULA-1 FORMULA-2 N) means that FORMULA-1 and  FORMULA-2 are the same length, that the arguments in every argument position (including 0, when N is not equal to 0) other than the Nth are the same in the two formulas, and that the two formulas differ in the Nth argument position. For example, the sentence `(#$differsOnlyInArg (#$genls #$Dog #$Mammal) (#$genls #$Cat #$Mammal) 1)' holds. Note that #$differsOnlyInArg's first and second argument-places are both \"quoted\" (see #$quotedArgument); thus in the context of the above #$differsOnlyInArg sentence the constituent sentence `(#$genls #$Dog #$Mammal)' denotes _itself_ and similarly for the constituent sentence `(#$genls #$Cat #$Mammal)'.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8356).
