x_comment(x_directlyServesBodyParts,"(#$directlyServesBodyParts PARTA PARTB) means that the #$Organ, system segment, or part PARTA directly provides a  biologically useful or necessary service to organ, system segment, or  part PARTB (both being #$anatomicalParts of the same #$Organism-Whole).  Examples: the  #$SplenicArtery serves the #$Spleen (as blood supply), the JugularVeins drain the #$Head-Vertebrate, the left  #$SuperiorLobarBronchus supplies air to the left #$SuperiorLobeOfLung,  the #$SciaticNerve innervates the leg, etc.  Part of PARTA joins and  is #$connectedTo part of PARTB.  This does not refer to general or  indirect serving: not, for example, the case of the #$Liver being  needed for all body parts, etc., nor the case that the #$SpinalCord  serves the left little toe, etc.  This predicate applies only to the final part of the supply system supplying just the target PARTB and no other target parts; it does not apply to all of the 'upstream' links of a supply system.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a836c).
