x_comment(x_distalTo,"(#$distalTo OBJ-1 OBJ-2) means that OBJ-1 lies in the #$DistalDirection of OBJ-2, with respect to a reference point (see #$centralReferencePoint) within an object having an #$AnimalBodyShapeType (often, a #$Person) that they are located in.  This reference point is determined by the location of OBJ-1 and OBJ-2.  For example, if OBJ-1 and OBJ-2 are in the #$CirculatorySystem, the #$Heart is the point of reference, so (#$distalTo FredsFemoralArtery FredsAorta) means that Fred's aorta lies between Fred's femoral artery and his heart (see #$betweenOnPath for the relevant sense of between).  Note that (#$distalTo OBJ-1 OBJ-2) implies that OBJ-2 is proximal to OBJ-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent \"proximal to\".  OBJ-1 and OBJ-2 are often, but not always, #$AnimalBodyRegions.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8477).
