x_comment(x_relativesForUSTaxPurposes,"(#$relativesForUSTaxPurposes RELATIVE TAXPAYER) means that \nRELATIVE is related to TAXPAYER in such a way that RELATIVE is not requred \nto cohabitate with TAXPAYER in order to pass the household or residence \ncondition of the dependency test with respect to TAXPAYER.  \n#$relativesForUSTaxPurposes is a #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate, so that if \nRELATIVE satisifies the household or residence condition vis-a-vis TAXPAYER, \nthen TAXPAYER satisfies that condition vis-a-vis RELATIVE. As a general rule, \ntwo persons are related in the #$relativesForUSTaxPurposes relationship if \none is the ancestor (through biology or adoption), step-child, \nstep-parent, aunt, uncle, niece or nephew of the other, or if they are \nsiblings (including step-siblings) or in-laws.  A spouse does \nnot qualify as a #$relativesForUSTaxPurposes.  In some cases, the determination \nof whether an individual stands in the #$relativesForUSTaxPurposes to a \nmarried taxpayer depends on whether the taxpayer files a joint or a separate return.  \nFor example, the child of a sibling of the spouse of a married taxpayer who \nfiles a joint return satisifies the #$relativesForUSTaxPurposes condition.  \nConversely, if that taxpayer files a separate return, the  \n#$relativesForUSTaxPurposes condition is satisfied only vis-a-vis the \nspouse.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a84d0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a84d0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
