x_comment('x_Sac-Organic',"#$Sac-Organic is a specialization of #$OrganismPart  and #$Container.  Each instance of #$Sac-Organic is a plant or animal membranous sac or bladder, whether or not it is still part of a living #$Organism-Whole.  Instances of #$Sac-Organic have zero (some plant bladders), one (e.g. #$GallBladder), two (#$Stomach), or three  (#$Bladder-Urinary) tubes attached for the flow of material into or out of the bladder.  The bladder may used for storage of some material in the body, and possible processing thereof, or merely as a mechanism for separating structures (e.g. the #$Peritoneum).   Any tubes connected  to the bladder are of far smaller diameter than the bladder itself.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a858b).
