x_comment('x_SymlinkFault-Overwrite',"#$SymlinkFault-Overwrite is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has a #$SymlinkFault-Overwrite if when running it creates files with predictable filenames and world write permissions in the /tmp directory.  This fault allows a user to create a file in the /tmp directory with the same name and then symlink that file to a file to which the user does not have write permissions.  When the malicious user or another user executes the program, it follows the symlink and overwrites the protected file.  As with other faults, the severity of #$SymlinkFault-Overwrite depends on the privilege level under which the exploited program is running.  If the program runs at root, for instance, when creating the /tmp files, then the malicious user can overwrite any known file on the computer.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8593).
