x_comment(x_relationCategoryType,"This predicate relates instances of #$RelationshipType to instances of #$Collection that are required as #$argIsa constraints for predicates that are instances of the category. (#$relationCategoryType RELATION COLLECTION) means that any instance of RELATION must have at least one argument place such that the argIsa for that argument place is COLLECTION or one of its specs.  This is useful for defining relation types whose instances, by definition, must have some collection as one or more of its argument type restrictions, but where the definition of the predicate type places no restrictions on argument placement, i.e. is agnostic about N for (argIsa PRED N REQUIREDCOLLECTION).  For instance, (#$relationCategoryType #$MetaPredicate #$CycLExpression) means that for any instance of #$MetaPredicate, MPRED, (#$argIsa MPRED N CycLExpression) must be true for some positive integer although membership in the predicate category is not dependent on the value of N.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a85d8).
