x_comment(x_typeLevelCognates,"(#$typeLevelCognates PRED TYPEPRED) means that TYPEPRED is a type-level variant of PRED with respect to some argument place. Example: (#$typeLevelCognates #$behaviorCapable #$typeBehaviorCapable). This meta-property is used to effect type-shifting via #$reformulatorRules for quantifier processing. It has no purpose in ordinary KE. Note that #$InstantiationInstanceFn is a way to get type-level cognate predicates `on the fly', but #$typeLevelCognates is simpler to use in #$reformulationPrecondition because it doesn't depend on the creation of a predicate-denoting NAT.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8646).
