xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526a875a,[]).
x_comment(x_FormalProductType,"A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$FormalProductType is a collection of products (i.e. a subcollection of #$Product (q.v.)),  all of which conform to the same standardized product specification  (or \"form\").  In Western-style capitalistic markets, instances of  #$FormalProductType are often associated with a particular brand name  (and perhaps model), since competing providers of products design them  to be distinctive.  For example, the collection  #$InternalCombustionEngine is not an instance of #$FormalProductType,  but a specific collection of engines manufactured by (e.g.) Mazda might  be.  On the service side, the collection #$HairCuttingEvent is not a  formal product-type, but a subcollection of hair stylings for men (e.g.  at a particular salon) might be.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a875b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a875b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
