x_comment(x_QuasiGovernmentalOrganization,"The collection of all #$Organizations which are neither strictly governmental nor strictly private in nature and character.  For example, #$FederalHomeLoanMortgageCorporation is an instance of #$Organization that was created by a specific Congressional charter and, as such, is exempt from some governmental regulations that apply to private sector, publicly held companies (e.g., filings under the Securities and Exchange Act).  #$FederalHomeLoanMortgageCorporation is, however, subject to other regulations that do not apply to strictly private sector organizations (e.g., the Federal Housing Enterprises Financial Safety and Soundness Act of 1992).  #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganizations may or may not engage in profit-making activities.  Not all instances of #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitution are #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganization; in fact, most are not.  #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganizations, like #$FederalHomeLoanMortgageCorporation, were specifically contemplated by the chartering organization (in the case of #$FederalHomeLoanMortgageCorporation, the #$USCongress).  Many instances of #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitutions (e.g., instances of #$NationalBank) were not specifically contemplated by the chartering organization; rather, the generic idea of such institutions was contemplated and provided for by statute.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8764).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a8764,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a8764,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
