x_comment(x_Daggerboard,"A fin-like boat part which helps provide resistance to sideways motion.  When in use, the daggerboard is `sheathed'--i.e. inserted through a hole in the bottom of the boat so that it extends down into the water.  It should be `unsheathed' or raised in shallow water.  It is not necessary when sailing downwind, but it is necessary when sailing close-hauled or reaching (i.e. upwind or sideways to the wind).  The hole through which the daggerboard is sheathed is above the water-line, so that removing the daggerboard does not cause the boat to sink.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a87a8).
