x_comment(x_hasDepartments,"The predicate #$hasDepartments relates a particular organization to some particular department(s) within that organization.  (#$hasDepartments ORG DEPT) means that ORG, an instance of #$Organization, has DEPT among its #$Departments.  DEPT is a sub-organization of ORG that performs some of the activity of ORG.  In Cyc, the collection #$Department (q.v.) covers generically what may be called a division, department, office, bureau, ministry, etc., within an actual organization.  Commercial organizations, for example, commonly have instances of #$AccountingDepartment, #$HumanResourcesDepartment, and perhaps #$LegalDepartment, among others.  For example, (#$hasDepartmentTypes KMartStoreAtParmerLane #$CustomerServiceDepartment).  Government organizations have different specialized departments to carry out the functions of that government; e.g., (#$hasDepartments CityOfAustinTXCityGovernment AustinFireDepartment).  Cf. #$hasDepartmentTypes.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8956).
