x_comment(x_ScreenShotFn,"#$ScreenShotFn takes as an argument an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW and returns a collection of all 'stills,' or #$ScreenShots from that ComputerProgram.  For example, (#$ScreenShotFn #$Doom-TheGame) is the collection of all still, complete frames one would/could get on one's screen while running a copy of the Doom program.  The word 'complete' here is used to distinguish a screen shot from any sub-image in the screen shot.  So, for example, one pixel from a screen shot is not a screen shot.  An image of a person, considered by itself outside of the screen shot in which it appears, is not a screen shot.  For more info on this function, see the comment under its close relative, #$PicturesFromFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8a8d).
