x_comment(x_hasDepartmentTypes,"The predicate #$hasDepartmentTypes indicates what kinds of departments a particular organization has among its sub-organizations.  (#$hasDepartmentTypes ORG DEPTYP) means that a particular instance of #$Organization, ORG, has some #$Department(s) of the type DEPTYP among its sub-organizations.  Note that DEPTYP in (#$hasDepartmentTypes ORG DEPTYP) does not represent a particular #$Department within ORG, but instead refers to a type of #$Department that ORG has.  For example, universities have many #$AcademicDepartments, and (#$hasDepartmentTypes #$UniversityOfPittsburgh #$AcademicDepartment) is true.  So is the more specialized assertion (#$hasDepartmentTypes #$UniversityOfPittsburgh #$PhilosophyDepartment).  But neither assertion names a particular department.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8ad5).
