x_comment(x_Megaword,"A function and an instance of  #$UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity. It equals approximately four million (8-#$Bit) #$Bytes. Like all instances of #$UnitOfMeasure, its #$arity is variable between one and two, and its arguments must be instances of #$SubLRealNumber. If a single instance of #$SubLRealNumber is put in the argument position to this function, it returns a precise quantity of megabytes (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). If two #$SubLRealNumbers are put in the argument position, it returns an interval (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). Thus, the value of (#$Megaword 1) is one megaword. The value of (#$Megaword 1 2) is \"between one and two megawords. See also #$Word-UnitOfComputerMemory.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8c53).
