x_comment('x_interArgFormat2-2',"An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.). (#$interArgFormat2-2 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.) requirement for the second argument-place of PRED when PRED's second argument is restricted to being an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form  (PRED ARG1 ARG2 ... ARGN) in which ARG2 is an instance of COL, PRED's arg2 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG2' in the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances for further explanation.  Note that #$interArgFormat2-2 is one of several  \"degenerate-case\" inter-argument format predicates, in which the specified  condition and the corresponding format constraint both have to do with the  _same_ argument-place of a given predicate.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8ca9).
