x_comment(x_NLQuantFn,"(#$NLQuantFn TAG TERM) means that TERM appeared in a natural language utterance with the quantification denoted by TAG.  For example, (#$NLQuantFn #$Some-NLAttr #$Dog) would mean that some word meaning #$Dog occurred with the quantifier \"some\".  This function serves as a hint to the NL subsystems that this term was used with a particular feature, and is only intended to serve as a stand-in until the NL subsystems can determine the correct form of TERM to use in the semantic translation of the utterance.  Note that uses of this can (and frequently should) have as its arg2 another #$NLTagFn expression.  For instance, \"some cats\" would return from the parser as (#$NLQuantFn #$Some-NLAttr (#$NLNumberFn #$Plural-NLAttr #$Cat)).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8d2d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a8d2d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
