x_comment(x_ExperiencingPerception,"A collection of events that are related to perception.  We can think of instances of this collection as the mental component of perceptual events, (see #$Perceiving).  For instance, if one sees an apple, then there is a physical component to this event, i.e. the apple being in place, the light reflecting from it and into the eyes, etc.  However, the aspect of perceiving an apple that is an instance of #$ExperiencingPerception is the apple-like images that appear, so to speak, in one's mind as a result of the perception event.  We might note that while apples are necessary components in perceiving apples, they are not necessary components in having apple-like mental experiences.  This points out a possible gulf that is the source of much discussion in philosophy and cognitive science, i.e. the possible gulf between the real world and the world as it is experienced.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8dcd).
