x_comment('x_inferiorTo-Spatial',"(#$inferiorTo-Spatial OBJ-1 OBJ-2) means that OBJ-1 lies in the #$InferiorDirection of OBJ-2, when viewed in the frame of reference of the object with #$AnimalBodyShape (often, a #$Person) that they are located in.  In a #$Person, #$inferiorTo-Spatial almost always corresponds to #$caudalTo, but in a #$Dog or other four-legged animal, #$inferiorTo-Spatial usually corresponds to #$ventralTo.  Note that if OBJ-1 is #$inferiorTo-Spatial OBJ-2, OBJ-2 is superior to OBJ-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `superior to'.  OBJ-1 and OBJ-2 are often, but not always, #$AnimalBodyRegions.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8ef3).
