x_comment(x_WorldWideWebRobot,"#$WorldWideWebRobot is a collection of programs that automatically traverse the Web's hypertext structure by retrieving a document, and recursively retrieving all documents that are referenced. Note that \"recursive\" here doesn't limit the definition to any specific traversal algorithm -- if it applies some heuristic to the selection and order of documents to visit and spaces out requests over a long space of time, it is still a #$WorldWideWebRobot. Normal Web browsers are not #$WorldWideWebRobot, because they are operated by humans, and don't automatically retrieve referenced documents (other than inline images). Instances of #$WorldWideWebRobot are sometimes referred to as \"Web Crawlers\", \"Worms\", or \"Spiders\".") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8f1d).
