x_comment('x_RotaryDial-Telephone',"A collection of devices for inputing telephone numbers. Each instance of #$RotaryDial-Telephone consists of a disk with ten holes arranged around the periphery connected via a rotary shaft through its center to an instance of TelephoneBody. The ten holes correspond to the ten single-digits numerals 0-9, and the typical mode of operation is for the caller to insert a fingertip into a hole, rotate the dial clockwise until the fingertip hits a stop device attached to the telephone body, and then release the dial by removing the fingertip from the hole and let the dial return to its initial position. The dial generates clicks while rotating back to its initial position, and the clicks encode one digit of a telephone number.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8f82).
