x_comment(x_obligatedMeansOfLocomotion,"(#$obligatedMeansOfLocomotion AGENT MOVETYPE) means that MOVETYPE is a form of #$LocomotionProcess-Animal that the particular individual AGENT is physically obliged to use in the course of 'daily' existence.  A requirement is that the obligation be fairly persistent over some significant portion of obligated agent's #$Entity, or over the temporal extent of the context of the assertion. I.e., it cannot be something imposed for a short span of time by a comparatively fleeting circumstance.  I.e., someone who was forced to use a wheelchair to leave the hospital after an examination requiring a powerful local anaesthetic would not have #$Wheelchair-LocomotionEvent as an #$obligatedMeansOfLocomotion, unless this assertion were being made in a context whose temporal window was restricted to just that time span.  Note also that (#$obligatedMeansOfLocomotion AGENT MOVETYPE) does not mean that AGENT is incapable of being the #$performedBy of locomotion processes of types not known to be specializations of MOVETYPE: figuring out what an organism with a particular #$obligatedMeansOfLocomotion can and cannot do is a potentially complex story.  See #$restrictsAsObligatedMeansOfLocomotion") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8f9b).
