x_comment(x_RelationshipType,"A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$RelationshipType is a collection of #$Relations.  The relations in a given relationship-type represented in the Knowledge Base are typically those sharing some common feature(s) -- often having to do with what kinds of things the relations relate (see e.g. #$argIsa and #$argGenls) -- considered significant enough that the collection of all such relations is useful to reify.  Although what constitutes a \"significant common feature\" is difficult to specify precisely, there are many clear-cut cases.  Examples include #$UnaryFunction, #$LogicalConnective, #$IndividualDenotingFunction, #$GenericTimePredicate, and #$LanguageDescribingPredicate.  Two important specializations of #$RelationshipType are #$PredicateType and #$FunctionType.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a8fc7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a8fc7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
