x_comment(x_TelephoneKeypad,"A collection of devices for inputing telephone   numbers. Each instance of TelephoneKeypad contains at least 12   buttons, one for each digit 0-9, plus one marked * and one marked   #. Unlike the NumericKeypad used as a computer input device, a   TelephoneKeypad generally has the small numbers at the top. The   buttons are typically arranged in four rows of three buttons apiece,   from top to bottom as follows: 123 456 789 *0#. When one of these   buttons is pressed, the keypad generates a tone consisting of two   pitches sounding simultaneously. Each tone corresponds in the   Dual-Tone MultiFrequency (DTMF) standard to a digit 0-9, the symbol   * or #, or (on some keypads) a letter A-D.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9009).
