x_comment(x_BrachialPlexus,"The collection of all brachial nerve plexi located in #$Shoulders below/behind the #$Clavicle.  A #$BrachialPlexus is supplied by #$VentralRamusC5 - #$VentralRamusC8 and #$VentralRamusT1.  #$VentralRamusC4 and #$VentralRamusT2 are often included as suppliers to the #$BrachialPlexus but not always.  The ventral rami connect to create the #$SuperiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus, #$MiddleTrunk-BrachialPlexus, and #$InferiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus (also known as upper, middle, and lower branches).  Each of the 3 trunks then splits into anterior and posterior divisions.  The 6 trunk divisions then converge to form the #$PosteriorCord-BrachialPlexus, #$MedialCord-BrachialPlexus, and #$LateralCord-BrachialPlexus.  Most of the #$Nerves in the #$Arm are then formed from these cords.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9158).
