x_comment(x_VersusFn(x_ObjectType,x_StuffType),"Note that specializations of instances of #$ObjectType need not themselves be instances of #$ObjectType, and some specializations of instances of #$StuffType need not themselves be instances of #$StuffType. For example, #$Event is an instance of #$TemporalStuffType, but some specializations of #$Event, such as #$LunarRoundTrip, are instances of #$TemporalObjectType.  #$Events qua #$Events are temporally stuff-like, but #$Events qua $LunarRoundTrips are temporally object-like. To put it another way, if one cuts an #$Event in half into two time slices, one is left with two things which are themselves #$Events. On the other hand, if one cuts a #$LunarRoundTrip in half, one is left with two objects that are *not* #$LunarRoundTrips. Those two time slice objects are, however, #$Events.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9205).
