x_comment(x_fileAccessibleToComputer,"A #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$ComputerFile-Abstract to instances of #$ComputationalSystem.  A more specific predicate tha #$containsInformation and a more general predicate than #$fileFoundOnComputer, (#$fileAccessibleToComputer FILE COMP) means that although there may not be a copy (#$ComputerFileCopy) of FILE which is a part of COMP, there is a copy of FILE found on some machine to which COMP is appropriately linked.  If a file is accessible from COMP then, for all COMP cares, there is a copy of FILE on COMP.  That is, a user on COMP will not have to log in to a different machine (viz., the machine that FILE is found on) in order to read from, write to, or execute FILE.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9262).
