x_comment(x_Bit,"A function and an instance of #$UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity, generally used to denote the #$sizeOfObject for some sort of #$ComputerFileCopy or #$ElectroMagneticIBT.  Like all instances of #$UnitOfMeasure, its #$arity is variable between one and two, and its arguments must be instances of #$SubLRealNumber. If a single instance of #$SubLRealNumber is put in the argument position to this function, it returns a precise quantity of bits (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). If two #$SubLRealNumbers are put in the argument position, it returns an interval (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). Thus, (#$Bit NUM) denotes a\n\nparticular quantity of binary bits. (#$Bit NUM1 NUM2) returns a\n\nrange of binary bits. See also #$Byte, #$Megabyte.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a926a).
