x_comment(x_SpeciallyCharteredInstitution,"The collection of all instances of #$Organization organized in accordance with a particular jurisdiction's law governing the organization of institutions permitted to participate in particular activities or businesses.  For example, within the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, #$Organizations are allowed to participate in banking or savings or savings and loan activities only to the extent that they are chartered by specific state or federal laws.  Instances of #$LegalCorporation or #$Partnership are not permitted to engage in those types of activities.  The collection #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitution is disjoint with other instances of #$OrganizationByEntityType; those collections have instances of #$Organization that can ordinarily engage in a wide variety of activities and businesses.  By contrast, instances of #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitutions are created pursuant to specific statutory authority and can only engage in particular types of activities and businesses as authorized by that statute.  Within the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, some #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitutions are organized pursuant to federal law, while other instances are organized pursuant to state law.  Instances of #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitution are either #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganizations or #$PrivateSectorOrganizations; they are not #$GovernmentalOrganizations.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a944d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a944d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
