x_comment('x_Packet-SYN-Spoofed',"#$Packet-SYN-Spoofed is a #$Packet-Internet.  Under normal circumstances, following the #$InternetProtocol, a #$Packet-SYN is sent from a specific port on a computer to a specific port that is in a\n\"listen\" state on another computer.  The listening computer sends a\nSYN/ACK packet back to the first computer, which completes the\nhandshake by sending an Packet-ACK. When an\n#$AttackByComputerOperation-SYNFlooding is initiated, attackers\ninitiate this handshaking sequence with a #$Packet-SYN with a spoofed\nsource address, forcing the listening computer to send SYN/ACK\npackets and wait for #$Packet-ACKs that will never arrive.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9537).
