x_comment(x_Kaleidoscope,"Each #$Kaleidoscope is a toy which one looks into to see symmetrical patterns of moving colors.  Kaleidoscopes are generally cylindrical, with an eye-hole at one end, and with a compartment at the far end which contains colored objects that can move freely within the compartment.  The far end is either translucent or transparent, so that light can enter.  The inside walls of a kaleidoscope have mirrors, usually two set at an angle, so that when the compartmentalized objects move around, they appear to be multiplied N-fold (depending on the angle of the mirrors) and moving in symmetry with their reflections.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9600).
