x_comment(x_Kilobyte,"A function (an instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction and of #$UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity) used to represent a common unit of computer memory and disk capacity.  Like all instances of #$UnitOfMeasure, its #$arity is variable between one and two. Its arguments must be instances of #$SubLRealNumber. If a single instance of #$SubLRealNumber is put in the argument position to this function, it returns a precise quantity of megabytes (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). If two #$SubLRealNumbers are put in the argument position, it returns an interval (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). Thus, the value of (#$Kilobyte 1) is one kilobyte (approximately one thousand #$Bytes, each with a length of 8 #$Bits). The value of (#$Kilobyte 1 2) is \"between one and two kilobytes\". It is often referred to as \"K\". See also #$Megaword.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9648).
