x_comment('x_signifiesTo-Index',"This is a specialized representation (semiotic) predicate meaning representation due to causation, such as when a deer track 'represents' the deer to a tracker because the deer caused the deer track to be the way it is.  Similarly, a weathervane 'represents' the wind direction because of the way the wind direction has caused the vane to move. (#$signifiesTo-Index THING1 THING2 AGENT) means that, to AGENT, THING1 represents THING2 because AGENT regognizes that THING2 has caused  THING1 to be the way it is.  This is called 'indexical' representation. Compare this with the predicates #$signifiesTo-Icon and #$signifiesTo-Symbol.  It's possible for all three to apply to the same representation.  If the basis for the representation is unknown, use the more general predicate #$signifiesTo.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a978b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a978b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a978b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
