x_comment(x_dividedAmongGroup,"This predicate relates a group of intelligent agents to some thing that has been divided up among the group's members. (#$dividedAmongGroup THING GROUP) means THING has been divided or split into two or more shares, portions, or amounts among the group-members of GROUP.  The default assumption is that each portion is at least roughly equal to the others, and that each member of group gets a portion.  THING might be an individual physical object that has been cut or otherwise separated into physical portions (e.g. \"They split the last piece of cake.\"), a group of objects that has been distributed in (roughly) equal numbers among the group members, something of value that has been divided into shares of (roughly) equal value (e.g. \"The crooks divided up the spoils.\"), and so on.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a97db).
