x_comment(x_UniqueLinkIDFn,"The function #$UniqueLinkIDFn, when applied to a #$Path-Generic LINK and a #$PathSystem SYS in which LINK is a link, as in (#$UniqueLinkIDFn LINK SYS), results in the unique #$IDString by which that link is designated within the #$PathSystem SYS.  Example: if (#$UniqueLinkIDFn Link-9865656 CommNet) = 'Arc2', then this means that the link object Link-9865656 is labeled as 'Arc2' in the #$PathSystem CommNet.  It may often be the case that the internal machine name for the link is the same as that used in the #$PathSystem, but if they are not the same, this function allows reference to the name used in the #$PathSystem for that link.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a97e3).
