x_comment(x_Wheel,"The collection of all instances of the most general kind of wheel.  Each instance is a disk-shaped thing which can be rotated on an #$Axle which typically goes through the center of its circular cross-section. #$Wheels are found on #$LandTransportationDevices, serving the function of allowing #$RollingOnASurface for such  devices.  Wheels may take the form of #$Gears, parts of a #$Pulley, or may be present instead of ball bearings in places where a device needs to roll against a surface - like on the edges of some #$GarageDoors, which roll in a track when they are raised (#$LiftingAnObject).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a97f7).
