x_comment(x_doLocalBufferOverflowAttack,"(#$doLocalBufferOverflowAttack AGENT COMPUTER TARGET) means that AGENT performs a local buffer overflow attack on TARGET using COMPUTER.  It is \"local\" in the sense that it does not exploit a program listening on a port on TARGET, but the program exploited must be running on TARGET. Cf. #$doRemoteBufferOverflowAttack.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9803).
