x_comment(x_UniqueNodeIDFn,"The function #$UniqueNodeIDFn, when applied to a thing NODE and a #$PathSystem SYS in which NODE is a node, as in (#$UniqueNodeIDFn NODE SYS), results in the unique #$IDString by which that node is designated within SYS.  Example: if (#$UniqueNodeIDFn Point-454545 CommNet) = 'B2', then this means that the node object Point-454545 is labeled as 'B2' in the #$PathSystem CommNet.  It may often be the case that the internal machine name for the node is the same as that used in the #$PathSystem, but if they are not the same, this function allows reference to the name used in the #$PathSystem for that node.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a980c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a980c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
