x_comment(x_NetBIOSCachePoisoningFault,"Similar to a #$DNSCachePoisoningFault.  An #$OperatingSystem has this fault if it mishandles incoming datagrams in such a way that it is possible to plant false NetBIOS name/IP address information in the NetBIOS cache of the server TARGET_SERVER running the faulty program.  A malicious remote attacker who controlled an SMB/NetBIOS server MAL_SERVER with IP address XXXX could exploit the #$NetBIOSCachePoisoningFault of the OS on TARGET_SERVER by sending a specially-formed NetBIOS datagram to TARGET_SERVER.  The NetBIOS datagram header contains a  source and destination NetBIOS name, as well as a source IP  address, in addition to the IP headers.  Upon receiving a NetBIOS packet, an #$OperatingSystem with this fault will blindly (i.e., without verifying the authenticity of the source) extract the source NetBIOS name/IP address information from the packet and store it in the NetBIOS cache. If an attakcer could discover a NetBIOS name NAME used by some machine COMP on TARGET_SERVER's network, a remote attacker could redirect all NetBIOS datagrams intended for COMP to MAL_SERVER.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9883).
