x_comment(x_SetOfLinksAtNodeFn,"A function from path-systems and nodes in those path-systems to set-or-collections of links in those systems. (#$SetOfLinksAtNodeFn NODE SYS) is the #$SetOrCollection (q.v.) of all links in the #$PathSystem SYS that NODE is on, i.e., the set-or-collection of all links LINK in SYS such that (#$linkBetweenInSystem LINK NODE OTHER-NODE SYS) holds for some OTHER-NODE.  Note that if SYS is a #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem (q.v.) and NODE is a node in SYS, then (#$SetOfLinksAtNodeFn NODE SYS) equals the union of (#$InwardLinkSetFn NODE SYS) and (#$OutwardLinkSetFn NODE SYS) (these two set-or-collections will overlap if there are any 'bidirected' links at that node).  Note also that (#$SetOfLinksAtNodeFn NODE SYS) = #$TheEmptySet if there is no link in SYS that is between NODE and another node in SYS.  Loops, if any, are not included as links.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9898).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9898,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
