x_comment(x_FlowRateOnLinkFn,"The function #$FlowRateOnLinkFn applied to a thing and to the #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded of which it is a link, as in (#$FlowRateOnLinkFn LINK SYSTEM), denotes the actual flow rate occuring across that link (often varying with time), such as the actual vehicles-per-hour, gallons-per-minute, or any other flow or quantity that conforms to the rules for #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded.  This function results in the actual value of the flow along the link, not to the flow capacity of the link within the system nor to the flow capacity the link would have if isolated from the rest of the system -- for these see #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn and #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn, respectively.  The predicate #$flowTypeOfSystem is used find what kind of 'flow' is represented in a particular #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a98a0).
