x_comment(x_SituatedFlowCapacityInToNodeFn,"The function #$SituatedFlowCapacityInToNodeFn, applied to some thing and to a #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded in which it is a node, as in (#$SituatedFlowCapacityInToNodeFn NODE FLOWSYS), denotes the net maximum inward flow to NODE that can possibly flow into NODE, given the complete FLOWSYS in which every link has a value of #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn.  The result is the total of the #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn values on all the links going into that node from other nodes (it excludes all of the node's outward links). Note: The predicate #$flowTypeOfSystem is used to find what kind of 'flow' is represented in a particular #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded. See also #$SituatedFlowCapacityOutFromNodeFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a98cc).
