x_comment(x_infectionRoute,"(#$infectionRoute INFECTION-TYPE ORGANISM-TYPE PART-TYPE) means, colloquially, that organisms of type ORGANISM-TYPE are ordinarily vulnerable to infections of type INFECTION-TYPE through physical parts or features of type PART-TYPE, when some instance of an appropriate infection-causing pathogen penetrates the organism through such a part.  More formally, it means that  if an organism of the type ORGANISM-TYPE is penetrated by at least one instance of a pathogen such that this pathogen causes infections of type INFECTION-TYPE, and the penetration occurs through a physical part of the organism of type PART-TYPE, then the organism is #$vulnerableTo an infection of type INFECTION-TYPE caused by the pathogen, unless of course the organism is for some reason immune to infections of that kind.  It also entails that a pathogen of a type capable of causing infections of type INFECTION-TYPE is capable of entering an organism of type ORGANISM-TYPE through a physical part of type PART-TYPE.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a98d4).
