x_comment(x_SituatedFlowCapacityOutFromNodeFn,"The function #$SituatedFlowCapacityOutFromNodeFn, applied to some thing and to a #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded in which it is a node, as in (#$SituatedFlowCapacityOutFromNodeFn NODE FLOWSYS), denotes the net maximum outward flow from NODE that can possibly flow from NODE, given the complete FLOWSYS in which every link has a value of #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn.  The result is the total of the #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn values on all the links going out of that node into other nodes (it excludes all of the node's inward links). Note: The predicate #$flowTypeOfSystem is used to find what kind of 'flow' is represented in a particular #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded. See also #$SituatedFlowCapacityInToNodeFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a98fb).
