x_comment(x_relatedToVia,"(#$relatedToVia OBJ1 OBJ2 SET NUM) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are related via some sequence of NUM or fewer steps via the binary relations in the set SET.  More precisely, (#$relatedToVia OBJ1 OBJ2 SET NUM) means that there is a sequence of objects of the length equal to or less than NUM and such that OBJ1 is the first element of the sequence, OBJ2 is the last element of the sequence, and each element of the sequence is related to its successor (if any) by some predicate in SET, or by the inverse of some predicate in SET. For instance, if (#$likesAsFriend #$BillClinton #$TonyBlair) and (#$knows #$TonyBlair #$GeorgeWBush) are true, then (#$relatedToVia #$BillClinton #$GeorgeWBush (#$TheSet #$likesAsFriend #$acquaintedWith) 2) is true (given that (#$genlPreds #$knows #$acquaintedWith) is true). Note that a predicate in SET may be used to relate more than one pair: if (#$likesAsFriend #$BillClinton #$TonyBlair) and (#$likesAsFriend #$TonyBlair #$GeorgeWBush) are true, then (#$relatedToVia #$BillClinton #$GeorgeWBush (#$TheSet #$likesAsFriend #$acquaintedWith) 2) is true.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9921).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9921,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
