x_comment(x_needsFor,"This predicate relates an agent, a goal the agent has, and\n\nsomething the agent needs (in a very broad sense of `needs') in order\n\nto achieve or further that goal.  The goal is represented by a \n\nsentence (i.e. an #$ELSentence-Assertible; see #$goals).  The \n\n\"something\" needed might be either a thing the agent needs directly \n\n(such as a physical object or person) or a thing the agent has a need \n\nin (close) connection with (such as an object-type or a proposition); \n\nsee the specializations of #$needs-Generic for a fuller account.  \n\n(#$needsFor AGENT THING GOAL) means that AGENT needs THING (or has a \n\nneed in connection with THING that s/he must fulfill) in order to \n\nachieve her/his GOAL.  The sense of `need' relevant here ranges from \n\nmatters of practical convenience to matters of life and death; see the \n\ncomment on #$needs-Generic.  See also #$satisfiesNeed.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9940).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9940,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a9940,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526a9940,18204).
