xc_kb_names(a65b16526a994a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526a994a,[]).
x_comment(x_originallyFromRegion,"Where a tangible object has come from, where it was made.  A Russian automobile is #$originallyFromRegion #$Russia.  An African person is #$originallyFromRegion Africa.  Etc, etc. How do we axiomatize the sufficient conditions for this predicate?  This is not always clear.  Often, wherever an artifact has been fabricated is the value on #$originallyFromRegion.  (But there are some exceptions. E.g.  some Japanese Autos are fabricated in USA.)  Often, a person is #$originallyFromRegion where they were from.  (But I doubt a 25 year resident of the USA who was born 26 years ago to Anglo parents would be considered `African'.)") :- x_cid(a65b16526a994b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a994b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a994b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
