x_comment(x_SituatedLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn,"The function #$SituatedLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn, applied to a set of some things and to a #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded in which they are links forming a 'cutset', as in (#$SituatedLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn LINKCUTSET FLOWSYS), denotes the sum of all the #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn values of the links in LINKCUTSET, in FLOWSYS.  This is without regard to the links' connections to other links in FLOWSYS (for the version is limited by connections, see #$LocalLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn).  The result is the total of the #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn values on all the links going in or out of that node.  Note: The predicate #$flowTypeOfSystem is used to find what kind of 'flow' is represented in a particular #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded.  See also #$LocalLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9960).
