x_comment(x_EMailReplyCommandExecutionFault,"A program has this fault if an attacker can place a carefully-formed string containing shell meta-characters in the Reply-To: field of an email message.  If the attacker then sends the email to a victim/recipient, and the message elicits a response, the contents of the Reply-To: field will be interpreted as a reference to a pre-existing file in /tmp (or some other directory), placed earlier by the attacker, which can contain arbitrary commands. Of course, exploitation of this fault requires the attacker to be able to trick the user into replying to the message.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9977).
