x_comment('x_negativeInterest-Prop',"(negativeInterest-Prop AGT PROP) means that AGT has a con-attitude towards PROP -- i.e., AGT has a negative interest in PROP being or becoming true. #$negativeInterest-Prop is a generalization of more specific con-attitude predicates such as #$embarrassed, #$fears, #$regrets. In contrast with #$desires and #$goals, #$negativeInterest-Prop is not strictly future-directed. An agent may have a negative interest in a proposition which already holds. Indeed, this is always the case with such backward-looking emotional attitudes such as #$embarrassed and #$regrets. It captures the sense in which these emotions involve a wishing that something that is the case not be so.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a99bb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a99bb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
