x_comment('x_surrounds-2D',"This predicate describes situations in which one object surrounds\nanother in (at least) two dimensions.  More formally, if\n(#$surrounds-2D SURROUNDER SURROUNDED), then there is an abstract\nplane that cross-sections SURROUNDER and SURROUNDED.  In this plane,\nthe cross-section of SURROUNDER encircles the cross-section of\nSURROUNDED.  Thus, any ray drawn from SURROUNDED in that plane\n#$spatiallyIntersects SURROUNDER.  This is a generalization of\n#$surroundsHorizontally (q.v.), the special case in which the planar\ncross-section is defined by gravity.  Another specialization is\n#$surrounds-3D, where SURROUNDER 'covers' SURROUNDED as well (e.g. a\nbaseball cap on someone's head).  See also #$surroundsCompletely.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a99f6).
