x_comment('x_structureEncodesGenInfo-Exactly',"(#$structureEncodesGenInfo-Exactly GIS G-INFO) means that GIS\nis an abstract structure encoding exactly G-INFO. It may be the case that\nGIS encodes many pieces of genetic information; this predicate gives a\nmeasure of how optimal this encoding can be. For instance, any instance of\n#$Gene-GIS encodes exactly one instance of #$Gene-GenInfo. On the other\nhand, the same #$Gene-GIS is composed of a certain number of subsequences\nthat are instances of #$Codon-GIS, and thus it will encode all of the\ngenetic information encoded by these subsequences. An instance of\n#$Genome-GIS may contains sub-parts that encode a plurality of instances of\n#$Gene-GenInfo; however, there is a functional relation with the instance\nof #$Genome-GenInfo that contains all and only those abstract genes as\n#$subGeneticInformation.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9a43).
