x_comment(x_negationInverseWRTTypes,"(#$negationInverseWRTTypes BINPRED1 BINPRED2 COL1 COL2) means that if (BINPRED1 INS1 INS2) where INS1 is an instance of COL1 and INS2 is an instance of COL2, then (#$not (BINPRED2 INS2 INS1)).  This allows us to specify a pseudo-negationPreds relationship between two #$BinaryPredicates when their arguments are of the appropriate types.  At a more specific level, #$negationInverseWRTTypes can serve as a useful rule macro predicate.  See also #$genlPredsWRTTypes, #$genlInverseWRTTypes, and #$negationPredsWRTTypes.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9a48).
