x_comment(x_pathIntersectsRegion,"This predicate relates spatial paths to the spatial regions they intersect. (#$pathIntersectsRegion PATH REGION) means that some segment of PATH is in REGION.  More precisely, there is some #$subPaths SUBPATH of PATH such that SUBPATH is #$pathInsideRegion REGION.  PATH might be wholly contained in REGION or might continue beyond REGION in one or both directions.(Note that it is possible in principle for a path to #$spatiallyIntersects a region and yet not be related to it by #$pathIntersectsRegion, say if only part of the edge of the path overlaps the region.)  For more specific predicates, see #$pathIntoRegion, #$pathInsideRegion, #$pathThroughRegion, #$pathPassesThroughRegion, #$pathEndsInRegion, and #$pathDividesRegion.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9a59).
