x_comment(x_resultIsaArgIsaType,"(#$resultIsaArgIsaType FUNC N COL-TYPE) means that the NAT resulting from a use of FUNC is a member of the same collections that the term in arg N is a member of, where these collections are constrained to be members of the collection type COL-TYPE. For example: (#$resultIsaArgIsaType #$MotherFn 1 #$BiologicalTaxon) means that if CHILD is  an instances of TAXON which is an instance of #$BiologicalTaxon, then (#$MotherFn CHILD) is also an instance of TAXON.  But #$resultIsaArgIsa won't do because the mother won't be a member of *all* of the collections that her child will be a member of, e.g. #$MaleAnimal or #$Mule. In this case we need to make a #$resultIsaArgIsaType assertion to constrain the resulting NAT to be a member of a specific subset of the collections the child is a member of, in this case, those that are instances of #$BiologicalTaxon. Then, if (#$isa CHILD #$EquineAnimal), (#$isa (MotherFn CHILD) #$EquineAnimal) as well.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9a6d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9a6d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
