x_comment(x_vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString,"#$vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString is used to specify the general format of the URL string for reports of faults and vulnerabilities in on-line databases.  To generate an actual URL, it should be the case that all that need be added to the string are characters that map to the ID string for the fault or vulnerability.  For example, \"http://www.cert.org/advisories/~A.html \" is an appropriate #$vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString for #$CERTAdvisoryDatabase because, to generate the URL for a CERT entry, it is necessary only to substitute the ID of the fault (say, \"CA-2000-13\") for the occurrence of \"~A\" in the #$vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString to generate the appropriate URL (\"http://www.cert.org/advisories/CA-2000-13.html \").  Similarly, \"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/~A \" is an appropriate #$vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString for #$BugtraqFaultDatabase because it is necessary only to substitute the ID of the fault (say \"219\") for the occurrence of \"~A\" in the #$vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString to generate the appropriate URL (\"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/219 \").") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9a88).
