x_comment(x_touchesWith,"(#$touchesWith AGENT OBJECT2 OBJECT3) means that AGENT touches OBJECT2 with OBJECT3. This implies (#$touches AGENT OBJECT3) and (#$touches OBJECT2 OBJECT3), but not (#$touches AGENT OBJECT2): AGENT may or not be touching OBJECT2 in the sense of #$touches. For example, if #$Zaiss touches POSSUM45 with the end of long STICK87, opposite to the end he is holding, then although (#$touchesWith #$Zaiss POSSUM45 STICK87), it is not the case the (#$touches #$Zaiss POSSUM45). Whereas if #$Zaiss touches POSSUM45 with his hand, or with a gloved hand, then it is true that (#$touches #$Zaiss POSSUM45) (see the comment of #$touches).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9aa5).
