xc_kb_names(a65b16526a9abe,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526a9abe,[]).
x_comment(x_OfficialRecord,"A collection of #$InformationBearingObjects.  Each element of OfficialRecord is a record of some agent and exists for a particular purpose.  For example, #$PersonnelRecord may contain employee information and other facts that are pertinent to the functioning of a business.  #$OfficialRecords are typically issued and generated by institutions and they are held to a higher degree of veracity and authenticity than a mere collection of data.  For example, official financial records are 'official' enough to be used to file taxes, request a loan, or appear as evidence in a court of law.  There is an important distinction between #$OfficialDocument and #$OfficialRecord.  An #$OfficialRecord may record the the number of passports issued to whom and on which date, but the #$OfficialDocument is the passport itself.  In the same sense, a list of transactions for a business on a particular day is an #$OfficialRecord, the credit card receipts and tickets of sale are #$OfficialDocuments.  One should read the comment for #$OfficialReport as a third distinction.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9abf).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9abf,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
