x_comment(x_cultureOfMt,"(#$cultureOfMt MICROTHEORY CULTURE) defines the culture dimension of MICROTHEORY. It relates a #$Microtheory to the culture(s) it is relevant for or pertains to.  (#$mtOfCulture MICROTHEORY CULTURE) means that the assertions in MICROTHEORY are maden the context of CULTURE.  Beyond this, the precise type of relevance or pertinence will depend on other dimension attributes for MICROTHEORY, including modality.  See #$mtOfCulture for describing microtheories that are believed true in a given culture.  The predicate #$mtDefinesCulture relates a culture to the microtheory that precisely specifies its associated beliefs, practices, and artifacts.  See also #$mtCultureBeliefs.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9b14).
