x_comment(x_cutLinkInSystem,"(#$cutLinkInSystem LINK SYS) means that LINK is a single link in the #$ConnectedPathSystem SYS whose removal would cause the system to be disconnected.  Thus {LINK}, i.e., (#$TheSet LINK), is a link-cut-set in SYS.  That is to say, (#$cutLinkInSystem LINK SYS) holds if and only if (#$linkCutSetInSystem (#$TheSet LINK) SYS) holds. Note that since SYS is a #$ConnectedPathSystem whenever (#$cutLinkInSystem LINK SYS) holds, it is easy to see that (#$cutLinkInSystem LINK SYS) holds if and only if (#$linkCutMinimalSetInSystem (#$TheSet LINK) SYS) holds.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9b31).
