x_comment(x_IntentionalMentalState,"A collection of mental states whose instances are \n\ncharacterized by intentionality: they are \"of\" or \"about\" \n\nsome thing external to themselves.  Propositional attitudes \n\n(as held by particular agents) are a common type of intentional \n\nmental state.  Thus, believing that the Eiffel Tower is located\n\nin Paris is an intentional mental state that has the Eiffel Tower \n\nand the city of Paris (and arguably the located-in relation as \n\nwell) as its objects.  Any thing whatsoever can in principle\n\nbe the object of an intentional mental state: I can have a\n\nbelief (or doubt, wish, etc.) about a certain physical object, \n\nan event, a relation, an attribute, a proposition, a mental \n\nstate (my own or another's), a set, a collection, or anything \n\nelse.  (Note that the above mentioned belief about the Eiffel \n\nTower and Paris is arguably not itself about the _proposition_ \n\nthat the Eiffel Tower is in Paris.  But now note that my belief \n\nin the content of the sentence preceding this one clearly _is_, \n\nin part, about that proposition.)  Mental states that are _not_ \n\nintentional, and thus not in this collection, include moods,\n\nsuch as being in a general state of happiness or depression.  (These \n\nstates are to be distinguished from an experience of feeling \n\nhappy or depressed, which are mental _events_ rather than states.\n\nOne can be in an uninterrupted state of depression for weeks, \n\neven though one doesn't feel depressed continuously throughout \n\nthat time; e.g. one would not feel depressed while asleep.)\n\nNote that, although they are indirectly related, the sense of \n\n\"intentional\" described above is not to be confused with \n\nits other sense as an antonym of \"accidental\".  See also\n\n#$IntentionalMentalEvent and #$objectOfMentalSituation.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9b3f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9b3f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a9b3f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526a9b3f,18992).
