x_comment(x_sinkNodeInSystem,"(#$sinkNodeInSystem X SYS) means that X is a sink node in the #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS, i.e., a node to which all links attached to it come 'in', and from which no such links go 'out'.  A sink node X in SYS is a node in SYS such that X is on some links but no loops in SYS, and such that each link in SYS that X is on is a link directed to X from another node.  Another way to put this is that X is a node in SYS that is neither on any loop in SYS, nor an isolated node in SYS, nor a node from which a link in SYS is directed.  See #$loopInSystem, #$isolatedNodeInSystem and #$linkFromToInSystem.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9b41).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9b41,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a9b41,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
