x_comment('x_cultureArtifacts-Significant',"This predicate relates cultures \n\nto individual artifacts that are particularly significant to them.\n\n(#$cultureArtifacts-Significant CULTURE OBJECT) means that OBJECT was \n\nprobably produced within CULTURE, and is highly valued by and meaningful to \n\nthe participants of CULTURE.  Generally speaking, most of the artifacts\n\nassociated with a given culture (see #$cultureArtifacts) will not be \n\n#$cultureArtifacts-Significant.  For example, while the #$StatueOfLiberty \n\nis certainly one of #$UnitedStatesCulture's #$cultureArtifacts-Significant, \n\na souvenir reproduction of the statue is not.  Note that, unlike\n\n#$cultureArtifacts, which takes a _type_ of artifact as its second \n\nargument, this predicate takes an individual instance of #$Artifact-Generic\n\nin that argument position.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9b46).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9b46,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
