x_comment(x_TranscriptionEvent,"The collection of all acts of transcription.  If PERFORMER is the performer of a #$TranscriptionEvent, TRANSCRIBE, then PERFORMER brings it about that the information (to some degree of specificity) contained in the  #$informationOrigin, ORIGIN, of TRANSCRIBE comes to be contained in the #$informationDestination, DESTINATION, of TRANSCRIBE. ORIGIN and DESTINATION must both instantiate instances of #$AbstractInformationStructure (at times during TRANSCRIBE), and some of the #$AbstractInformationStructures instantiated by ORIGIN must come to be instantiated by DESTINATION, during TRANSCRIBE. #$TranscriptionEvents are distinguished from other sorts #$IBTGeneration-Replication (such as #$PhotocopyingADocument) in that, generally, the performer of a #$TranscriptionEvent is aware (sometime during that event) of the #$AbstractInformationStructures instantiated by ORIGIN, and is also aware (sometime during TRANSCRIBE) of the #$AbstractInformationStructures that come to be instantiated by DESTINATION. #$TranscriptionEvents are typically composed of many subevents that are also #$TranscriptionEvents. For example, if TRANSCRIBE is the transcription of an audio tape, ORIGIN, to the tablet DESTINATION, then TRANSCRIBE will typically be composed of other #$TranscriptionEvents in which small segments of the whole tape are #$informationOrigins in transcription events that have small portions of the tablet as #$informationDestinations.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9b4c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9b4c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a9b4c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
