x_comment('x_intends-SitType',"This predicate relates an agent to a kind of situation it intends, or has in mind as a purpose, to help bring about or maintain. (#$intends-SitType AGENT SITTYPE) means that AGENT intends either\n\nthat (i) a situation of type SITTYPE come about or (ii) some particular pre-existing situation of type SITTYPE continue.  This implies that AGENT believes it has at least some degree of influence or control over (i) or (ii) occurring.  Although clearly similar to a goal (see e.g. #$goalSitRole), AGENT's intending SITTYPE is likely to be more short-term (\"I did it because I intended that...\") and more mechanically satisfied (\"I intend that the lamp be turned off.\") than any of AGENT's goals.  You may intend that the lamp be turned off, but it would be odd to call that one of your goals.  We assume that if AGENT intends a particular kind of temporal situation, it intends any more general kind of temporal situation as well.  For a similar predicate that represents intending as a propositional attitude, see #$intends.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9b80).
