x_comment(x_Splitting,"A collection of separation events in which something splits apart, often at a seam (e.g. in an item of clothing), perforation, or grain-line (e.g. in a piece of wood).  That is, two areas of the thing are separated from one another (though perhaps not separated completely into discrete pieces or parts).  Usually, a splitting occurs along a single \"line\" or \"plane\" that runs parallel to, and for a significant distance relative to, the length of the thing split. In order to undergo a #$Splitting, the #$objectOfStateChange must be in a #$Solid-StateOfMatter.  See also #$Cracking.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9ba5).
