x_comment(x_hasAgents,"(#$hasAgents AGENT1 AGENT2) means that AGENT2 acts on behalf of AGENT1.  This does not mean that AGENT2's actions are entirely controlled by AGENT1, but that AGENT1's desires and goals can influence (prohibit, enable or constrain) the behavior of AGENT2 in some domain.  Examples include several kinds of situations: #$subOrganizations (the U.S. government has the U.S. Army as an agent), servants and slaves, and agents engaged for shorter periods of time or more restricted purposes, such as #$buyingAgents and #$sellingAgents.  In these latter cases, where control is not absolute, the predicate #$hasAgents applies only in a narrow context.  Often, but not always, AGENT1 and AGENT2 temporally intersect.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9bd9).
