x_comment(x_linkedViaAffiliation,"This predicate is a transitive form of the CycL relation #$affiliatedWith.  #$affiliatedWith is not itself transitive, for the good reason that the fact that, where AGENT1, AGENT2, and AGENT3 are all different, (#$affiliatedWith AGENT1 AGENT2) and (#$affiliatedWith AGENT2 AGENT3) cannot ordinarily be taken to entail (#$affiliatedWith AGENT1 AGENT3).  However, for 'link discovery' purposes, it can be very useful to know that a pair of agents can be tied together via a series of #$affiliatedWith links; moreover, because #$affiliatedWith is a #$genlPreds of a great many more specialized binary relations, #$linkedViaAffiliation affords the user of ferreting out 'chains of affiliation' between agents from masses of data that it might otherwise take a considerable amount of time to sift through.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9bfb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9bfb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
