x_comment(x_treatProperSpecsAsNameableCollections,"This predicate is used to identify collections whose proper specs are prima facie reasonable to treat as \"nameable\" -- i.e., one might reasonaby use a name when making generic claims about these specs qua classes of their instances.  For example, one might use the word \"cancer\" as a name for the class of instances of #$Cancer conditions, say in \"Cancer is a terrible disease.\" Thus (#$treatProperSpecsAsNameableCollections #$AilmentCondition) means that if a UIA user defines a new constant TERM as a spec of #$AilmentCondition, it is reasonable for Cyc to believe that (#$nameableCollection TERM).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9c0a).
