x_comment(x_linkedViaPositiveInterest,"This predicate is a transitive form of the CycL relation #$positiveVestedInterest.  #$positiveVestedInterest is not itself transitive, for the good reason that the fact that, where AGENT1, AGENT2, and AGENT3 are all different, (#$positiveVestedInterest AGENT1 AGENT2) and (#$positiveVestedInterest AGENT2 AGENT3) cannot ordinarily be taken to entail (#$positiveVestedInterest AGENT1 AGENT3).  However, for 'link discovery' purposes, it can be very useful to know that a pair of agents can be tied together via a series of #$positiveVestedInterest links; moreover, because #$positiveVestedInterest is a #$genlPreds of a great many more specialized binary relations, #$linkedViaPositiveInterest affords the user of ferreting out 'chains of affiliation' between agents from masses of data that it might otherwise take a considerable amount of time to sift through.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9c32).
