x_comment(x_maximalPathSystemOfType,"(#$maximalPathSystemOfType SYSTEM TYPE) means that\n\nSYSTEM is a \"maximal\" path system of TYPE.  That is, \n\nSYSTEM is of TYPE and is not a proper #$subPathSystems\n\nof any other path system of TYPE.  SYSTEM might, however,\n\nbe a proper #$subPathSystems of some path system not\n\nof TYPE.  Thus a given path system might be maximal with\n\nrespect to one type to which it belongs, yet not maximal \n\nwith respect to another (perhaps broader) path system \n\ntype to which it also belongs.  For example, a maximal \n\n#$GridStreetSystem that is part of a larger road system\n\nis not a maximal #$RoadSystem.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9c54).
