x_comment(x_linkedViaInterest,"This predicate is a transitive version of the CycL relation #$vestedInterest.  Ordinarily, where AGENT1, AGENT2, and AGENT3 are all #$different, it would not be legitimate to infer that because (#$vestedInterest AGENT1 AGENT2) and (#$vestedInterest AGENT2 AGENT3), (#$vestedInterest AGENT1 AGENT3).  However, there are circumstances in which it can be very useful to know that two agents are linked via a transitive chain of 'interests', especially when the underpinning relationships involved may be more specialized forms of #$vestedInterest:  in a 'raw' database, it could take a human a considerable amount of time poring over the data to discover such linkages.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9c62).
