x_comment(x_CacheBypassFault,"A program has a #$CacheBypassFault if it allows attackers to\nuse an HTML-formatted message to store files outside the cache. Inside\nthe cache, the files are usually governed by a more restrictive\nsecurity policy than outside the cache.  When exploited, this\nvulnerability allows an attacker to store an HTML file in an area that\nis not protected by the policies in cache.   This file may\nthen be used to open arbitrary files on the victim's machine and send\ntheir contents back to the attacker.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9c71).
