x_comment(x_cultureSpecialPractices,"This predicate relates a human culture to types of \n  practices that are distinctive of it though normally only\n  participated in by a relatively small number of its participants.  \n  (#$cultureSpecialPractices CULTURE ACTTYPE ROLE) means that \n  a specialized subcollection of the participants in CULTURE play \n  ROLE in instances of ACTTYPE from time to time, and that most \n  participants in CULTURE would consider such activities important \n  to or distinctive of CULTURE itself.  Examples include \n  religious ceremonies and artistic endeavors that, while \n  distinctive of a given culture, are only directly participated\n  in by a fraction of its members.  For a similar predicate that \n  applies to characteristic practices that are participated in by\n  most or many of a culture's participants, see #$culturePractices.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9c76).
