x_comment(x_endsOfPathSegment,"(#$endsOfPathSegment PATH END) means that END is at one end of the #$Path-Generic PATH; END may be either a junction or a genuine terminal-end of the path segment (note that if PATH is an instance of #$Path-Simple, then it would be related to one of its genuine terminal-ends via the more specialized predicate #$pathTerminus).  #$endsOfPathSegment is also used to relate an instance of #$SimpleLoopedSegmentOfPath (q.v.) to its single end-point.  Note that if PATH is an instance of #$PartiallyTangible, #$SpatialThing, or #$TemporalThing, then END is also; however, neither of them need to be an instance of any of these collections.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9ce0).
