x_comment(x_CommandExecutionFault,"#$CommandExecutionFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW, and an important specialization of #$InputValidationFault.  A program has a #$CommandExecutionFault if an unauthorized person can execute code by sending commands directly to the program, sometimes in the form of a malicious format string (typically with metacharacters), sometimes in the form of a file sent to the program.  When this fault is present in a CGI script, for instance, it allows a remote attacker to run commands on a web server.  This fault is also found on some local programs, which often allows a local user to run commands at an elevated privilege level.  The privilege level of the commands resulting from the exploitation depends on the privilege level of the program being exploited.  For instance, exploiting an #$CommandExecutionFault on a program that runs with root privileges allows a unprivilged user to run commands as root.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9d0f).
