x_comment(x_packetTypeFirewallTarget,"(#$packetTypeFirewallTarget PACKET-TYPE-BY-DIRECTION PACKET-TYPE-BY-PORT FW TARGET) means that packets of type PACKET-TYPE-BY-PORT and PACKET-TYPE-BY-DIRECTION are assigned the attribute TARGET by a firewall program running on FW.  For example, (#$packetTypeFirewallTarget (#$OutgoingWRTLANFn #$CycorpLAN) #$Packet-Internet #$Helmet-Cyc-Com #$Deny-FirewallTarget) means that helmet drops all IP packets that are outgoing with respect to the Cycorp LAN.  Again, for example, (#$packetTypeFirewallTarget (#$DestinationIPFn \"208.209.34.175\") (#$DestinationPortFn #$TransmissionControlProtocol 80) #$Helmet-Cyc-Com #$Accept-FirewallTarget) means that helmet does not filter TCP packets bound for port 80 on 208.209.34.175.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9d20).
