x_comment('x_directionsOfPath-EndToEnd',"This predicate relates a spatial path to the directions between one of            its ends and the other.  (#$directionsOfPath-EndToEnd PATH DIR OPPDIR)            means that the direction from one of PATH's #$endsOfPathSegment to the            other -- call them END1 and END2 -- is DIR and the direction from            END2 to END1 is OPPDIR.  DIR and OPPDIR must of course be opposite            directions, and #$directionsOfPath-EndToEnd is symmetric with respect            to its second and third argument-positions.  This predicate is more            general than #$directionsOfPath in that it does not require that PATH            be relatively straight.  #$directionsOfPath-EndToEnd depends only on            the relative positions of END1 and END2.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9dcf).
