x_comment(x_pathBetween,"(#$pathBetween PATH X Y) means that the #$Path-Simple PATH goes between points (or places) X and Y, where X and Y do not 'overlap', and no further.  Both X and Y have to be on PATH (see #$pointOnPath).  Note that (#$pathBetween PATH X Y) is more specific than (#$pathConnects PATH X Y) because here the PATH cannot extend beyond X and Y.  Within a particular #$PathSystem, a path's end points in the system are unique, and #$pathBetweenInSystem (q.v.) is restricted to paths and points in the system.  When considered without a context of a path system, a path may have several different places at one end, such as Austin and Texas both being at the same end of some path along Highway I-35.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9df1).
