x_comment('x_sourcePatternFor-Indirect',"(sourcePatternFor-Indirect THING1 THING2) means that THING1 is indirectly the source pattern for the structure, arrangement or shape of THING2, only through some intermediate patterned things.  This applies to physical pattern sources (like rubber-stamps as sources of photocopied designs, stencils derived from copies, viral DNA strands indirectly copied, CDs derived indirectly from record-masters via vinyl records, and photocopies of photocopies) as well as abstract patterns that are transformed in multiple stages or that only indirectly affect the configuration of something else.  THING2 is thus a derivative of a derivative of the original, including complementary 'reverse' copies or indirect 'negatives', or an approximate or partial derivative of another derived pattern.  But it needs more than just causal influence: some basic structure of the original pattern should be preserved, despite the multiple stages. See also #$sourcePatternFor-Direct.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9e42).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9e42,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526a9e42,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526a9e42,20318).
