x_comment('x_SymlinkFault-Deletion',"#$SymlinkFault-Deletion is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  It is a specialization of #$FileDeletionFault and #$SymlinkFault-Overwrite.  A program has a #$SymlinkFault-Deletion if when running it writes null to a standard file.  If the file is not the expected file but rather a a symbolic link,\n the null will be written to the file pointed to.  When the malicious user or another user executes the program, it follows the symlink and deletes the specified file.  As with other faults, the severity of #$SymlinkFault-Overwrite depends on the privilege level under which the exploited program is running.  If the program runs at root, for instance, when writing null to the standard files, then the malicious user can delete any known file on the computer.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9e51).
