x_comment(x_smallestSubSystemUnderTraversal,"(#$smallestSubSystemUnderTraversal SUB SYS TRAV) means that\nSUB is the smallest subsystem of SYS such that TRAV is a traversal in\nSUB. (See #$SubSystemUnderTraversalFn, #$traversalInSystem and\n#$pointClosedSubSystems)  Note that 'smallest' here means that no link\nLINK between X and Y in SYS is a link in SUB if neither (#$TraversalFn \n(#$TheList X LINK Y)) nor (TraversalFn (#$TheList Y LINK X)) is a \n#$subTraversals of TRAV. Note also that since SUB is a point-closed\nsubsystem of SYS, every point in SYS that is on TRAV (see\n#$pointOnTraversal) is a point in SUB. Note finally that since SUB is the\n'smallest' subsystem of SYS in which TRAV is a traversal, SUB must be\na #$ConnectedPathSystem.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9e6f).
