x_comment(x_onTraversal,"(#$onTraversal ARG1 TRAV) means that ARG1 is located along the #$Traversal TRAV.  ARG1 could be a moving object or a stationary point (see the more specific predicate #$pointOnTraversal).  For example, if I drive from Austin to Dallas to LA and back to Dallas, and if the #$Traversal TRAV here is characterized by the #$PathChain 'Austin--Dallas--LA--Dallas, then all Austin, Dallas and LA are qualified to be the ARG1 in (#$onTraversal ARG1 TRAV), and so are my car and me.  Let TRAV be (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList X(1) PATH(1) ... X(n) PATH(n) X(n+1))).  Then (#$onTraversal A TRAV) holds if and only if there is a k = 1, ..., n such that (#$onPath A PATH(k)) holds.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9e7b).
