x_comment(x_translationAlongWithinDistance,"(#$translationAlongWithinDistance MOVE TRAV DIST) means that the moving object OBJ (see #$objectMoving) in #$Translation-SingleTrajectory MOVE moves along the #$Traversal TRAV with the #$Distance specified by DIST.  For example, an airplane may fly along the Great Wall, and a person may walk on the top of an oil pipe, or on the side of a river.  But in any case, the 'distance' between OBJ and TRAV should be at most the distance specified by DIST (e.g. (#$Kilometer 100)).  DIST here is an instance of #$Distance which is greater than or equal to the distance between OBJ and TRAV at each moment during the event MOVE.  Note that when DIST equals 'zero-unit' (whatever the #$UnitOfDistance is), we mean that at every moment during MOVE, OBJ is on TRAV (see onTraversal), and hence we would have (#$traverses-Complete MOVE TRAV).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9ed3).
