x_comment(x_FileCommandExecutionFault,"A program has this fault if  it executes arbitrary code in response to invalid input in the form of a file.  Unlike other sorts of #$ArbitraryCommandExecutionFault, this fault is exploited not directly by sending a malformed string to the program but indirectly by sending a  file of some kind to that program, which results in the execution of code  when the file is read.  These faults are common in web browsers, allowing  a malicious web site to execute code by embedding a file in the site  (see, for example, #$CABFileExecutionFault). For cases where a program can be exploited to run executables already existing on a target machine, see #$FileExecutionFault-Local and #$FileExecutionFault-Remote.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9ee4).
