x_comment(x_MakingAPhoneCall,"The collection of all actions wherein a phone call is made by inputting a multi-digit telephone number to a phone system.  It includes both cases where the phone call is 'successful' in the sense that the person whom the caller is trying to contact is contacted, and cases where the call is 'unsuccessful', insofar as the call does not succeed in reaching its intended recipient for any one of a variety of reasons.  The call must, however, actually be 'placed'--dialing must be successfully completed.  Cases where the full number is not dialed do not count as instances of #$MakingAPhoneCall.  The collection includes instances where the call is placed manually, by a human agent picking up a receiver and hitting buttons or dialing a rotary dial, and cases where the call is placed electronically, e.g., via a modem. In cases where an instance of #$MakingAPhoneCall is successful for the agent placing the call, the instance will figure as the initiating subevent in an instance of (#$CommunicatingByMeansOfFn #$Telephone).  As a rule, an instance of #$MakingAPhoneCall will consist of a complete 'dialing' and an instance of #$EstablishingAPhoneLink.  If the placer of the call is human, the instance will usually include an initial act of #$PickingUpATelephoneReceiver.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9f9f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9f9f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
