x_comment(x_ExternalAccessToAccountsFault,"#$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has this fault when it allows unauthorized remote users access to some account on the system.  The more specialized attributes, such as #$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-Root or #$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-User, should be used if possible.  However neither #$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault nor any of its specializations should be used if some more precise attribute (e.g., #$BufferOverflowFault-CommandExecution, #$CommandExecutionFault) applies.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9fa3).
