x_comment(x_pointOnTraversal,"(#$pointOnTraversal A TRAV) means that A is a point along a #$Traversal TRAV of some path or paths.  Let TRAV be (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList X(1) PATH(1) ... X(n) PATH(n) X(n+1))), using a #$PathChain to describe the traversal.  Then (#$pointOnTraversal A TRAV) holds if and only if there is a k = 1, ..., n such that (#$pointOnPath-Generic A PATH(k)).  Note that each PATH(k) is an instance of #$Path-Generic. See also #$Traversal and #$TraversalFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9fb6).
