x_comment(x_BlockedForFn,"For any given movement type TYPE, (#$BlockedForFn TYPE) is the attribute of instances of #$Path-Customary that are blocked for movements of the type TYPE (from end to end).  For example, (#$holdsIn TIME (#$pathState PATH (#$BlockedForFn (#$TransportViaFn #$Truck)))) means that during TIME, PATH is blocked for transportation through PATH (from end to end) via trucks.  Note that when (#$pathState PATH (#$BlockedForFn (#$TransportViaFn #$Truck))) is true during TIME, it says nothing about whether, during TIME, PATH is blocked or open (see #$OpenForFn) for any other kind movement of transportation on PATH. Note also that (#$pathState PATH (#$BlockedForFn TYPE)) does not imply that no movement of the type TYPE is on PATH---it simply means that there is no movement of the type TYPE whose #$objectMoving can get one end from the other through the entire PATH.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9fd1).
