x_comment(x_correlatedStructures,"This is a very general predicate that claims that the so-related items have structures that are somehow correlated, or reflect, one another.  (correlatedStructures THING1 THING2) means that THING1 and THING2 have somehow-correlated structures.  It makes no claim of causal influence; it does not say whether the structure of one influenced the structure of the other, or whether they both are affected by some common third thing, just that there is some correspondence.  (For a very general causal connection, see #$influencesStructure.) The correspondence can be exact or loose and indirect, for example that between written music and the dance motions of someone dancing to it, or between an ancient islamic art pattern and a recent, causally unrelated, wallpaper design.  Thus the truth of this predicate is often in the eye of the beholder, although there are many obvious cases for which almost everyone would agree to the correlation of the structures, e.g. (#$correlatedStructures #$EiffelTower #$TokyoTower).") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9feb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526a9feb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
