x_comment('x_relatedToVia-Least',"Like #$relatedToVia (#$relatedToVia-Least OBJ1 OBJ2 SET NUM) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are related via some sequence of NUM steps via the binary relations in the set SET. More precisely, (#$relatedToVia-Least OBJ1 OBJ2 SET NUM)\n\nmeans that there is a sequence of objects of the length equal to NUM that OBJ1 is the first\n\nelement of the sequence, OBJ2 is the last element of the sequence, and each element of the sequence is\n\nrelated to its successor (if any) by some predicate in SET, or by the inverse of some predicate in SET.  Unlike #$relatedToVia, #$relatedToVia-Least returns in the fourth argument the least number of steps by which OBJ1 and OBJ2 can be related using the relations in SET.") :- x_cid(a65b16526a9ff7).
