x_comment('x_allows-AgentProp',"This predicate relates agents to propositions (as represented by sentences that express them) that they allow to be, or let be, true. (#$allows-AgentProp AGENT SENT) means that AGENT  -- either by performing some action or (more saliently) refraining from performing an action that s/he might have done -- allows the proposition PROP expressed by SENT to become or remain true.  This relation is weaker than being a contributing cause (see e.g. #$enables-ThingProp), but the above formula entails that either (i) AGENT refrains from performing some type of action that s/he is capable of performing and which, were s/he to do it, would (ceteris paribus) prevent (or significantly reduce the likelihood of) PROP's being true or (ii) AGENT performs an action such that, were s/he not to do it (ceteris paribus) the likelihood of PROP's being true would at least be less than it actually was.  A further default assumption is that AGENT knows that her acting or failing to act, as the case may be, has the above consequences for PROP.  For example, if I do nothing to prevent a book's falling off the edge of my desk when I could have caught it, I allow it to be the case that the book falls off the desk.  If a parent answers a child's request for candy by saying \"Yes, you may\", s/he allows it to be true that the child has candy.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa031).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa031,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa031,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
