x_comment(x_influencesStructure,"This is a very general causal predicate that indicates that one thing influences the structure or pattern of another, directly or indirectly.  (influencesStructure THING1 THING2) means that the pattern or structure of THING1 somehow causally affects, or has affected, the pattern or structure of THING2, and that had THING1 been arranged differently in certain ways, THING2 would therefore have been arranged differently.  An example is where THING2 is a copy of THING1, or where THING1 is a computer program that controls the form of THING2.  Contrast this with a mere correlation between the two structures (see #$correlatedStructures).  Unlike the more specific #$sourcePatternFor predicate, #$influencesStructure does not require that any particular pattern in the source be preserved in the affected thing.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa054).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa054,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa054,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
