x_comment(x_perceivesThat,"(#$perceivesThat AGENT PROP) means that AGENT discerns that PROP is true, by the use of one of AGENT's sense modalities. \n\nFor example, an agent may perceive (via seeing) that the water is boiling, or perceive (via smelling) that the roast is done. #$perceivesThat does not relate an agent to any proposition PROP which is not discerned 'directly' by the use of one of its sense modalities. For example, seeing that various events have occurred at various times and later deducing some proposition, PROP, from these observations is not a case or perceiving that PROP. For a practical guideline: It is typically necessary that some sentence of the form 'AGENT Xs that PROP' be true in order for (#$perceivesThat AGENT PROP) to be true, where Xs is a verb expressing the activity of a sense modality, such as 'sees', 'hears', etc. This condition is not satisfied only in cases where AGENT perceives that PROP by the use of some sense modality for which there is no corresponding sensory verb.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa0c1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa0c1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
