x_comment(x_adversarialResponseTo,"(#$adversarialResponseTo ACT SIT) means that (#$inReactionTo ACT SIT) and that ACT is an adversarial or hostile response to  SIT.  Roughly speaking, ACT is an adversarial response if (i) the director or performer of ACT (AGENT1) intends ACT to either threaten or harm some interest of some doer of SIT (AGENT2), and (ii) AGENT1 acts with this intention towards AGENT2 *because of* AGENT2's participation in SIT.  A bit more formally: in the case of an adversarial response, AGENT1 has a goal GOAL1 and AGENT2 has a goal GOAL2 such that AGENT1 believes that AGENT2 is #$responsibleFor SIT and also believes that SIT decreases the likelihood that GOAL1 will be realized. This belief causes AGENT1 to perform the action ACT, which #$startsAfterStartingOf SIT.  AGENT1 believes that ACT decreases the likelihood that GOAL2 will be realized.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa0e6).
