x_comment(x_FourWayJunctionOfPaths,"A collection of junctions of paths. A member of this collection exists where four #$SimpleUnloopedSegmentOfPaths meet together, or where two #$SimpleUnloopedSegmentOfPaths join the two ends of a #$SimpleLoopedSegmentOfPath that loops back to that junction, or else where two #$SimpleLoopedSegmentOfPaths both loop to the same point abstractly forming a figure-eight pattern.  If there is a specified #$PathSystem, use #$fourWayJunctionInSystem instead.  (Determining what constitutes a #$FourWayJunctionOfPaths depends on the #$PathTypes of the joined paths; if it is #$River then only a junction of four segments of rivers qualifies (which is fairly rare), not a place where two roads joins a river.)") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa11d).
