x_comment(x_UrbanArea,"A subcollection of #$HumanResidenceArea.  Each instance of #$UrbanArea is a geographical region the whole of which (more or less) is characterized by typically \"urban\" features (such as streets, buildings, businesses, houses, schools, sidewalks, sewer systems, power lines, automobiles, pedestrians, and so on).  An urban area might be as small as an inner-city street corner or as large as the New York City Metropolitan Area.  By default, urbanness is a \"stuff-like\" property of human residence areas: (nearly) every subregion of an #$UrbanArea is itself an #$UrbanArea.  Examples include #$UTAustinCampus, #$ResearchTrianglePark, and the territorial extent of various cities (#$CityOfAustinTX, #$CityOfToulouseFrance, etc.).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa134).
