x_comment(x_objectField,"This relation is intended to capture a subtle but important\n\nfeature of logical table schemas: namely, it picks out the logical\n\nfield in the schema (possibly corresponding to an 'implicit' field at\n\nthe physical level) whose value denotes the thing that the schema is\n\nabout. Thus, for example, suppose one had a logical table schema\n\nSCHEMA such that any instantiation constituted a description of a\n\nperson in the context of the database. It would therefore be correct\n\nto assert (#$objectField SCHEMA (#$The\n\n#$Person)). In general, then, (#$objectField SCHEMA FIELD)\n\nmeans that FIELD is the #$IndexicalConcept corresponding to the\n\ninstance that SCHEMA actually describes.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa166).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa166,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
