x_comment(x_PointSourceInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic,"A collection of #$CommonVehicleInfectiousDiseaseEpidemics each of whose instances are such that the cases constituting the epidemic result from exposure to the same source of the infecting agent at about the same time, and usually at the same place. Thus all the cases develop symptoms within one incubation period of the #$Microorganism that causes the infection. For example, an outbreak of food poisoning which occurs after ingesting contaminated egg salad served at a picnic at Stewart Park, Ithaca NY on 7/20/2001 would be an instance of #$PointSourceInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic. Typically food-borne and water-borne transmission routes are involved in #$PointSourceInfectiousDiseaseEpidemics. If the date and time of exposure can be determined, one can calculate the incubation period of the pathogen causing the outbreak. The incubation period is the period of time that elapses from the time of exposure to the time of onset of symptoms.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa183).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa183,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
