x_comment(x_BufferOverflowStringFn,"This function takes an instance of a #$ComputerProgram-CW, PROG, as an argument and returns an instance of #$ComputerFile-CW which is designed to exploit the buffer overflow fault (#$BufferOverflowFault-CommandExecution or #$BufferOverflowFault-ProgramCrashing) of PROG.  This file contains a data string that is larger than the buffer for the program can handle, and is designed to be read as input to the program via a function in the program that does not perform bounds checking.  By inputting this file to the program, a hacker can push commands into the execution stack of the computer on which the program is running, and overwrite the return address so that it points back into the buffer.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa21a).
