x_comment(x_fileDoesNotSetParameterToValueOnComputer,"A predicate that relates an instance of #$ConfigurationFile to instances of #$SoftwareParameter, #$CharacterString, and #$ComputationalSystem. (#$fileDoesNotSetParameterToValueOnComputer FILE PARAM VALUE COMP) means that on COMP, when the program configured by FILE runs (see #$fileConfiguresSoftware), it runs with the value of PARAM set by FILE to some value other than VALUE.  For example, if on vega.cyc.com the file /etc/sendmail.cf sets AliasFile to /etc/aliases, it is true that (#$fileDoesNotSetParameterToValueOnComputer #$Sendmail-cf-TheConfigurationFile #$SendmailOption-AliasFile \"/etc/mail/aliases\" #$Vega-Cyc-Com).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa237).
