x_comment(x_synonymousRelnArgs,"(#$synonymousRelnArgs RELN SOURCE LIST) means that when it is known that (#$synonymousExternalConcept RELN SOURCE STRING) or (#$overlappingExternalConcept RELN SOURCE STRING) and STRING appears with an associated set of arguments in an output deriving from SOURCE, the appropriate argument order to observe on the corresponding Cyc relation RELN is given by LIST.  For example suppose (#$synonymousExternalConcept #$ethnicity #$SRATemplateExtractionOntology 'NATIONALITY') and suppose NATIONALITY appears in an #$SRATemplateExtractionOntology mediated output with the arguments 'Sudanese' 'Abu Doha' in that order and , where additional mapping info tells us that 'Abu Doha' corresponds to AbuDoha and 'Sudanese' to #$EthnicGroupOfSudaneseArabs.  (#$synonymousRelnArgs #$ethnicity #$SRATemplateExtractionOntology (TheList 2 1) means that AbuDoha (corresponding to the second argument associated with NATIONALITY) should appear as the first argument to #$ethnicity, and #$EthnicGroupOfSudaneseArabs (corresponding to the first argument shown with NATIONALITY) should appear as the second argument to #$ethnicity.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa242).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa242,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa242,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
