x_comment('x_Subcommittee-Organization',"The collection of all subcommittees formally organized by their parent committees (instances of #$Committee-Organization), usually to accomplish tasks or address issues determined by their parent committees. Typically, subcommittees are formed in order to divide up large tasks or issues addressed by the parent committee into smaller tasks or issues to be addressed by the subcommittee and reported back to the parent committee. Instances of #$Subcommittee-Organization usually operate in accordance with rules or procedures inherited from or determined by their parent committees. Each instance of #$Subcommittee-Organization consists of at least two (and perhaps many) individual #$CommitteeMembers and may, in certain instances, include a #$CommitteeChairman. Note that since a subcommittee is itself a committee, the collection #$Subcommittee-Organization is a subcollection of #$Committee-Organization. However one salient difference between the two is that every instance of #$Subcommittee-Organization necessarily bears the relation #$subOrganizations with a unique instance of #$Committee-Organization, while not every committee must have subcommittees.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa256).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa256,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
