x_comment(x_CycLToELFn,"(#$CycLToELFn CYCL-EXPR) denotes the EL version of CYCL-EXPR.  NARTs are unreified, #$CycLAssertions are converted to their EL forms, etc.. This is an extremely useful function to use in situations where an #$ELFormula is needed because of arg constraints, but you don't happen to have one handy. For example, since the #$arg3Isa of the function #$SubstituteFormulaFn is #$ELFormula, trying to get terms substituted within #$CycLNonAtomicTerms won't work since these are #$CycLFormulas. With this function, one can do a quick conversion, create the EL version of the NAT, and have the substitution take place on that like so: (#$SubstituteFormulaFn #$Emu #$Cat (#$CycLToELFn (#$JuvenileFn #$Cat))).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa27d).
