x_comment('x_InfectingEvent-MechanicalVectorBorneTransmission',"The collection of #$InfectingEvent-VectorBorneTransmissions in which the infectious agent is merely transported by a living #$Animal to a susceptible host (see #$infectingVector). For example, an insect vector may carry the infectious agent on its feet or proboscis as it flies and crawls or the infectious agent may pass through its gastrointestinal tract. Another example would be a rodent carrying fleas infected with the #$Plague-Bacterium. A rodent's transporting the fleas is an example of a #$InfectingEvent-MechanicalVectorBorneTransmission. In contrast, a biting by an infected flea would be an example of a #$InfectingEvent-BiologicalVectorBorneTransmission because the flea is infected by #$Plague-Bacterium and the latter undergoes part of its life cycle within the flea before the flea can transmit the infective form of #$Plague-Bacterium.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa294).
