x_comment('x_InfectingEvent-BiologicalVectorBorneTransmission',"The collection of #$InfectingEvent-VectorBorneTransmissions in which the infectious agent infects a living #$Animal (see #$infectingVector) before developing into a form that can infect a #$Vertebrate host species. The pathogen must propagate (multiply), develop cyclically, or both inside the vector before the vector is capable of transmitting the pathogen in its infective form. The time period between the infection of the vector and the pathogen becoming infective to a different host species is the extrinsic incubation period for the infectious agent. The infectious agent may be transmitted to a #$Vertebrate host in several ways which include via saliva during biting, or by regurgitation or deposition of feces or other material on the skin which penetrates through the bite wound or through the abrasions caused by scratching.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa29d).
