x_comment(x_favorableResponseTo,"(#$favorableResponseTo ACT SIT) means that #$Action, ACT is #$inReactionTo the situation, SIT, and that ACT is an favorable response to  SIT.  Roughly  speaking,  ACT is a favorable response if (i) the director or performer of ACT (AGENT1) intends ACT to assist some interest of some doer of SIT (AGENT2), and (ii) AGENT1 acts with this intention towards AGENT2 *because of* AGENT2's participation in SIT.   A bit more  formally: in the case of  a favorable response, AGENT1 has a goal GOAL1 and believes AGENT2 has a goal GOAL2 such that AGENT1 believes that AGENT2 is #$responsibleFor SIT and also believes that SIT increases the likelihood  that GOAL1 will be realized. This belief causes AGENT1 to perform the action ACT, which #$startsAfterStartingOf  SIT.  AGENT1 believes that ACT increases the likelihood that GOAL2 will be realized.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa2c7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa2c7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
