x_comment(x_rowInSourceClaims,"This predicate relates a structured knowledge source with a CycL sentence that expresses one or more of the physical field values which appear in some row of the knowledge source.  The sentence does not itself interpret logical meaning of the row, or of its field values, but only expresses the physical field values in Cyc.  More formally, let SOURCE denote an instance of #$StructuredKnowledgeSource and SENTENCE denotes an instance of #$ELSentence-Assertible, then (#$rowInSourceClaims SOURCE SENTENCE) is true precisely if SENTENCE is a CycL representation of one or more of the physical field values in some row of SOURCE. See also the predicate #$fieldValue, which is often used in SENTENCE to express the physical field values of a row in CycL.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa2e9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa2e9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
