x_comment('x_kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Binary',"(#$kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Binary BROADP NARROWP COL1\n\nCOL2) indicates that whenever [1] (BROADP INS1 INS2) is known and [2]\n\nCOL1, COL2 are respectively the 1st and 2nd argument type constraint on NARROWP and\n\n[3] INS1, INS2 are instances of COL1, COL2 resp., then (NARROWP INS1\n\nINS2) is likely to be true. This predicate is used to suggest plausible\n\nspecializations to ke'rs via the predicate strengthener. If one of the\n\n#$Collection arguments is irrelevant to the suggested restriction, use\n\nthe arg type constraint for BROADP in that position. E.g.  if\n\n(#$kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Binary BROADP NARROWP BROAD_COL1 COL2)\n\nand (#$arg1Isa BROADP BROAD_COL1), then that collection is ignored by the\n\nstrengthener.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa346).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa346,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa346,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
