x_comment(x_epidemicTypeResultsFromTransmissionType,"(#$epidemicTypeResultsFromTransmissionType EPI-TYPE INFECTING-TYPE) means that typically the type of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic EPI-TYPE is the result of #$InfectingEvents of type INFECTING-TYPE. This predicate is used to make type-level statements about the type of #$InfectingEvent that typically causes the #$Infections that constitute #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics of a certain type. For example, (#$epidemicTypeResultsFromTransmissionType #$AirborneEpidemic #$InfectingEvent-AirborneTransmission) means that typically #$AirborneEpidemics are the result of #$InfectingEvent-AirborneTransmissions. However, it is possible for an instance of #$AirborneEpidemic to have some #$epidemicInfectionCases that result from a different type of #$InfectingEvent, for example, from #$InfectingEvent-DirectTransmissions.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa348).
