x_comment('x_kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Inverse',"(#$kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Inverse BROADP NARROWP COL1\nCOL2) indicates that whenever [1] (BROADP INS1 INS2) is known and [2] COL1, COL2\nare respectively the 2nd and 1st arg constraint on NARROWP and [3] INS1,\nINS2 are instances of, resp., COL1 and COL2, then (NARROWP\nINS2 INS1) is likely to be true. This predicate is used to suggest\nplausible specializations to ke'rs via the predicate strengthener. If one\nof the #$Collection arguments is irrelevant to the suggested restriction,\nuse the arg constraint for BROADP in that position. E.g.  if\n(#$kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Inverse BROADP NARROWP BROAD_COL1 COL2)\nand (#$arg1Isa BROADP BROAD_COL1), then that collection is ignored by the\nstrengthener.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa355).
