x_comment(x_alleged,"(#$alleged AGENT SENTENCE) means that AGENT has alleged that the proposition expressed by the CycL formula FORMULA is true. An allegation remains in force as long as the alleger doesn't withdraw it and the allegation is not disproven. To allege something is to assert it without presently being able to prove it. It is similar to conjecturing, but alleging is essentially a public act and carries with it the implication that the alleger is under some obligation to attempt to prove what is alleged. The publicity of allegation also plays into when it is considered to be in force: an allegation that is not remembered by anyone is no longer in force. Note that \"allegations\" in the present sense are not typically about wrongdoing.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa4a9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa4a9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
