x_comment(x_FirewallTypeByPacketTarget,"A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of firewall programs in a particular state with respect to how they assign attributes to packets.  The instances of\n\n#$FirewallTypeByPacketTarget represent features or attributes that a firewall program F assigns to a\n\npacket P that determine the fate of P when P arrives at the computer on\n\nwhich F is running. The most common #$FirewallTypeByPacketTarget are\n\n#$Accept-FirewallTarget, #$Deny-FirewallTarget,\n\n#$Reject-FirewallTarget, #$Redirect-FirewallTarget, and\n\n#$Masquerade-FirewallTarget.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa4e5).
