x_comment(x_HumanCulture,"A specialization of #$Culture-Practice and #$AnimalActivity each instance of which is a very extended, multi-performer activity involving social and material modifications by #$HomoSapiens to their environment. Human cultures are generally considered very important by their participants (see #$cultureParticipants). Humans tend to identify themselves largely in relation to the cultures in which they participate.  Exactly what sorts of events constitute a human culture is hard to specify (see the instances of #$CultureClassificationType for guidance here), but cultures generally can at least be said to involve the following sorts of activities on the part of many of their participants: (1) the expression of certain characteristic beliefs, (2) the following of certain characteristic practices, and (3) the use (and sometimes, production) of certain characteristic artifacts. See #$cultureBeliefs, #$culturePractices, #$cultureSpecialPractices, and #$cultureArtifacts.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa4e9).
