x_comment(x_positionOfPersonInOrganization,"The predicate #$positionOfPersonInOrganization is used to relate a particular person to his or her position in a particular organization.  (#$positionOfPersonInOrganization PERSON ORG POS-TYPE) means that the #$Person PERSON  is a member of the #$Organization ORG, and holds a position of type POS-TYPE.  Even in an employment situation, POS-TYPE may or may not specifically indicate PERSON 's occupational field or training; for example, one individual occupying a position of #$Manager may be a #$MarketingPerson, while another is an #$ElectricalEngineer.  In addition, POS-TYPE may or may not correspond to an official `Job Title' (cf. #$titleOfPersonInOrganization), or be the primary occupation of PERSON .  Note that assertions using #$positionOfPersonInOrganization should be properly time-constrained.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa4fb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa4fb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
