x_comment(x_identifiedThing,"This predicate allows one to specify an instance of #$Individual\nidentified in some instance of #$Identifying.\n(#$identifiedThing IDENT IND) means that in the instance\nIDENT of #$Identifying the instance IND of #$Individual\nis identified.  For example, to partially represent in #$CycL, say,\na process of tree identification carried out by some biologists,\nwe might use the GAF, (#$identifiedThing IDENT002 OAK004),\nif one of the biologists identified a particular tree as an\ninstance OAK004 of #$OakTree in some instance IDENT002 of\n#$Identifying.  See also #$IdentifyingObjectAsType,\n          #$identifiedAsType and #$IdentifyingAsTypeFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa4fe).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa4fe,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
