x_comment(x_alterEgoOfHero,"This predicate is used to relate instances of   #$Superhero with their alter-egos, in   the #$FictionalContexts in which the     alter-ego relationship holds.    For example, (#$alterEgoOfHero    #$BruceWayne-MillionaireSocialite #$Batman)   says that Bruce Wayne is Batman's 'secret   identity,' and should be asserted in    those contexts in which this is held to    be true, e.g., (#$ContextOfPCWFn    #$Batman-The1960sTVShow).  Keep in mind    the importance of contexts here: Though   it's true in the above context that    (#$alterEgoOfHero #$DickGrayson-HeroAlterEgo       #$Robin-BatmanSidekick), the same   assertion is not always true in others, e.g.,   (#$ContextOfPCWFn #$BatmanTheAnimatedSeries-TheTVShow), where    Robin's secret identity is generally  #$TimDrake-HeroAlterEgo.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa537).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa537,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa537,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
