x_comment(x_normalityOfThing,"A predicate to describe how normal a thing is to a 'typical observer'.  (#$normalityOfThing THING COL NORMALITY) means that, for an instance of COL, THING has the normality level NORMALITY for a typical observer. The notion of typical observer will, of course, be dependent on the microtheory in which the assertion is made.  Such assertions need to be asserted in sufficiently specific contexts.  Note that normality is different from but related to frequency (e.g. #$frequencyOfActionType, #$Frequency). For example, a mechanic sees broken cars every day, but those cars are still abnormal cars.  To assert the normality of thing for a particular observer, see #$normalityForAgent.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa53a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa53a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa53a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
