x_comment(x_acquaintances,"(#$acquaintances PERSON AGENT ACQUAINTANCE-PRED) means that PERSON is acquainted with AGENT, at least in the way (and/or to the degree) specified by ACQUAINTANCE-PRED; i.e. (ACQUAINTANCE-PRED PERSON AGENT).  Note that AGENT must be an #$IntelligentAgent, so this is not the predicate to use to express the fact that Fred `is acquainted with' drag racing.  Note that, depending on the value for ACQUAINTANCE-PRED, there may or may not be some way in which one can conclude that AGENT is acquainted with PERSON.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa53f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa53f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
