x_comment(x_differentInQuantity,"(#$differentInQuantity THING1 THING2 QUANT-TYPE) means that the two things THING1 and THING2 do not have the same values of the quantity type QUANT-TYPE.  Here 'the same' could mean complete identity or close resemblance -- what this 'different' means, and what the standard of closeness or identity is, depends on the context, but #$differentInQuantity and #$identicalInQuantity cannot both be correctly asserted of the same two things.  See also #$resemblesInQuantity.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa54f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa54f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
