x_comment(x_hyphenString,"(#$hyphenString STRINGS WORD PART TERM) means, just as with #$multiWordString, that the translation of the phrase or word containing STRINGS and WORD, with part of speech PART, is TERM. (See #$multiWordString for further usage notes). In addition, this predicate specifies that STRINGS and WORD may occur in THREE juxtapositions: they may be separated not only 1: by a space, but also 2: with a hyphen or 3: run together with no space at all. For example, (#$hyphenString (#$TheList \"time\") #$Zone-TheWord #$CountNoun #$TimeZone)denotes that \"time zone\", \"time-zone\", and \"timezone\" are all acceptable forms of the word.  In generation, by default, the hyphenated form will be used (e.g. \"time-zone\")") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa556).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa556,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
