x_comment(x_contentSentenceOfSchema,"(#$contentSentenceOfSchema SCHEMA\nSENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a logical feature, or domain\nassumption, of SCHEMA.  For example, (#$contentSentenceOfSchema\n#$TestLanguageSpoken-LS (#$completeExtentEnumerable #$languageSpoken))\nmeans that the complete extent of #$languageSpoken is known in any\ncontent microtheory which interprets data using the logical schema\n#$TestLanguageSpoken-LS.  These SENTENCEs are valid from within or\nbelow the 'content microtheory' associated with SOURCE via the\npredicate #$contentMt.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa55f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa55f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
