x_comment(x_naturalImmunity,"(#$naturalImmunity ORGANISM PATHOGEN-TYPE) means that ORGANISM has resistance to diseases caused by pathogens of PATHOGEN-TYPE mediated by cells capable of immune activity without being stimulated by immunization, or acquired through contact with an #$Antigen.  Natural immunity is non-specific and includes barriers to infectious agents, see #$Infection and #$LivingBiologicalAgent. For example, natural immunity activities are conducted by #$Skin, mucous membrane, #$NaturalKillerCells, phagocytosis, inflammation, interferon , and a variety of non-specific factors. Natural immunity may vary with age and with hormonal or metabolic activity.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa573).
