xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa57d,[]).
x_comment(x_EvaluativePredicate,"A collection of predicates whose instances are designed to predicate value judgements, in a broad sense of the  phrase that includes pragmatic, moral, and aesthetic assessments of a thing by an agent.    The salient example is that of evaluative\nstates: the subjective assessment of the value of an action is something\nprojected onto the world, i.e. not entirely objective, though not\nnecessarily dependent upon any one individual mind. An evaluative\nassessment in this sense may, for instance, supervene on the attitudes of\nmany minds -- those of a military unit, say, or of a country, or perhaps of\na culture.  These predicate can be used on their own to attribute an evaluatory property to an action relative to an agent or, they can be used as argument places in predicates that are specifically\ndefined for them, e.g. #$evaluates-Propositional.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa57e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa57e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa57e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa57e,23090).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa57e,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa57e,[]).
x_comment(x_SoftwareDevelopment,"A specialization of #$DevelopingAProduct and #$WritingAComputerProgram. The collection of events in which an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW is developed. The development process may involve several rounds of producing prototypes and fixing bugs and extending features.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa57f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa57f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa57f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa57f,23098).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa57f,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa57f,[]).
x_comment(x_GoalTypeByCategory,"A collection of collections.  Each element of #$GoalTypeByCategory is a collection of goals (sentences whose truth is intended to be acted towards by some agent) that represent a particular category of goals, e.g., #$ForeignPolicyGoal, #$NationalDefenseGoal, #$TradeGoal.  More precisely, elements of #$GoalTypeByCategory indicate the status of a goal when possessed by a particular #$Agent-Generic.  The qualification is important because goals may fall into different categories depending on who possesses them.  For example, improving the Russian economy might be a #$NationalEconomyGoal of #$Russia and a #$ForeignPolicyGoal of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.  Taking a closer look at the example, #$NationalEconomyGoal is the collection of goals that are national economy goals.  In other words, they are the collection of sentences such that someone's goal is to make them true to help improve or somehow affect their national economy.  So, \"improving the Russian economy\" is a national economy goal by virtue of #$Russia's attitude towards it.  To attribute a goal and category to an agent use #$goalCategoryForAgent.  ") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa580).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa580,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa580,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa580,23099).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa580,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa580,[]).
x_comment('x_evaluates-Propositional',"This predicate can be used to describe propositional attitudes in terms of an agent attributing a certain type of evaluative attitude (q.v.) to a proposition. (#$evaluates-Propositional AGENT SENT EVAL-PRED) means that AGENT attributes to some action, ACT, described by SENT the \nattitude that would be expressed by (EVAL-PRED AGENT ACT).  Thus it represents a certain propositional attitude on the part of AGENT toward that action.    Such attitudes correspond in some case to stances that are largely based on emotion, and in other cases to reasoned evaluative judgments. Entities capable of taking evaluative stances are entities capable of manifesting interests in purposeful action, hence the restriction of the first argument to #$Agent-Generic.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa581).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa581,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa581,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa581,23100).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa581,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa581,[]).
x_comment(x_EconomicGoal,"The attribute characterizing goals which  have to do with economic ends. This can include personal goals, such  as gaining employment, or maximizing one's income, to national or  company goals, such as reducing one's national budget deficit or  maximizing profits.--Okeefe, June 24, 1998") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa582).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa582,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa582,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa582,23102).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa582,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa582,[]).
x_comment(x_RadiallySymmetricObject,"A specialization of #$SpatialThing.  Each instance of #$RadiallySymmetricObject is a spatial thing whose spatial parts are regularly arranged about a central axis.  Instances of #$RadiallySymmetricObject include wheels and adult starfish.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa583).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa583,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
