xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa588,[]).
x_comment(x_evidentialSupportForBelief,"#$evidentialSupportForBelief AGENT INFO GEN-VAL-PRED) means that the evidence AGENT has bearing on the truth of INFO makes it reasonable to have degree represented by GEN-VAL-PRED of belief in INFO. Roughly, this is to say that there is some (possibly complex) proposition PROP such that (#$beliefs AGENT PROP) and (#$conditionalProbability INFO PROP NUMBER), where given the domain assumptions of the relevant Mt, NUMBER falls within the range determined by the #$GenericValuePredicate GEN-VAL-PRED.  What this means is if there were a quantity type called \"EvidentialSupport\" and GEN-VAL-PRED was, say, #$mediumAmountOf, then AGENT would have a (#$MediumAmountFn \"EvidentialSupport\") for the Information INFO.  (#$evidentialSupportForBelief AGENT INFO GEN-VAL-PRED) does not mean that AGENT in fact does have that degree of belief in INFO; that is, it does not entail (#$confidenceLevel AGENT INFO AMOUNT)) wher AMOUNT corresponds to the amount represented by GEN-VAL-PRED. arg3 is constrained to be an instance of #$GenericValuePredicate, rather than of #$Real0-1, in order to make use of this predicate feasible in practice (since we can often say of an agent that she has a low, medium or high amount of evidence for a given proposition, but can rarely or never say she has exactly N degree of evidence, for some particular instance N of Real0-1). This predicate's main use is in stating relations among propositional attitudes such as those expressed by #$beliefs, #$knows, #$goals and so on; there will probably be relatively few occasions to assert GAFs with #$evidentialSupportForBelief as arg zero.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa589).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa589,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa589,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa589,23109).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa589,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa589,[]).
x_comment(x_unacceptablyCostly,"(#$unacceptablyCostly AGT ACTION) holds just in case in AGT's considered opinion ACTION is too costly to perform.  The respect to which the action is considered too costly is undetermined, but meant to indicate an \"all things considered\" judgement.  Typically, this will be true when the agent judges that the cost of an action vastly exceeds the benefits of its\nexpected outcome, i.e., that the cost of the action is unacceptable with\nrespect to the goal of the agent. This is not to be understood merely as a\ngenerically negative disposition or feeling toward the action.  Often this will be used as an argument place certain other predicates: e.g. #$costOfAction.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa58a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa58a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa58a,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa58a,23110).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa58a,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa58a,[]).
x_comment(x_attitudeTowardsEvent,"#$attitudeTowardsEvent(AGT EVT DEGREE-OF-EMOTYPE) means that the #$SentientAnimal AGT has the instance of #$FeelingAttribute DEGREE-OF-EMOTYPE about the #$Event EVT.  By `attitude' we mean a feeling which may be latent and/or long-lasting.  The third argument to this predicate is usually constructed by wrapping a specialization of #$FeelingAttribute in a generic value function such as #$HighAmountFn.  Please avoid using these functions with #$FeelingAttribute itself.  To refer to feelings that AGT experiences immediately and consciously towards EVT, use #$feelsTowardsEvent.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa58b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa58b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa58b,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa58b,23114).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa58b,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa58b,[]).
x_comment(x_commensurateToBenefits,"(#$commensurateToBenefits AGT ACTION) holds just in case in AGT's considered opinion the cost of performing ACTION is commensurate to its benefits.  This predicate can encode an agent's evaluative\njudgment that the cost of an action does not exceed the benefits of its\nexpected outcome, i.e., that the cost of the action is acceptable with\nrespect to the goal of the agent. This is not to be understood as a\ngenerically positive evaluative disposition or feeling toward the action.  This predicate is often used in the 4th argument place of #$costOfAction") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa58c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa58c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa58c,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa58c,23115).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa58c,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa58c,[]).
x_comment(x_anatomicalResourceRequired,"#$anatomicalResourceRequired is an instance of #$ResourcePredicate. (#$anatomicalResourceRequired ACT BODYPARTTYPE NUM) means that the successful doer of ACT must have at least this many (NUM) of the #$AnimalBodyPartType BODYPARTTYPE. For example, if VOLANT is an instance of #$Flying-FlappingWings, then (#$anatomicalResourceRequired VOLANT #$Wing-AnimalBodyPart 2).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa58d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa58d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa58d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa58d,23120).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa58d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa58d,[]).
x_comment(x_anatomicalPartTypeRequired,"#$anatomicalPartTypeRequired is an instance of #$ResourcePredicate. '(#$anatomicalPartTypeRequired ACT-TYPE PART-TYPE ROLE)' means that the successful player of ROLE in an act of ACT-TYPE must have at least one physical part of type PART-TYPE.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa58e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa58e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa58e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa58e,23121).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa58e,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa58e,[]).
x_comment(x_NervousSystem,"A specialization of both #$ConnectedPhysicalPathSystem  and #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$NervousSystem is a bodily system composed of the brain, spinal cord, and nerves of an animal (see the collections #$Brain, #$SpinalCord, and #$Nerve).  This system enables the animal to receive, interpret, and respond to various stimuli.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa58f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa58f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa58f,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
