xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa5b5,[]).
x_comment(x_residesInRegion,"This predicate relates a person or other sort of animal to a geographical region in which or the geopoliticalEntity in whose territory s/he/it resides.  (#$residesInRegion RESIDENT GEO) means that RESIDENT lives or resides primarily in (the territory of) GEO.  This obviously does not entail that RESIDENT is physically in GEO at any particular time, since people are often away from their places of residence. Note that a given person/animal (even with respect to a particular time) is normally related by #$residesInRegion to many different regions, where each such region is a sub- or super-region of some of the others.  For example, Karen currently resides in Austin, in Texas, in the United States, in North America, and so on.  See also #$residesInDwelling, #$hasHabitat, and #$ethnicity.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa5b6).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa5b6,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
