xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa5c9,[]).
x_comment(x_coversWithConformity,"(#$coversWithConformity OBJ SHEET LEVEL) means that OBJ is covered by SHEET, and that the inner surface of SHEET conforms to the surface features of OBJ to the degree LEVEL.  SHEET may cover OBJ in either the sense of #$covers-Ruglike or #$covers-Baglike.  For example, hosiery covers legs with a #$highAmountOf conformity; sweat pants have #$lowAmountOf conformity to legs.  Level of conformity could probably based on the average of the distance between of lines going normal to the inside surface of OBJ to SHEET.  The lowness or highness of this number would be based on comparison to representative exemplars.  E.g. in a low conformity case, e.g. the average OBJ to SHEET distance for a pen in a grocery bag would be high relative to the dimensions of the pen.  Thus level would be #$lowAmountOf.  The analogous measure for a leg inside spandex pants would be very low compared to the dimensions of the leg.  In such a case LEVEL would be #$highAmountOf.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa5ca).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa5ca,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa5ca,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa5ca,23230).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa5ca,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa5ca,[]).
x_comment(x_qualitativeContent,"qualitative description of the amount present (or contained) of some type of stuff (e.g., (#$qualitativeContent(Leaf #$Chlorophyll #$veryHighAmountOf)).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa5cb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa5cb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
