x_comment(x_genericallyEquivalentQuantity,"(#$genericallyEquivalentQuantity COL SLOT QUANT GVP) <=> The #$GenericValuePredicate GVP's arg2 is equivalent to the quantity QUANT when it appears on SLOT in the context of instances of COL.  For example, (#$genericallyEquivalentQuantity #$Sprinter #$age (#$YearsDuration 14 17) #$lowAmountOf) holds just in case being age 14-17 is a low amount on the slot #$age with respect to instances of #$Sprinter.  In other words, it states that 14-17 is a low age for sprinters.  This is a way to relativize the values for #$lowAmountOf.  It is as if, in the context of sprinter's ages, (#$lowAmountOf #$Time-Quantity (#$YearsDuration 14 17)) holds.  Or, equivalently, in the context of sprinter's ages (#$LowAmountFn #$Time-Quantity) =   (#$YearsDuration 14 17).   ") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa5ce).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa5ce,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa5ce,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa5ce,23234).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa5ce,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa5ce,[]).
x_comment(x_relativeIntensityOfCondition,"This predicate allows us to relativize a subject's\ndiscomfort with respect to a particular symptom or ailment condition.\n(#$relativeIntensityOfCondition COND BLO DIS-LEVEL) means that BLO has\nthe level of discomfort DIS-LEVEL as a result of\nCOND.  Note that (#$relativeIntensityOfCondition COND BLO DIS-LEVEL)\nimplies that the agent has the condition COND.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa5cf).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa5cf,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa5cf,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
