x_comment(x_decreasesCausallyOverPeriod,"(#$decreasesCausallyOverPeriod EVENT THING SLOT PERIOD) means that EVENT causes the value of the predicate SLOT applied to THING to be lower immediately after (#$STIF q.v.)  PERIOD than it was immediately before (#$STIB q.v.) PERIOD.  PERIOD must start no earlier than EVENT starts in order to prevent effects preceeding their causes.  If PERIOD ends before EVENT, it still must be the case that the value of SLOT applied to THING must be lower immediately following EVENT than it was immediately before EVENT.  Like with #$decreasesImmediately, the decrease need not be monotonic.  This predicate is agnostic as to whether the decrease occurs during EVENT or after it.  See #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of related predicates.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa5f1).
