x_comment(x_LocallyExploitableFn,"(#$hasVulnerability COMPUTER (#$LocallyExploitableFn VULNERABILITY)) means that COMPUTER is an instance of the #$ComputerTypeByVulnerability VULNERABILITY and, furthermore, this vulnerability is due to the presence of a faulty #$LocalProgram on COMPUTER.  Only users who are logged in on COMPUTER may directly exploit this kind of vulnerability.  For example, (#$hasVulnerability #$Crystal-Cyc-Com (#$LocallyExploitableFn #$VulnerableToOSCrashing)) means that a savvy hacker or incautious user who was logged in on #$Crystal-Cyc-Com could cause the #$OperatingSystem to crash.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa606).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa606,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
