x_comment(x_RemotelyExploitableFn,"(#$hasVulnerability COMPUTER (#$RemotelyExploitableFn VULNERABILITY)) means that COMPUTER is an instance of the #$ComputerTypeByVulnerability VULNERABILITY and, furthermore, this vulnerability is due to the presence of a faulty #$ServerProgram on COMPUTER.  This vulnerability therefore may be directly exploited by a remote attacker (i.e., one who is not logged in on COMPUTER).  For example, (#$hasVulnerability #$Crystal-Cyc-Com (#$RemotelyExploitableFn #$VulnerableToOSCrashing)) means that a savvy remote hacker could crash the #$OperatingSystem running on #$Crystal-Cyc-Com.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa607).
