x_comment(x_WavePropagation,"A specialization of #$Translocation (q.v.).  Each instance of #$WavePropagation is an event in which a wavelike disturbance propagates through space, with or without a medium.  A wave propagation is like  a translational movement (see #$Movement-TranslationEvent) in that it can have both a starting and an ending point (see #$fromLocation and #$toLocation), but differs from a translational motion in that there is no object moving (see #$objectMoving).  Notable specializations of #$WavePropagation include #$ElectromagneticRadiation and #$Sound.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa61a).
