x_comment('x_Cell-Organization',"An instance of #$OrganizationTypeByStructuralCharacteristic, and a specialization of #$OrganizationOfPeopleOnly. Each instance of #$Cell-Organization is a sub-organization of some larger organization, where the larger organization is divided into many instances of #$Cell-Organization. Each instance of #$Cell-Organization is a small group of people who perform a set of tasks for the larger organization to which the cell belongs. Each cell within the larger organization is relatively isolated from all the other cells in that organization, so that members of one cell will generally not know members of the other cells, nor will they generally know what the other cells are doing for the larger organization. Organizations that structure themselves into cells usually do so because they wish to conceal their activities, and the extent of their membership, from others (so organizations that structure themselves into cells will usually be instances of #$CovertAgent, such as intelligence groups, criminal organizations, or terrorist groups). By organizing itself into independent cells, an organization ensures that its members will be able to divulge the identities and activities of only a few other members of that organization, if those members defect from the organization, or if they are captured by some agent interested in knowing about the organization's activities.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa61e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa61e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa61e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa61e,23330).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa61e,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa61e,[]).
x_comment(x_precedesInGraphicalStructure,"(#$precedesInGraphicalStructure WHOLE PART1 PART2) means that, within the #$GraphicalStructure WHOLE, the #$GraphicalStructure PART1 comes before the #$GraphicalStructure PART2.  There are certain types of #$GraphicalStructure that always precede certain other types of #$GraphicalStructure within an inclusive #$GraphicalStructure.  For example, within a #$CWStructure, an instance of #$TableOfContents always #$precedesInGraphicalStructure an instance of #$TextString that it is an #$alphabeticalIndexTo.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa61f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa61f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
