x_comment('x_AtomicSymbol-Abstract',"A specialization of #$AbstractInformationStructure (q.v.).  This is the collection of all abstract symbols that are not composed of further symbols.  By 'abstract symbol' we mean any abstract object whose concrete instantiations have meaning, broadly construed, according to some convention.  For example, the Roman letter 'A' is an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract, whereas concrete instantiations of it (see #$CharacterToken) are not.  The character string 'ABC' is not an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract, because it is composed of more than one symbol.  An arbitrary #$AbstractStructure (such as the abstract structure of carbon dioxide) is not #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract unless its instantiations have a meaning, according to some convention.  Other examples include all instances of #$Character-Abstract, punctuation marks, words (but not their corresponding character strings), symbols of diagram types (e.g. the symbols used in schematic diagrams for electrical curcuits), and abstract individual sound structures (see e.g #$Phoneme).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa627).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa627,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa627,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa627,23339).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa627,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa627,[]).
x_comment(x_partialInfoStructureOfCW,"(#$partialInfoStructureOfCW WORK STRUCTURE) means that an #$AbstractStructure of WORK contains the information structure STRUCTURE. For example, #$MobyDickNovel (an instance of #$PropositionalConceptualWork) has as partial information structures the #$AbstractInformationStructure \"fish\" (used in English versions) and \"poisson\" (used in French versions), as well as the entire abstract sequences of characters that were used in the writing of any edition of #$MobyDickNovel. This predicate allows us to refer to information structures used in a particular work without reference to any instantiation of that work.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa628).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa628,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
