x_comment(x_argsIsa,"A binary #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.) that is used to put a specified #$isa based argument-type constraint on all of a given relation's argument-places at once.  (#$argsIsa RELN COL) means that semantic well-formedness requires that each argument to which RELN is applied (regardless of argument-place) be an instance of COL.  For example, '(#$argsIsa #$PlusFn #$ScalarInterval)' means that the function #$PlusFn must only be applied to scalar intervals.   #$argsIsa is particularly useful for constraining (any and all of) the arguments to a #$VariableArityRelation (the preceding example being a case in point); though #$argsIsa may be applied to fixed-arity relations as well.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its immediate specializations.  See also #$argsGenl.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa642).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa642,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa642,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa642,23386).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa642,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa642,[]).
x_comment(x_MKSUnitOfMeasure,"A specialization of #$SIUnitOfMeasure and an instance of #$UnitOfMeasureTypeBySystem-Coherent.  Each instance of #$MKSUnitOfMeasure is a #$UnitOfMeasure which is part of the MKS system of measurement.  As its name suggests, MKS has three base units (see #$MKSUnitOfMeasure-Base): #$Meter, #$Kilogram, and #$SecondsDuration.  Derived units are those that can be defined algebraically from the base units or obtained by adding a #$MetricUnitPrefix to a non-prefixed MKS unit. Some instances of #$MKSUnitOfMeasure are #$CubicMeter, #$Joule, and #$KiloWatt.  Some notable non-instances are #$MetricTon, #$HoursDuration, and #$Liter.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa643).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa643,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa643,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa643,23387).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa643,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa643,[]).
x_comment(x_ParaphraseDataMicrotheory,"The collection of all microtheories containing assertions that specify a way to paraphrase an individual CycL expression or type of CycL expression. The body of assertions visible from a given\n#$ParaphraseDataMicrotheory constitutes a theory for paraphrasing CycL\nwithin certain parameters, such as a single natural language or\na specific application.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa644).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa644,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
