x_comment(x_CalendarSeason,"A specialization of #$Date and an instance of #$CalendarCoveringType and #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries-CoveringAndDisjoint (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$CalendarSeason is a time interval that is thought of by a significant group of people (often an entire culture -- see #$CalendarSeasonTypeByCulture) as significantly intersecting the instances of #$SeasonOfYear to which those people are typically exposed.  For example, one specialization of #$CalendarSeason (#$CalendarWinter-US) is the collection of time intervals that people in mainstream U.S. culture consider to be co-temporal with the cold winter season (each of these intervals begins on the December solstice of a given year and ends on the Vernal equinox of that year).  For more on the difference between #$CalendarSeason and #$SeasonOfYear see the #$SharedNoteOnHemispheresAndCalendars.  Important specializations of #$CalendarSeason include #$CalendarWinter, #$CalendarSpring, #$CalendarSummer, and #$CalendarAutumn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa64a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa64a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
