x_comment(x_ResemblingTypeFn,"'(#$ResemblingTypeFn COLLECTION)' denotes the collection of things that resemble instances of COLLECTION.  Since everything resembles itself, the collection returned will be a generalization of the collection used in argument 1.  The returned collection represents the quality of 'being like', or 'resembling' a typical instance of COLLECTION (in some unspecified way).  For example (#$isa MyCalculator (#$ResemblingTypeFn #$Computer)) says that my calculator is 'computer-like' is some respect.  In English, one usually says things like 'Y is X-like' in order to convey that Y is not an X, or that one is uncertain whether Y is an X. However, this is a matter of implicature and not strict inference, so in Cyc all instances of X are such that they are, indeed, X-like.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa764).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa764,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa764,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
