x_comment(x_responsibleFor,"If (#$responsibleFor AGENT SIT) holds at time t, this means that, sometime prior to time t AGENT deliberately performed an action which was instrumental in bringing about SIT to the extent that, other things being equal, if the action had not been performed, SIT would not have come about.  This sense of 'responsibility' is stronger than causal responsibility--ie, it requires that AGENT play more than an unwitting causal role in bringing about SIT; however, it is probably weaker than full-blown moral responsibility, since even though AGENT intended to perform the action which brought about SIT, AGENT might not have intended to bring about SIT.  This is roughly the level of responsibility that applies, eg, to a case where somebody has killed a pedestrian by recklessly running a stop sign: the malefactor may not have intended to kill the pedestrian, but a deliberate decision of the malefactor's nevertheless was instrumental in causing the pedestrian's death.  It is a necessary condition for the stronger sense of responsibility aforementioned, and is probably a sufficient condition for the weaker sense of causal responsibility aforementioned.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa7b8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa7b8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa7b8,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
