x_comment('x_DogTypeByBreed-Pure',"A collection of collections, a specialization of #$DogTypeByBreed. Each #$DogTypeByBreed-Pure is a collection of dogs belong to a single pure breed, recognized conventionally. To be recognized as a pure breed, a group of dogs must be sufficiently similar in genetics and in comformation to an accepted breed standard that a mating of any two dogs belonging to the breed produces offspring who also conform to that standard.  In general, popular acceptance of a group of dogs as a #$DogTypeByBreed-Pure also depends on the recognition of the breed by some organization that has dog breeding and standards as its focus, such as the #$AmericanKennelClub. Except in unusually isolated environments, this type of genetic uniformity does not occur naturally in domestic dogs. Most instances of #$DogTypeByBreed-Pure are the result of intentional design and action by some #$HomoSapiens.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa81a).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa81a,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
