x_comment(x_Map,"A specialization of #$VisualArtifact-CW.  Each instance of #$Map is a visual conceptual work that represents a region of physical space.  Instances of #$Map represent features such as the following: geographical areas (#$GeographicalRegion), topographical features (#$TopographicalFeature), political regions (#$GeopoliticalEntity), climate zones (#$ClimateCycleType), human artifacts (#$ConstructionArtifact), population densities (#$populationDensity).  Maps are generally intended to help an agent to orient itself in space or to understand some aspect(s) of a large spatial area.  Instances of #$Map are physically instantiated in map copies (see the collection #$MapCopy), which may be on paper, in computerized geographical information systems, or in other forms.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa832).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa832,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa832,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
