x_comment(x_CalendarCoveringType,"A specialization of both #$TemporallyDisjointTemporalObjectType and #$TimeParameter (qq.v.), and a collection of collections of time intervals.  Each instance COVTYPE of #$CalendarCoveringType is a collection of #$TimeIntervals such that the temporally-ordered sequence of all of the instances of COVTYPE would completely cover all of time without any overlap.  Thus, #$CalendarHour is a #$CalendarCoveringType because all of time consists of a non-overlapping sequence of #$CalendarHours.  Similarly, #$CalendarWeek, #$CalendarDay, and #$GregorianMonth are calendar-covering types.  Conversely, #$Monday and #$December are _not_ calendar-covering types because time does not consist of an unbroken sequence of Mondays, or of Decembers.  Also note that a collection called (say) \"Week\" -- defined (unlike CalendarWeek) as the collection of _all_ seven-day-long periods of time (thus an instance of #$SameLengthTimeIntervalType) -- would _not_ be an instance of CalendarCoveringType since different Weeks of this sort overlap; e.g. the week beginning today, the week beginning yesterday, and the week beginning tomorrow all overlap.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa83d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa83d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa83d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
