x_comment(x_correspondingCycCollection,"(#$correspondingCycCollection SIT-PRED SIT-COLLECTION) means that there is a mapping from the #$SituationPredicate, SIT-PRED, to some specialization of the Cyc #$Collection, #$Situation. More specifically, if (#$correspondingCycCollection SIT-PRED SIT-COLLECTION) holds, then an assertion of the form (SIT-PRED . TERMS), if made in the context of a #$SituationSpecificationMicrotheory, entails the existence of an instance of of SIT-COLLECTION. (Please see #$SituationPredicate, #$EventPredicate and #$ActionPredicate for more information. If (SIT-PRED.TERMS) is asserted in a #$PlanSpecificationMicrotheory, it entails that some agents intends that there be an instance of SIT-COLLECTION.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa887).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa887,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
