x_comment(x_subSituationTypeGenls,"(#$subSituationTypeGenls SIT-TYPE1 SIT-TYPE2) means that some proper sub-situation type of SIT-TYPE1 (a specialization of #$Situation) stands in the #$genls relation to SIT-TYPE2.  For example, PhosphodiesterBonding is includes as sub-situation types several kinds of hydrolysis.  The latter can be accomplished with various kinds of molecules playing particular roles.  In the case of PhosphodiesterBonding, these roles are played by particular kinds of molecules. Hence those sub-situation types stand in the #$genls relation to hydrolysis, while PhosphodiesterBonding as a whole does not.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa8af).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa8af,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa8af,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa8af,24050).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa8af,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa8af,[]).
x_comment(x_someTypePlaysRoleInSituationType,"(#$someTypePlaysRoleInSituationType SIT-TYPE COL ROLE) means that a situation of type SIT-TYPE always involves  (as a result of some type of requirement) an instance of COL playing ROLE.  #$someTypePlaysRoleInSituationType is a variant of  the predicate #$requiresForRole with the first argument a subclass of, rather than an instance of, #$Situation. A salient assertion on  #$someTypePlaysRoleInSituationType allows Cyc to infer the instance-level version from the type-level version.  See also the more general predicate #$onlyTypePlaysRoleInSituationType.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa8b0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa8b0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa8b0,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa8b0,24051).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa8b0,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa8b0,[]).
x_comment(x_UnaryIntersectionFunction,"A #$FunctionType that is a specialization of both #$GenlsPreservingSubcollectionDenotingFunction and #$UnaryFunction (qq.v.). A #$UnaryIntersectionFunction takes a collection as its argument and always returns a subcollection of a given collection-as-argument as its corresponding value.  This value is in effect the \"intersection\" (see #$collectionIntersection) of the collection that is its argument with a collection specified in the function's definition (via #$intersectionType).  For example, where ANIMALTYPE is a type of #$Animal, (#$JuvenileFn ANIMALTYPE) is the collection of juvenile animals of ANIMALTYPE (i.e. the \"intersection\" of ANIMALTYPE and #$JuvenileAnimal).  Other instances of #$UnaryIntersectionFunction are #$FemaleFn, #$PureFn, and #$SolidFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa8b1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa8b1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa8b1,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa8b1,24052).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa8b1,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa8b1,[]).
x_comment('x_covers-Skinlike',"An instance of #$CoveragePredicate.  (#$covers-Skinlike SKIN OBJECT) means that SKIN forms all or part of OBJECT's outer surface, shell, or skin.  (#$covers-Skinlike SKIN OBJECT) does _not_ imply that SKIN is a part (see #$physicalDecompositions) of OBJECT, nor does it imply that SKIN is _not_ part of OBJECT.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa8b2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa8b2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa8b2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
