xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa8bf,[]).
x_comment(x_pathBetweenInSystem,"(#$pathBetweenInSystem PATH X Y SYS) means that PATH is a path in the system SYS, and X and Y are the end points (in the #$PathSystem) of PATH.  If PATH is a \"link\" of the system (see #$linkInSystem), (#$pathBetweenInSystem PATH X Y SYS) iff (#$linkBetweenInSystem PATH X Y SYS).  Note that there can be multiple paths in SYS between the same two points in SYS (which may or may not be \"nodes\" in SYS; see #$nodeInSystem).   See also #$pathBetween when no #$PathSystem is specified.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa8c0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa8c0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
