x_comment(x_surfaceParts,"An instance of #$PhysicalPartPredicate.  (#$surfaceParts BIG LITTLE) means that LITTLE is an external physical part (see #$externalParts) of a surface of BIG, or that LITTLE is a physical part of BIG itself, and a surface of LITTLE is part of a surface of BIG.  LITTLE is also something which 'does not go all the way through' BIG, in the sense that there is no line segment spatially subsumed by LITTLE that goes from a point at the surface of one side of BIG to a point of the surface on the opposite side of BIG. Positive examples: the skin of an orange is a #$surfaceParts of the orange, a window of a house is a #$surfaceParts of that house.  Borderline positive examples: the inside surface of a coffee cup is one of the #$surfaceParts of the cup; the inside surface of a beer-can in some contexts is a #$surfaceParts of the can.  Negative examples:  the brain is not a #$surfaceParts of a person.  A person's head is also a negative example of a #$surfaceParts.  There is a line that can go, for example, from the front side to the back side of that person.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa8f6).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa8f6,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
