x_comment('x_followingIntervalType-Cumulated',"(#$followingIntervalType-Cumulated Type-A Type-B TYPE n) means that there are n-1 instances Type-1, ..., Type-(n-1) of TYPE, none of which is the same as Type-A or Type-B (or any among themselves), such that (#$succeedingIntervalType Type-A Type-1), (#$succeedingIntervalType Type-1 Type-2), ..., (#$succeedingIntervalType Type-(n-2) Type-(n-1)), (#$succeedingIntervalType Type-(n-1) Type-B).  (See comment for #$succeedingIntervalType.)  For example, (#$succeedingIntervalType #$Monday #$Tuesday) and (#$succeedingIntervalType #$Tuesday #$Wednesday) are true, and all of #$Monday, #$Tuesday and #$Wednesday are different instances of #$DayOfWeekType, and therefore (#$followingIntervalType-Cumulated #$Monday #$Wednesday #$DayOfWeekType 2) is true.  Note that for each suitable arg3 to #$followingIntervalType-Cumulated, there is a maximal integer for its arg4.  For example, if the arg3 is #$DayOfWeekType, the maximal integer for the arg4 is 7, and if the arg3 is #$MonthOfYearType, the maximal integer for the arg4 is 12, etc.  Note also that this predicate is functional in its arg4 place.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa904).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa904,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa904,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa904,24139).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aa904,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa904,[]).
x_comment(x_positiveVestedInterest,"(#$positiveVestedInterest AGENT THING) means that the #$Agent-Generic AGENT has a positive interest in the #$TemporalThing THING.  If THING is an instance of #$SomethingExisting, then (#$positiveVestedInterest AGENT THING) will generally imply that AGENT has a positive interest in the preservation or flourishing of THING, and that AGENT will be adversely affected if THING is not preserved, or does not flourish.  If THING is an instance of #$Event, then (#$positiveVestedInterest AGENT THING) will generally imply that AGENT stands to benefit from the outcome of THING.  Note that the restriction of THING to #$TemporalThing means that it would be incorrect to use this predicate to say (e.g.) that Douglas Adams has a #$positiveVestedInterest in the number 42.  Rather, what he has a vested interest in is public popularity and faddism focusing on that number.  A fad is a #$TemporalThing, but the number 42 isn't.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa905).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa905,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa905,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
