x_comment(x_cotemporalSubEvents,"The predicate #$cotemporalSubEvents is used to relate an event to some sub-event which has the same duration as the whole event, but doesn't necessarily include everything that happens in the whole event.  (#$cotemporalSubEvents WHOLE PART) means that WHOLE and PART are cotemporal events (i.e., they have the same exact duration), and PART is a component of WHOLE.  For example, a particular instance of #$RainStormAsEvent may have distinguishable #$cotemporalSubEvents for (1) raining and (2) wind blowing, and an instance of swimming #$Backstroke has separable events for (1) kicking and (2) arm motion throughout the swimming.  See also #$cotemporal, #$subEvents.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa931).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa931,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aa931,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aa931,24197).
