xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aa931,[]).
x_comment('x_transferRouter-Generic',"This predicate can be used to indicate whatever acts as a router in an instance of #$GeneralizedTransfer and therefore plays an active and crucial role in it. (#$transferRouter-Generic TRANS THING) means that THING acts as a router in the #$GeneralizedTransfer TRANS.  For example, suppose a trip TRANS via airplane taking a person PER from New York to Austin makes a stop in #$CityOfOmahaNE, where PER changes flights.  If 'CityOfOmahaNEAirport-Org' is the instance of #$AirportOrganization running the airport located in the #$CityOfOmahaNE, then we can (probably) say that 'CityOfOmahaNEAirport-Org' is a router in the #$GeneralizedTransfer            TRANS of PER and represent this by (#$transferRouter-Generic TRANS 'CityOfOmahaNBAirport-Org').  See also #$transferRelay-Generic.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aa932).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aa932,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
