x_comment('x_culturePrescribes-Categorical',"(#$culturePrescribes-Categorical CULTURE ACTTYPE ROLE)    means that within CULTURE it is considered good or proper or    right to play ROLE in instances of ACTTYPE on a regular basis,   and bad or improper or wrong not to do so.  For example, some   cultures consider it proper to make an offering to a deity each day.     This does not entail, however, that CULTURE has a (hypothetical)    prescription for playing ROLE in instances of ACTTYPE with respect    to every possible condition; i.e. there might exist exceptional    situations in which playing ROLE in an ACTTYPE is not prescribed    (and might even be proscribed) by CULTURE.  One might be temporarily   exempted from the daily religious offering duty, for example, while    engaged in a protracted military battle.  This predicate applies    equally to moral rules, rules of conduct or etiquette, and customs.     See also #$culturePrescribes-Hypothetical,    #$cultureProscribes-Categorical, and #$cultureProscribes-Hypothetical.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaa0d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaa0d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaa0d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
