x_comment(x_caloricContentOfFood,"(#$caloricContentOfFood EDIBLESTUFF MASS CAL) means that MASS of EDIBLESTUFF, if burned, releases CAL of energy. CAL will generally be stated using the unit function #$Kilocalorie. For example, (#$caloricContent PeachPie001 (#$Gram 1) (#$Kilocalorie 7)) means that PeachPie001 has 7 Calories per gram. Unlike #$caloricContent, #$caloricContentOfFood allows qualitative values like (#$HighAmountFn #$EnergyQuantity) in addition to quantitative values like (#$Kilocalorie 400). A qualitative value indicates the substance's caloric content relative to some relevant specialization of #$EdibleStuff, but usually the collection #$EdibleStuff itself.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaa3b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaa3b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
