x_comment(x_AddingToSystemOfDevicesFn,"An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to denote the collection of           #$PurposefulActions in which some instance of a type of #$PhysicalDevice           is added to some instance of #$SystemOfDevices. (#$AddingToSystemOfDevicesFn SYS DEVTYPE) denotes the collection of #$Actions in which some instance of DEVTYPE is added to SYS so that it can work together with the other members of SYS.  Note that the #$resultGenls of this function includes #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. What kind of #$Actions this subcollection contains depends of course on what the type of #$SystemOfDevices SYS is. If, for instance, SYS consists of instances of #$RadioTransmitter and #$RadioReceiver, then the #$Actions that consist in adding to SYS may involve no more than placing an instance of #$RadioReceiver in an appropriate location and seeing to it that it is in working condition and can receive a proper range of frequencies. If SYS is an instance of #$TelephoneSystem, then the #$Actions that consist in adding to SYS will likely be much more involved: all the actions that go into hooking up a telephone.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaa54).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaa54,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaa54,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
