x_comment(x_helpfulProposition,"The predicate #$helpfulProposition is used to state a condition that, if true, would (normally) increase an agent's chances of success in a particular effort.  (#$helpfulProposition ENDEAVOR PROP DEGREE) means that if the #$ELSentence-Assertible PROP is true, then AGENT (who is referred to in PROP) will (normally) be helped in achieving the #$PurposefulAction ENDEAVOR.  DEGREE is a #$GenericValuePredicate giving an estimate of how helpful such an occurrence would be to the success of ENDEAVOR.   For example, in a basketball game, it's normally helpful if one or more of the team's players is alot taller than the average adult.  Thus, for any particular game, a #$veryHighAmountOf advantage is indicated if the following #$helpfulProposition (expressed in #$CycL) is true: (#$heightOfObject PLAYER-X (#$RelativeGenericValueFn #$heightOfObject #$BasketballPlayer #$veryHighAmountOf)). (Rohrbaugh, 3/1998)") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaacd).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaacd,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
