x_comment(x_credibilityToAgent,"(#$credibilityToAgent INFOTR AGT AMOUNT) means that the #$InformationTransferEvent INFOTR has a credibility, or believability, to the #$Agent-Generic AGT, of amount AMOUNT. So, for instance, (#$credibilityToAgent ReadingUSAToday001 Sue (#$VeryLowToLowAmountFn #$Credibility)) means that Sue finds what she is reading in #$USAToday-TheNewspaper in that particular instance fairly unconvincing, and (#$credibilityToAgent Threatening101 Bill (#$HighAmountFn #$Credibility)) means that Bill finds that particular #$MakingAThreat quite credible.  Note: to say that some agent is credible, write rules stating that any #$Communicating in which that agent is the #$senderOfInfo has a high credibility for whomever receives it. Similarly, to say that some #$InformationBearingThing is credible, say that any #$InformationTransferEvents in which it is the #$informationOrigin has a high credibility for the #$recipientOfInfo.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaada).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaada,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
