x_comment(x_BusinessAdvisor,"A collection of persons; a specialization of #$BusinessPerson.  Each instance of #$BusinessAdvisor provides advice to individuals or businesses about specific areas of interest.  #$BusinessAdvisors are very similar to #$Consultants, but differ from them in that #$BusinessAdvisors will frequently work with individuals rather than organizations.  Additionally, business advisors are generally more focused on the client's interests, while a consultant may just be asked to give their views on a certain topic, without knowing many details of the client's relationship to the topic.  Finally, an advisor (a non-professional advisor) need not be an expert in the field in which they are giving advice--it merely matters that the advisor be a trusted individual.  For example, a person's friend might be an advisor on financial affairs without knowing very much about finances, but a consultant would be expected to have significant knowledge of financial affairs.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaaf7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaaf7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaaf7,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaaf7,24732).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaaf7,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaaf7,[]).
x_comment('x_Disapproving-CommunicationAct',"A specialization of #$Informing. In each instance of #$Disapproving-CommunicationAct, an #$IntelligentAgent communicates disapproval of something.  Instances of #$Disapproving-CommunicationAct are usually accompanied by feelings of #$Disapproval. For situations in which what the agent disapproves of can be expressed in propositional form, see #$disapprovedStatement. It is also worth noting that instances of #$Disapproving-CommunicationAct differ from instances of #$Rejecting-CommunicationAct, in that the former are expressed judgments that a certain action or opinion is inappropriate, morally wrong, etc., while the latter involve the denial of the propositional content of some communication.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaaf8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaaf8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaaf8,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
