x_comment(x_BorderFn,"<code>(#$BorderFn OBJECT)</code> denotes the entire border <code>BORDER</code> of <code>OBJECT</code>.  If <code>OBJECT</code> is two-dimensional <code>BORDER</code> is one-dimensional (e.g. a linear curve or perimeter), while if <code>OBJECT</code> is three-dimensional <code>BORDER</code> is two-dimensional (i.e. a surface).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad03).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad03,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aad03,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
