x_comment('x_causes-SitTypeSitType',"<code>(#$causes-SitTypeSitType CAUSE EFFECT)</code> means that each instance of #$Situation <code>CAUSE</code> is normally a cause of an instance of #$Situation <code>EFFECT</code>.  Often <code>EFFECT</code> is a specialization of #$Event and <code>CAUSE</code> is a specialization of #$Event or #$Action.  The occurrence of an instance of <code>CAUSE</code> is typically associated with the occurrence of an instance of <code>EFFECT</code>.  However, this association is not necessarily iron-clad, and may depend on certain prerequisites, or may be defeated by the occurrence of other events or situations. Cf. #$preconditionFor-SitTypeSitType, which is not a generalization of this relation, and #$fosters-SitTypeSitType, which is.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad14).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad14,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
