x_comment(x_ImitationOfCollectionFn,"<code>(#$ImitationOfCollectionFn ORIGINAL-COLLECTION)</code> returns a collection that is an instance of #$ImitationOfCollection.  Instances of the instance of #$ImitationOfCollection returned by <code>(#$ImitationOfCollectionFn ORIGINAL-COLLECTION)</code> are designed by someone to seem as though they are instances of the collection            <code>ORIGINAL-COLLECTION</code>. \n<p>\nFor example, (#$ImitationOfCollectionFn #$EdibleFruit) is the instance of #$ImitationOfCollection whose instances are only every imitation edible fruit.  \n<p>\nNote that the collection returned by <code>(#$ImitationOfCollectionFn ORIGINAL-COLLECTION)</code> <i>will not</i> itself be a specialization of the collection <code>ORIGINAL-COLLECTION</code>.  Compare this function to #$ImitationOfIndividualFn.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad1c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad1c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
