x_comment('x_GoldenRatio-Number',"#$GoldenRatio-Number is the mathematical constant which represents the Golden Ratio and is defined to be (#$QuotientFn (#$PlusFn 1 (#$SquareRootFn 5)) 2).  The Golden Ratio has many surprising and curious mathematical properties.  It is also sometimes called the 'Divine Proportion', and has been extensively used in architecture because objects in this proportion tend to be visually appealing.  Although #$GoldenRatio-Number is an instance of #$IrrationalNumber, a reasonable rational approximation is 1.6180340") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad47).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad47,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
