x_comment(x_slotsAdditive,"(#$slotsAdditive SUM-SLOT ADD-SLOT) expresses the following relationship between two #$QuantitySlots: the value of SUM-SLOT applied to OBJ is (by definition or convention) the sum of OBJ's value on ADD-SLOT plus zero or more other values.  For example, it is true that (#$slotsAdditive #$financialAssetsOfAgent #$cashAssetsOfAgent), because the value of an agent's financial assets is the sum of the value of her cash assets plus other values (e.g., of her stock holdings, securities, etc.).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad80).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad80,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aad80,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aad80,26783).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aad80,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aad80,[]).
x_comment(x_initialLoanAmount,"(#$initialLoanAmount LOAN AMOUNT) means that the inital amount borrowed at the origination of LOAN is AMOUNT.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad81).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad81,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aad81,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aad81,26784).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aad81,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aad81,[]).
x_comment(x_basicPrice,"<code>(#$basicPrice OBJECT MONEY)</code> means that to buy the #$TemporalThing <code>OBJECT</code> one needs to pay the #$MonetaryValue <code>MONEY</code>, where <code>MONEY</code> can be either a discrete quantity or an interval.  #$basicPrice should be distinguished from the (rather different) predicates #$appraisedValue and #$cost (qq.v). For the price at which an item was bought some time in the past, see #$bookValue. For the total charge for purchase of an object, including tax, shipping, handling, etc., see #$totalCharge. For relating #$Buying events to the basic price of items bought during those events, see #$basicPrice-Event. Since prices are time-sensitive, assertions about #$basicPrice should be suitably qualified.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad82).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad82,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aad82,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aad82,26785).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aad82,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aad82,[]).
x_comment(x_cost,"<code>(#$cost OBJECT MONEY)</code> means that the #$TemporalThing <code>OBJECT</code> has a cost in #$MonetaryValue of <code>MONEY</code>. Note that this amount can be a discrete quantity or an interval.  This concept is subtly different from (and considerably more complex than) that of #$basicPrice, which denotes the amount of money requested for an item which is for sale. For instance, the price of an airconditioning unit might be $200 while its #$cost (over a lifetime of repairs, and to the environment, if it is environmentally destructive) might be considerably higher. See also the ternary predicate #$costTo.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad83).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad83,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aad83,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aad83,26786).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aad83,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aad83,[]).
x_comment(x_CreditScoring,"A specialization of both #$FinancialActivity and #$Evaluating.  Each instance of #$CreditScoring is a standarized act of evaluating an agent's #$CreditWorthiness (q.v.).  Credit scoring is typically done by a bank, credit card company, or similar financial organization, whenever a person applies for a credit card, personal loan, or mortgage.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad84).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad84,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aad84,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aad84,26787).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aad84,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aad84,[]).
x_comment(x_FinancialCompany,"#$FinancialCompany is a specialization of #$PrivateSectorOrganization, #$FinancialOrganization, and #$CommercialServiceOrganization.  Each instance of #$FinancialCompany is a business engaged in financial activities as its main concern.  An instance of #$FinancialCompany is a commercial service organization that buys, sells, trades, converts, or lends money, in the form of currency or negotiable financial instruments (such as stocks, bonds, commodities futures, etc.), as (one of) its major function(s).  The collection #$FinancialCompany does not include businesses, such as retailers, which simply exchange goods or non-financial services for money.  Examples: Chase Bank, University Federal Credit Union, Fidelity Investments (but NOT the IMF). Cf. the supercollection #$FinancialOrganization for non-business organizations engaged in financial activities (such as the IMF).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad85).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad85,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aad85,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
