x_comment(x_EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityFn,"(#$EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityFn ACTIVITY) denotes the collection of equipment types whose elements are used in performances of ACTIVITY [a #$DevisedStructuredActivity].  There are two sufficient conditions for a given collection being a subset of this collection.  One such condition applies to device collections whose major, predominant, or primary function is to play the role of #$deviceUsed in performances of ACTIVITY (see #$primaryFunction).  Another such condition applies to device collections which are always used in performances of ACTIVITY (see #$eventTypeUsesDeviceType).  For example, (#$EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityFn #$Baseball-TheGame) denotes ``baseball equipment''.  Thus, because #$BaseballBat and #$BaseballMitt have #$BaseballGame as one of their main functions, Cyc should infer that these two device types are instances of (#$EquipmentTypeForStructuredActivityFn #$Baseball-TheGame).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad98).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad98,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
