x_comment(x_TransitiveInfinitivePhraseNPGapFrame,"This frame is used for transitive adjectives that take an infinitival complement that has a gap in one position, i.e. it is for 'tough'-class adjectives.  In HPSG terms: [COMPS <CP[Infinitive]/NP>].  Can be used with or without a 'for NP' at the beginning of the infinitival.  Examples: 'The movie was exciting to see __', 'The game was tough for the team to win __'.  Note that all adjectives in #$TransitiveInfinitivePhraseNPGapFrame can also be used in the #$PleonasticInfinitivePhraseFrameType.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aad9f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aad9f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
