xc_kb_names(a65b16526aad9f,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aad9f,[]).
x_comment(x_PleonasticThatClauseFrame," This frame is used for transitive words (usually verbs or adjectives) that take an expletive 'it' subject and exactly one complement which is a that-clause, but can not take a that-clause as a subject. In HPSG terms: [SUBJ <NP[it]>], [COMPS <S[that]>. Example: 'it seems that he left', 'it appears that the candidate wins the election next year', but not *'that he left seems'. 'it is likely that John and Mary will get along', 'it is nice that Fred invited us' do not have this frame, since they can also be used with a clausal subject as in 'That Fred invited us to the party is nice'. Use #$ClausalSubjectTransitiveNPFrame for those cases.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aada0).
