x_comment('x_EventPredicate-FrameTemplate',"A special type of #$EventPredicate (q.v.). Instances of this collection are `template predicates' that can be used with any event type, i.e. spec of #$Event. Think of them as #$ActionPredicates that are not specific to a particular action type: the action type is specified explicitly in each assertion by entering it as the first argument of an #$EventPredicate-FrameTemplate. A template predicate takes as arguments exactly one event type and a fixed (though arbitrary) number of individuals: the resulting gaf expresses the relation existing between these individuals when they play specific roles in events of type TYPE. For instance, in place of (#$cleans SUBJ OBJ) we would use (#$doesTo #$Cleaning SUBJ OBJ): the latter is logically equivalent to the former. Typically, each argument (except the first) of an event-predicate template corresponds to the `participant role' expressed in Davidsonian representation by an #$ActorSlot: in the example above, SUBJ corresponds to the filler of a #$doneBy clause, and OBJ to the filler of an #$objectActedOn. However, this correspondence is not a definitional requirement: as in the case of other action predicates, one can define event-predicate templates that don't have an obvious correspondence to actor slots, although this practice is discouraged. Like  #$NonDavidsonianPredFn (q.v.), event-predicate templates abstract from any particular event types. Unlike that function, however, and like #$EventPredicates of the ordinary kind, each event-predicate template encodes a particular combination of #$ActorSlots or #$Roles in its argument structure.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaded).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaded,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaded,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaded,27019).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaded,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaded,[]).
x_comment(x_does,"The simplest event-predicate template: it expresses the fact that the filler of the 2nd argument place is engaged as the agent or performer in activitity of the type denoted by the first argument. A more precise meaning is determined by the temporal qualification parameters of the microtheory in which a #$does GAF is asserted. Example: (#$does #$Running #$PeterWagner) is true at time T with parameter #$CalendarSecond iff Peter runs at T and also at every sub-interval of T that is no smaller than a #$CalendarSecond -- which means <i>any</i> sub-interval of T. So the meaning of this assertion would be close to the English phrase 'Peter <i>is running</i>'. See also #$hasDone.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aadee).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aadee,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aadee,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aadee,27020).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aadee,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aadee,[]).
x_comment(x_doesWith,"This event-predicate template expresses the relation between the\nagent (active participant) and the tool or device s/he uses in an\nactivity. Example: (#$thereExists ?X (#$and (#$isa ?X #$Feather)\n(#$doesWith #$WritingACheck #$Klein ?X)))  is true iff\nCharles Klein writes (or: is writing) a check using a feather.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aadef).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aadef,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aadef,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aadef,27021).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aadef,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aadef,[]).
x_comment(x_doesToAtLocation,"This event-predicate template expresses the relation between the\nagent (active participant), the object (passive participant) and the\nlocation of an activity. Example: (#$doesToAtLocation #$Teaching #$AlonzoChurch #$StephenCKleene\n#$PrincetonUniversity) means that Alonzo Church teaches (or: is teaching) to\nStephen Kleene at Princeton University (something that was actually true at\nsome time in the 1930s).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aadf0).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aadf0,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aadf0,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aadf0,27026).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aadf0,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aadf0,[]).
x_comment(x_doesToWithAtLocation,"This event-predicate template expresses the relation between the agent (active participant), the object (passive participant), the device and the location of an activity. Example: (#$doesToWithAtLocation #$WritingByHand #$Klein DOCUMENT FEATHER #$CycorpHeadquarters) is true iff Charles Klein writes (or: is writing) DOCUMENT with device FEATHER at Cycorp's main offices.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aadf1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aadf1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aadf1,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aadf1,27032).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aadf1,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aadf1,[]).
x_comment(x_associateSlotInArg,"(#$associateSlotInArg EPFT-PRED SLOT N) means that SLOT is\n\nthe #$ActorSlot predicate conceptually associated with the N-th argument place of\n\nEPFT-PRED, in the following sense: Suppose (EPFT-PRED COLL ARG_1 ... ARG_N ...)\n\nis true. Then, were one to represent the same fact within the Davidsonian\n\nframework, i.e., by asserting the existence of a particular event of type\n\nCOLL, ARG_N would play in the event the role expressed by SLOT.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aadf2).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aadf2,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aadf2,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aadf2,27033).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aadf2,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aadf2,[]).
x_comment(x_coordinateSlot,"For any N greater than or equal to 2, (#$coordinateSlot PRED1\nPRED2 N) is true iff both (#$associateSlotInArg PRED1 SLOT N) and\n(#$associateSlotInArg PRED2 SLOT N).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aadf3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aadf3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aadf3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aadf3,27044).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aadf3,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aadf3,[]).
x_comment('x_movingToFrom-EPFT',"This event-predicate template expresses the relation between the\n\nobject in motion, the point of departure and the point of arrival in\n\ntypes of activity subsumed by #$Movement-TranslationEvent. Example:\n\n(#$movingToFrom-EPFT (#$TransportViaFn #$AirTransportationDevice) OBJECT \n\nLOC-TO LOC-FROM) is true iff OBJECT is (being) transported by air from place LOC-FROM\n\nto place LOC-TO. It is not implied that OBJECT has either a passive or\n\nactive role in the motion, or that it need be a separate object from the\n\n#$conveyor-Generic used.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aadf4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aadf4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aadf4,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aadf4,27047).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aadf4,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aadf4,[]).
x_comment('x_transportedToFrom-EPFT',"This event-predicate template expresses the relation between the\n\nobject transported, the point of departure and the point of arrival in\n\ntypes of activity subsumed by #$TransportationEvent. Example:\n\n(#$transportedToFrom-EPFT (#$TransportViaFn #$AirTransportationDevice) THING\n\nLOC-TO LOC-FROM) is true iff THING is (being) transported by air from place LOC-FROM\n\nto place LOC-TO. The #$associateSlotInArg condition for arg2 implies that\n\nTHING is distinct from the conveyor of transportation -- the package on the plane,\n\ne.g. or the pilot, but not the plane itself.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aadf5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aadf5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aadf5,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aadf5,27062).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aadf5,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aadf5,[]).
x_comment(x_decontextualizedCollection,"(#$decontextualizedCollection COL) states that COL is a collection in which membership is context-independent.  In effect, any instance of COL is an instance of COL in every microtheory.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aadf6).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aadf6,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
