x_comment(x_syndromeOfInfection,"(#$syndromeOfInfection SYN-TYPE INF-TYPE) means that #$Infections of type INF-TYPE are often associated with #$BIOS-SurveillanceSyndromeType SYN-TYPE. If someone has both an instance of INF-TYPE and an instance of SYN-TYPE, then it is likely that the infection caused the syndrome. Thus, the presence of an instance of #$BIOS-SurveillanceSyndromeType SYN-TYPE is a useful predictor of the presence of an instance of the #$Infection INF-TYPE. However, since #$SurveillanceSyndromes are defined quite broadly, they are indicators of only very general types of #$Infections. Diagnosis of an instance of INF-TYPE usually requires more information than provided by observation of symptoms. For example, confirmed diagnoses require laboratory tests to identify the pathogen responsible for the infection. Thus the rapidity of syndromic surveillance is offset by its lack of precision.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aae27).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aae27,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
