x_comment('x_BIOS-EpidemicHypothesisMt',"A collection of #$HypotheticalContexts. Each instance represents a hypothesis about the nature of a putative #$Epidemic. The non-derived assertions made in a #$BIOS-EpidemicHypothesisMt form the content of a hypothesis about the epidemic being investigated. These hypotheses will be generated initially in response to an alert generated by the Essence II Biosurveillance alerting system. These assertions can then be examined and made the starting point for inference without carrying the implicature that they are true outside the context of the hypothesis. Each hypothesis when fully developed will contain assertions about the type of infection constituting the epidemic, where and when exposure to the pathogen causing the outbreak occurred, what population is at risk for infection, and whether the outbreak was accidental or the result of a deliberate attack. Facts about the situation that are relevant to the truth of a hypothesis but are not themselves hypothetical should NOT be placed in an instance of #$BIOS-EpidemicHypothesisMt. Rather, they should be placed in a #$Microtheory visible from the relevant #$BIOS-EpidemicHypothesisMts.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aae35).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aae35,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
