x_comment(x_ExposureToPathogen,"The collection of #$ExposureToHarmfulSubstance events in which an instance of #$Organism-Whole is in proximity to and/or has contact with an instance of #$Microorganism in such a manner that effective transmission of the pathogen to the #$Organism-Whole is possible. If such transmission does occur and the #$Organism-Whole is susceptible to #$Infections caused by that #$Microorganism, the transmission is likely to result in #$Infection in the #$organismExposed. Thus, whether an instance of #$ExposureToSubstance is also an instance of #$ExposureToPathogen depends on the type of #$Microorganism and the possible means by which it can infect a susceptible host. For example, contact with a person suffering from #$InhalationalAnthrax would not be an instance of #$ExposureToPathogen because #$Anthrax-Bacterium cannot be transmitted by close contact with infected hosts. On the other hand, contact with a person suffering from #$SmallpoxInfection would be an instance of #$ExposureToPathogen because #$Smallpox-Virus can be transmitted effectively by close contact with an infected host.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aae3d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aae3d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aae3d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aae3d,27206).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aae3d,[]).
