x_comment(x_SolsticeDay,"A specialization of #$CalendarDay and an instance of #$AnnualTemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$SolsticeDay is a calendar day during which the sun is at its greatest distance from the celestial equator.  One solstice occurs annually about June 21 (see #$JuneSolsticeDay) when the sun is at the zenith at the tropic of Cancer -- in the northern hemisphere such a solstice would be an instance of #$SummerSolsticeDay, and in the southern hemisphere it would be an instance of #$WinterSolsticeDay. The other solstice occurs annually about  December 21 (see #$DecemberSolsticeDay) when the sun is at the zenith at the tropic of Capricorn -- in the northern hemisphere such a solstice would be an instance of #$WinterSolsticeDay, and in the southern hemisphere it would be an instance of #$SummerSolsticeDay.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aae53).
