x_comment(x_CompleteDiseaseSituationTypeFn,"(#$CompleteDiseaseSituationTypetFn DIS-TYPE) denotes the type of #$Situation for the #$DiseaseType DIS-TYPE. This function is needed because #$DiseaseTypes are instances of #$TemporalStuffType whereas the course of a #$DiseaseType from its onset to death or recovery should be an instance of #$TemporalObjectType. That is, any time slice of an instance of DIS-TYPE will still be an instance of DIS-TYPE, whereas any time slice of an instance of the course of the disease DIS-TYPE from its onset to its end will not be an instance of the complete course of the disease. Since we anticipate developing scripts for the courses of various #$DiseaseTypes, this function will prove useful. The result of this function represents the course of a #$DiseaseType if left untreated and to which the person undergoing it has no immunity. Other functions might be needed if we want to represent the course of a #$DiseaseType when either or both of these conditions are not met.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aae92).
