x_comment(x_substituteArgIn,"A predicate that relates an integer (representing an argument-position) and a CycL term to a CycL formula in which the term appears (in that position) and a second CycL formula in which has identical arguments to the first in every argument position save the one represented by the integer; #$substituteArgIn is a #$QuaternaryPredicate that relates an instance of #$NonNegativeInteger to an instance of #$CycLTerm and two instances of #$CycLFormula.  \n<p>\n<code>(#$substituteArgIn N TERM FORMULA-OLD FORMULA-NEW)</code> means that TERM occurs as argument N within FORMULA-NEW and that otherwise FORMULA-OLD and FORMULA-NEW have identical arguments.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaec3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaec3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaec3,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaec3,27360).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaec3,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaec3,[]).
x_comment(x_expansionExceptWhen,"A #$BinaryPredicate that relates one instance of #$CycLFormula to another.  (#$expansionExceptWhen EXCEPTION RMP-GAF) means that an exception to the #$expansion rule asserted for the #$RuleMacroPredicate in the arg0 slot of RMP-GAF is EXCEPTION.  Any free variables that occur in EXCEPTION should be understood as occuring in the same quantificational context as the #$expansion of the predicate that occurs as the 0th argument to RMP-GAF. Thus,   (#$expansionExceptWhen (#$and (#$genls ?TERM #$FlightlessBird) (#$equals ?SENT  (#$typeBehaviorCapable #$Bird #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy)))(#$transitiveViaArgInverse #$typeBehaviorCapable #$genls 1) means that (#$genls ?TERM #$FlightlessBird) (#$equals ?SENT  (#$typeBehaviorCapable #$Bird #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy) is an exception to the #$expansion for #$transitiveViaArgInverse, which is:  (#$expansion #$transitiveViaArgInverse (#$implies (#$and  (#$knownSentence ?SENT) (#$argN :ARG1 0 ?SENT) (:ARG2 ?TERM ?ARG)  (#$argN ?ARG :ARG3 ?SENT)(#$substituteArgIn :ARG3 ?TERM ?SENT  ?NEWSENT)) (#$trueSentence ?NEWSENT))).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaec4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaec4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaec4,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaec4,27363).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaec4,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaec4,[]).
x_comment(x_transitiveViaArgInverseExceptions,"A #$QuintaryPredicate used to state exceptions to the applicabilty of #$transitiveViaArgInverse assertions. (#$transitiveViaArgInverseExceptions THING FORMULA PRED BINPRED N) means that the Nth argument position of PRED is \"transitive\" with respect to the inverse of BINPRED except when THING (or a constant that stands in the inverse of BINPRED to THING) occurs as the Nth argument to PRED in a GAF whose arguments are otherwise identical to those of FORMULA.  For example, (#$transitiveViaArgInverseExceptions #$FlightlessBird (#$typeBehaviorCapable #$Bird #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy) #$typeBehaviorCapable #$genls 1) means that (#$typeBehaviorCapable COLL #$Flying-FlappingWings #$doneBy) is true for all specializations of COLL except for those specializations of COLL that are also specializations of #$FlightlessBird.  See also #$transitiveViaArgExceptions.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaec5).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaec5,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaec5,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaec5,27364).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaec5,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaec5,[]).
x_comment('x_BIOS-InitialAlertReportMicrotheory',"A collection of #$BIOS-AlertReportMicrotheorys. Each instance is an initial alert issued by the Essence II Biosurveillance System. An initial alert is the initial member of a series of alerts, each successive alert updating the temporally prior one. Upon receiving an alert, the hypothesis manager determines whether it is an initial alert. If it is, the hypothesis manager creates (1) an instance of #$BIOS-InitialAlertReportMicrotheory, (2) an instance of #$PhysicalEvent as the actual object of the alert (see #$bios-AlertReportObject), (3) an instance of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic as the hypothesized epidemic of the initial alert (see #$bios-AlertReportHypothesizedEpidemic), and (4) several hypotheses (see #$BIOS-EpidemicHypothesisMt) about the type of infection, and place and date of exposure. Both the hypothesized epidemic and the hypotheses will be linked to the initial alert (see #$bios-MicrotheoryInitializedBy). Thus the initial alert will enable the hypothesis manager to know which alerts and hypotheses pertain to the same hypothesized epidemic. Our initial assumption is that if an alert is issued more than 31 days after the most recent alert, then it is an initial alert and triggers a new epidemiological investigation.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaec6).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaec6,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaec6,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaec6,27365).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaec6,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaec6,[]).
x_comment('x_BIOS-InitializableMicrotheory',"A collection of #$BIOS-Microtheorys. Each instance is capable of standing in the #$bios-MicrotheoryInitializedBy relation to one and only one instance of #$BIOS-InitialAlertReportMicrotheory. All and only those #$BIOS-InitializableMicrotheorys that are created as part of the same epidemiological investigation of an initial alert are initialized by that alert. Some of the important specializations of this collection include #$BIOS-AlertReportMicrotheory, #$BIOS-EpidemicHypothesisMt, #$BIOS-HypothesisGenerationVocabularyMt, and #$BIOS-HypothesisGenerationMt. Some negative examples are #$BIOS-BackgroundVocabularyMt and #$BIOS-BackgroundMt.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaec7).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaec7,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaec7,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaec7,27366).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaec7,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaec7,[]).
x_comment('x_bios-MicrotheoryInitializedBy',"(#$bios-MicrotheoryInitializedBy MT INIT) means that the #$BIOS-InitializableMicrotheory MT is initialized by the #$BIOS-InitialAlertReportMicrotheory INIT. The initialization relationship provides a convenient way to track which #$BIOS-InitializableMicrotheorys are part of the same epidemiological investigation. A new investigation begins when the hypothesis manager determines that an alert is separated enough temporally from earlier alerts to warrant a new investigation. It then creates a #$BIOS-InitialAlertReportMicrotheory. Whenever the hypothesis manager creates a new microtheory as part of this investigation it asserts that #$bios-MicrotheoryInitializedBy holds between the new microtheoory and the #$BIOS-InitialAlertReportMicrotheory that started the investigation. See #$BIOS-InitializableMicrotheory for further information about the kinds of microtheories created by the hypothesis manager.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaec8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaec8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaec8,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaec8,27367).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaec8,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaec8,[]).
x_comment('x_bios-AlertReportInitializedBy',"(#$bios-AlertReportInitializedBy ALERT INIT) means that the #$BIOS-AlertReportMicrotheory ALERT is initialized by the #$BIOS-InitialAlertReportMicrotheory INIT.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaec9).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaec9,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
