x_comment('x_bios-AlertReportObject',"(#$bios-AlertReportObject ALERT EVENT) means that the #$PhysicalEvent EVENT is the object of the #$BIOS-AlertReportMicrotheory ALERT. The object of the alert is the #$PhysicalEvent that is the underlying distal cause of the indicators that trigger the alert. The alerting algorithm of the Essence II biosurveillance system is designed to detect instances of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics. However, there will be situations where the alert is a false alarm (false positive). In these cases, there will still be some event or group of events that trigger the alert (for example, school absenteeism due to severe weather). When an instance of #$BIOS-InitialAlertReportMicrotheory is created by the hypothesis manager, an instance of #$PhysicalEvent will be created that is the object of that alert. All subsequent alerts that update the initial alert will have the same object. (See #$bios-AlertReportHypothesizedEpidemic.) ") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaeca).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaeca,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaeca,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaeca,27369).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaeca,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaeca,[]).
x_comment('x_bios-AlertReportHypothesizedEpidemic',"(#$bios-AlertReportHypothesizedEpidemic ALERT EPI) means that the #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic EPI is hypothesized as the object of the #$BIOS-AlertReportMicrotheory ALERT. EPI is hypothesized as the underlying distal cause of the indicators that trigger the alert. If the alert turns out to be real (a true positive) then the hypothesized epidemic will also be the actual object of the alert (see #$bios-AlertReportObject).  If the alert turns out to be a false alarm (false positive), then the hypothesized epidemic exists only in the context of the alert. There will still be an existing object of the alert, but it won't be an instance of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic. When an instance of #$BIOS-InitialAlertReportMicrotheory is created by the hypothesis manager, an instance of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic will be created that will be the hypothesized epidemic of the alert. All subsequent alerts that update the initial alert will have the same epidemic as their hypothesized object.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaecb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaecb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaecb,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaecb,27370).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaecb,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaecb,[]).
x_comment('x_BIOS-HypothesisGenerationMt',"A collection of #$HypotheticalContexts. Each instance is a #$BIOS-Microtheory that is uniquely linked to an initial alert generated by the Essence II Biosurveillance System (see #$BIOS-InitialAlertReportMicrotheory). Each instance is the #$HypotheticalContext that holds the assertions that will be distributed by the hypothesis manager to form the content of the hypotheses (see #$BIOS-EpidemicHypothesisMt) generated in response to an initial alert. Thus an instance may contain a pair of mutually incompatible assertions in situations where two incompatible hypotheses will be constructed-- each hypothesis having one of the two assertions as its content.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaecc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaecc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaecc,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaecc,27371).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaecc,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaecc,[]).
x_comment('x_BIOS-HypothesisGenerationVocabularyMt',"A collection of #$VocabularyMicrotheorys. Each instance is uniquely linked to an initial alert generated by the Essence II Biosurveillance System (see #$BIOS-InitialAlertReportMicrotheory) and is the #$VocabularyMicrotheory for that instance of #$BIOS-HypothesisGenerationMt initialized by the same initial alert.. The hypothetical objects of an initial alert (see #$bios-AlertReportObject and #$bios-AlertReportHypothesizedEpidemic) are defined in an instance of #$BIOS-HypothesisGenerationVocabularyMt because they may have no objective reality outside the context of the various hypotheses about the alert (see #$BIOS-EpidemicHypothesisMt).") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaecd).
