x_comment(x_situationIsSuchThat,"A binary predicate used to relate a #$Situation to sentences that are true because of (or: made true by) the situation. We can think of #$Situations, in this light, as the states of affairs or `parts' of the world that are the truth-makers of sentences. For example, (#$situationIsSuchThat MeetingInTheOvalOfficeOnJune12 (#$postureOfAnimal #$BillClinton #$SittingPosture)) allows us to characterize the state of affairs in the Oval Office on June 12 as a particular situation that `includes' the state of affairs  that Bill Clinton  is sitting.  This is not the same as #$holdsIn, at least given the intended meaning of #$holdsIn. For one thing, it doesn't presuppose that situations must have temporal extent throughout which something holds.  Note that if (#$situationIsSuchThat SIT P) and P entails Q, then (#$situationIsSuchThat SIT Q).  So, any situation in which Clinton is sitting in the Oval Office is a situation in which an #$Individual is sitting in the Oval Office.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaf01).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaf01,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaf01,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
