x_comment(x_CoalitionInformationDesignation,"A subcollection of #$InformationDesignation.  Instances of this\ncollection are attributes of information.  Specifically, they are designations or classifications\nof information created by coalitions between governments.  For instance, if the US formed a coalition with\nIsrael for operations in the middle east, they might designate the information accessible by only those members of \nthe coalition. The designations in this scheme would be instances of #$CoalitionInformationDesignation.  The scheme might borrow\nfrom the US governments preexisting method of classifying information, but could include novel names to prevent confusion\nor misapplication of the scope of information accessible by the coalition members:  for instance, 'US-IsraelSecret' might \nreplace the usual 'Secret' classification used by the US government because it refers to distinct information sources,\nbut it could still preserve the meaning of the term 'secret' as understood by the US government.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaf73).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaf73,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaf73,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaf73,27677).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaf73,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaf73,[]).
x_comment('x_CoalitionClassification-US',"A subcollection of #$CoalitionInformationDesignation.\nInstances of this collection are attributes.  Specifically, they are the attributes \n#$CoalitionClassificationUS-TopSecret, #$CoalitionClassificationUS-Secret, or \n#$CoalitionClassificationUS-Confidential.  These attributes are similar to the attributes in the collection\n#$ClassificationUS (#$TopSecretInformation, #$SecretInformation, and #$ConfidentialInformation), but differ\nin that they are applied only to information that is classified and accessible by a\nselected members of those governments that comprise an active\ncoalition formed with the US.  Instances of this collection will not be applied \nto the same information that gets classified by\nthe US government, but rather to the sum of information that is\nused, valued and deemed in need of protection by members of the coalition, although there may indeed be overlap.\nHence, at least some of the information classified using an instance of the collection #$Classification-US will not\nbe classified by using an instance of the collection #$CoalitionClassication-US, and likewise \nsome of the information that gets classified using an instance of the collection #$CoalitionClassification-US will\nnot be classified using an instance of the collection \n#$Classification-US.  Note, however,\nthat instances of both collections will\nshare the US government's classification\nscheme--'Confidential', 'Secret', and\n'TopSecret'.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaf74).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaf74,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaf74,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaf74,27686).
