x_comment(x_MicrotheoryTypeByAnthropacity,"#$MicrotheoryTypeByAnthropacity is a class of #$AttributeValues which are used to organize the #$Microtheory structure in Cyc.  If a microtheory has a very general #$MicrotheoryTypeByAnthropacity value, it assumes less about the existence of a physical universe, living things, and so on. Microtheories which have more specific, detailed, or `dense' #$MicrotheoryTypeByAnthropacity values are assumed to be `about' civilized people living on Earth.  Relative generality (specificity) is indicated by the predicate #$genlAttributes.  (#$genlAttributes ATTRIBUTE-1 ATTRIBUTE-2) means that in a nested hierarchy of values including ATTRIBUTE-1 and ATTRIBUTE-2, ATTRIBUTE-2 is more general than ATTRIBUTE-1.  If a particulary microtheory has an anthropacity of ATTRIBUTE-1, this entails that it also has a (more general) anthropacity of ATTRIBUTE-2.  See also #$mtAnthropacity.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaf9d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaf9d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaf9d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaf9d,27760).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaf9d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaf9d,[]).
x_comment(x_AssertionConclusionType,"Consider an axiom of the form (P -> Q). \n\nIf P is true, we might want the system to go ahead and conclude Q. \n\nOn the other hand, we might want it just to verify that Q is true and \n\ncomplain if it is not. If later Q is retracted, we might want the system \n\nto immediately complain, or to detect this at its leisure. \n\nAll this is indicated by placing instances of the collection\n\n#$AssertionConclusionType as the arg2 of\n\nthe predicate #$assertionConclusionActionType, with the rule\n\nin question being the arg1. See the comments on the instances of the \n\ncollection #$AssertionConclusionType for further details.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaf9e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaf9e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aaf9e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526aaf9e,27761).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526aaf9e,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526aaf9e,[]).
x_comment(x_NarrativeModeType,"A collection of collections.  Instances of #$NarrativeModeType are collections of instances of #$CWInstantiating that are   \n instantiated in a certain mode.  These collections characterize the different modes in which a #$Narrative is or can be presented (i.e. instantiated), e.g.           is it presented in a way intended to be comical or dramatic?") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaf9f).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aaf9f,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
