x_comment(x_ObjectTypeByColorTinge,"A collection of collections. Each instance is a collection of objects whose main color (c.f. #$mainColorOfObject) has a certain color tinge. For example, #$Purplish is the collection of all things that are mainly purplish.  Every instance of #$Color is a specialization of some instance of #$ObjectTypeByColorTinge.  Having a tinge of a certain color must not be confused with being a shade of that color. More precisely, possessing some instance of #$ObjectTypeByColorTinge, XISH, does not imply having the color X. For instance, an object can be an instance of #$Reddish, without being an instance of #$RedColor. Anything which is #$GrayishReddishBrown-Color is #$Reddish but isn't #$RedColor. Many colors have more than one instance of #$ObjectTypeByColorTinge as generalizations. #$GrayishPink-Color has both #$Grayish and #$Pinkish as generalizations.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aafb1).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aafb1,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
