x_comment(x_MunsellChroma,"The collection of degrees of chroma in the Munsell system of color classification.  Chroma, also known as saturation, is what gives a color its 'colorfulness'.  Colors with a low chroma are generally grayish or dull.  Colors with a high chroma are vivid, colorful.  Every chromatic color (i.e. colors that have a #$MunsellHue value) has a degree of chroma.  #$PureWhiteColor does not have any chroma value, nor does any shade of #$PureGrayColor.  #$PureBlackColor need not have chroma but regardless of hue or chroma, if a color has a brightness value of 0, it will be black.  Please also see #$SharedNoteOnMunsellSystemOfColorClassification.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aafe8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aafe8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
