x_comment(x_MunsellBrightness,"The collection of degrees of brightness with respect to colors.  In the Munsell system of color classification, every color has a brightness value, or a range of brightness values, which expresses the degree of brightness, or lightness, of that color.  Instances of #$MunsellBrightness are denoted by means of the expression #$MunsellBrightnessFn.  Generally, darker colors have a low degree of brightness, while lighter colors have a high degree of brightness.  #$PureBlackColor has a brightness of 0.  #$PureWhiteColor has a brightness of 100.  Please also see #$SharedNoteOnMunsellSystemOfColorClassification.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aaff0).
