x_comment('x_PropositionalConceptualWork-CultGenre',"The collection of instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork that are of the \ncult genre.  Works of this genre usually have an obsessive appeal to some sub-group of the fans of a particular genre.  There is usually some element of \"camp\" in instances of this \ngenre.  #$EvilDead-TheMovie is a good example of a movie in this genre.  This is not a \n\"true\" genre in that it doesn't actually describe the style of the work.   \nIn many cases the creator of the work had no intent to make something of this\ngenre.  #$EdWood-MovieDirector is a good example of someone with no such intent.  \nHis movies are considered, by most film critics, to be universally bad.  Yet, in spite of \nthis (or more likely, because of this) his movies are considered by certain people \nto be very fun to watch and have attracted a large \"cult\" following.          ") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab166).
