x_comment(x_ELInferenceBindingFn,"(#$ELInferenceBindingFn VAR TERM) denotes an instance of #$ELInferenceBinding which states that TERM can be substituted for VAR.  Bindings are produced as part of the result of a CycL query, when it is found that the query formula can be proven from the KB by substituting TERM for VAR.  The entire query result consists of a #$ELSetOfInferenceBindingSets, which includes zero or more #$ELInferenceBindingSets, each of which contains one #$ELInferenceBinding for each free variable present in the query formula.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab30d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab30d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab30d,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526ab30d,29235).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526ab30d,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526ab30d,[]).
x_comment(x_InferenceBindingSetFn,"(#$InferenceBindingSetFn BINDING-1 ... BINDING-N) denotes one #$InferenceBindingSet, which is one complete answer to a CycL query.  Each of BINDING-1 ... BINDING-N is an #$InferenceBinding, stating that some variable can be replaced with some Cyc term to prove the query formula true.  The result of a CycL query includes zero or more #$InferenceBindingSet instances, grouped together as a #$SetOfInferenceBindingSets.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab30e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab30e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab30e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526ab30e,29236).
