x_comment(x_SubjectiveSlotTrendPredicate,"A specialization of #$SlotTrendPredicate.  Instances are predicates used to represent ceteris paribus expectations of net increases and decreases of quantities over time.  For any instance PRED of #$SubjectiveSlotTrendPredicate, (PRED SIT THING SLOT) will indicate that given the #$Situation (or situation-type) SIT, the value of the\n\n#$QuantitySlot SLOT (i.e. the arg2 to SLOT) to be attributed to THING would\n\nbe higher or lower than some default or presupposed base value. The `everything else\n\nbeing equal' clause indicates that the value of SLOT for THING might\n\nchange, even in the opposite direction as that indicated by the assertion, were more information to become available about\n\nSIT. This class of predicates captures the subjective dimension of assignments of probability -- that is, an assignment of probability is always based on the amount of information available to an evaluator.  See the #$comment on #$increasesSitSlot-Subjective for more information.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab32e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab32e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
