x_comment(x_colorHasBrightness,"The formula (#$colorHasBrightness ?COLOR ?BRIGHT) states that the #$Color ?COLOR has the #$MunsellBrightness ?BRIGHT.  Each instance of #$MunsellBrightness is represented by a NAT formed with #$MunsellBrightnessFn.  The brightness of a color is the attribute that makes a color light or dark.  A brightness value of 0 results in #$PureBlackColor.  A value of 100, when no hue is present, results in #$PureWhiteColor. (Please see also the comment on #$MunsellChroma.)  All instances of #$Color have a brightness value somewhere between 0 and 100.  Please see also #$SharedNoteOnMunsellSystemOfColorClassification and the constant #$MunsellBrightness for further explanation.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab33b).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab33b,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
