x_comment(x_rightsGranted,"This predicate is used to indicate what instances of #$SituationTypeByUserRights some #$ChangeInUserRights is related to.  If (#$rightsGranted EVENT SIT-TYPE) holds, then in the #$ChangeInUserRights EVENT, the #$SituationTypeByUserRights SIT-TYPE is granted (to some agent).  What this means is that EVENT causes a particular user right situation to come about and that situation is an instance of SIT-TYPE.  Note: nothing is entailed about whether any user rights are currently enjoyed by any actors in EVENT.  #$rightsGranted simply states a causal connection between an event and a situation type.  It simply states that as a result of EVENT a certain instance of SIT-TYPE obtained.  Nothing further is inferrable about whether that instance of SIT-TYPE currently obtains.  For example, the Louisiana purchase resulted in the existence of a particular user right situation (the situation corresponding to the USA's having exclusive use rights to the territory purchased).  And this situation is an instance of #$ExclusiveUserRights (the collection of all situations in which an agent has exclusive user rights over something).  But, (#$rightsGranted LouisiannaPurchase #$ExclusiveUserRights) would still be true now even if we had\n\nsold the territory back to France 20 years later.  The predicate is used to state a bald fact that a certain instance of argument 2 obtained at least for a short time following the temporal extent of argument 1.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab343).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab343,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab343,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
