x_comment('x_ingredients-Separable',"The predicate #$ingredients-Separable is used to indicate a particular input used to make a particular artifact.  (#$ingredients-Separable ART INGR) means that the #$PartiallyTangible thing INGR was one of the #$inputs to the creation of the #$Artifact ART, and INGR is one of ART's #$physicalParts.  Note that #$ingredients-Separable applies only to those inputs which retain their identity in the creation process and which are incorporated into the resulting #$Artifact.  For example, a meatball can be considered an ingredient of a plate of spaghetti, and a portion of ground beef can be considered a separable ingredient of the meatball.  On the other hand, we would not say that an egg is a separable ingredient, but an #$ingredients-Destroyed, of the meatball, even though it was an input to the creation process, because its identity was not preserved.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab39d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab39d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
