x_comment(x_PartialOrderingAlongFn,"A binary function that returns an ordering relation.  (#$PartialOrderingAlongFn POP KEY) denotes a predicate that represents an ordering on the element of a set generated by applying the KEY to the elements of a set.  So where (#$baseSet ORDERING (#$TheSet #$JonC #$Kahlert #$Goolsbey)), (#$orderingRelations ORDERING (#$PartialOrderingAlongFn #$lessThan #$zipCode)) says that the #$PartialOrdering ORDERING is ordered by the zip codes of Jon, Robert, and Keith, where the smallest zip code is first, the next smallest second, and largest last.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab3e7).
