x_comment(x_resultSetCardinality,"This predicate is used by the SKSI code to estimate the cost of querying the fields of a physical schema.  More precisely, let SCHEMA denote a physical schema, let PF-1, PF-2, ..., PF-N, denote the physical fields of SCHEMA, and let SELECT_SET and WHERE_SET denote two disjoint subsets of (#$TheSet PF-1 PF-2 ... PF-N). Then (#$resultSetCardinality SCHEMA SELECT_SET WHERE_SET NUM) means that NUM is the average cardinality of the result set returned from a query in which the fields in SELECT_SET left unbound and the fields of WHERE_SET are bound.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab3e8).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab3e8,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
