x_comment(x_VeryLowToLowAmountFn,"A #$GenericValueFunction (q.v.) that takes a given #$TotallyOrderedQuantityType to a #$GenericQuantity of that type.  In a given context, <code>(#$VeryLowToLowAmountFn QUANTTYPE)</code> is the properly interval-like quantity (and instance) of <code>QUANTTYPE</code> that is considered a <i>very-low-to-low amount</i> of <code>QUANTTYPE</code> with respect to that context.\n<p>\nFor example, (#$VeryLowToLowAmountFn #$Happiness) is the range of happiness from very low to low happiness.  It is more (see #$followingValue) than (#$NoAmountFn #$Happiness) and less than (#$MediumAmountFn #$Happiness).\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding predicate #$veryLowToLowAmountOf.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab405).
