x_comment(x_tupleMemberIndex,"A predicate that relates a given tuple -- which is essentially a set whose members are indexed in some way -- and one of its members (see #$memberOfTuple) to the member's associated index (see #$tupleIndexSet). (#$tupleMemberIndex TUPLE MEMBER INDEX) means that INDEX serves to index or represent the position of MEMBER in TUPLE.  Each element of TUPLE is associated with at least one element of the index set, and no element of the index set is associated with more than one member of TUPLE.  Note that MEMBER might be indexed by more than one element of the index set, as a given member can have more than one \"appearance\" within a tuple.  The complete predicate extent of #$tupleMemberIndex with respect to TUPLE in effect represents a function (TUPLE's \"indexing function\") from the index set onto the set of TUPLE's members.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab426).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab426,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
