x_comment(x_regionalTelephoneAreaCode,"(#$regionalTelephoneAreaCode PLACE CODE) means that CODE is a telephone area (or city) code number for the #$GeopoliticalEntity or #$GeographicalRegion PLACE.  Most city/area codes are specific to specific country subsidaries, but some small island countries share a country code with a larger nearby country and have a unique city/area code for the whole country.  Most area/city codes are unique for their region of coverage, but the United States has started having multiple area codes covering the same regions.  Area/city codes cover both telephone and fax numbers, at least into the year 2002.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab458).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab458,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
