x_comment(x_TimeParameter,"This is a sub-collection of #$ModalIndex.  Each instance of #$TimeParameter can be used as a `parameter of time index' of formulas. When a formula PROP is asserted, by hand or inferred, with time index (#$TimeInterval) t and time parameter (#$TimeParameter) p (and other indices), PROP is taken to be true at t as well as every time interval t0 that is properly subsumed by t such that (#$temporallySubsumes-InsType t0 p) holds (other indices fixed).  For example, suppose that a formula PROP is asserted with (in addition to indices i_0, ..., i_k) the time index 05/01/02 and the time parameter #$CalendarSecond.  This means that PROP is taken to be true not only at 05/01/02, but also at each calendar hour and each calendar second temporally subsumed by 05/01/02 (with all other indices i_0, ..., i_k fixed).  There are two kinds of time parameters, one kind is #$SameLengthTimeIntervalType, and each time parameter of this kind contains time intervals of the same length (the so-called `sliding' time parameters); and the other kind includes the rest of #$TimeParameter, and each time parameter of that kind contains time intervals, often disjoint, which are fixed on the time line.  Among the second type of time parameters, there is an important class, #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries, which is used for reasoning with metric tenses.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab466).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab466,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab466,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
