x_comment('x_Mission-AssignedActionType',"An instance of this collection is a specialization of #$Situation representing a mission in the sense commonly intended in the context of planning, in particular military planning. In such contexts, a `mission' is typically a normative specification of an action or complex action to be performed by a designated agent. Accordingly, the two key aspects of a mission are (i) the goal of the mission, that is, the end state the designated agent ought to bring about by executing the mission, and (ii) a specification, at a very general level, of the type of action that is expected to fulfill the mission. A typical instance of mission in a military planning context would be something like 'secure area Z by blocking all land access corridors', which can be taken as indicating both the type of state that must obtain at the end of a successful execution and the general type of operation that must be executed. In our representation, such a mission would be an instance of #$Mission-AssignedActionType, that is: a specialization of #$Situation in which (cf. #$SituationTypeSuchThatFn and #$situationTypeIsSuchThat) area Z has been secured by blocking  actions. Note that because situation types can in principle be described by propositions, there is a one-one correspondence between #$Mission-AssignedActionType and #$MissionSpecificationMicrotheory -- much like in the case of the more specific #$CourseOfAction and #$COASpecificationMicrotheory (q.v.).") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab4bb).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab4bb,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab4bb,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526ab4bb,29894).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526ab4bb,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526ab4bb,[]).
x_comment(x_missionDescribingSpecification,"(#$missionDescribingSpecification MISSION MT) is true iff MT is\nthe instance of #$MissionSpecificationMicrotheory that describes the facts\nobtaining in the situation type MISSION.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab4bc).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab4bc,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab4bc,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
