x_comment(x_ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries,"A specialization of #$ConventionalClassificationType and #$TimeParameter.  Each member TYPE of #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries is a conventionally named 'series' of 'solid' time intervals in the sense that, for each instance t of TYPE, one can meaningfully speak of 'the one before t' or 'the one after t' in the sequence (or speak of 'the last one' or 'the next one' etc. in the sequence if we are to temporally locate ourselves in t). Examples of instances of this collection are #$Friday and #$CalendarYear etc.  Specializations of this collection include #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries-Disjoint, #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries-DisjointWithGaps, #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries-Covering and #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries-CoveringAndDisjoint.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab512).
