x_comment(x_SpindleMicrotheory,"The collection of all microtheories which are the spindle elements.  A spindle microtheory system is one in which sibling spindle microtheories each have #$genlMt links to a superior #$CollectorMicrotheory, which has its own links to relevant contexts.  Additionally there exists a subordinate #$CollectorMicrotheory (inference microtheory) that has #$genlMt links to each of the spindle microtheories.  The name spindle derives from the visual metaphor of a spinning wheel spindle placed on its side in which the spokes represent the #$genlMt links.  Spindle microtheory systems are useful for organizing a set of contexts having shared assumptions, and requiring an inference context from which all are visible.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab52d).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab52d,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
