x_comment(x_mainColorsOfObject,"The formula (#$mainColorsOfObject OBJ COLOR-SCHEME) means that the #$PartiallyTangible OBJ is almost entirely colored with the #$Colors from the set of colors in COLOR-SCHEME.  For example, since a #$Zebra is roughly equally black and white, we would not say that it is primarily either of those colors. So neither (#$mainColorOfObject MyZebra #$BlackColor) nor (#$mainColorOfObject MyZebra #$WhiteColor) would be true.  And the assertion (#$objectHasColor MyZebra #$WhiteColor) would be too weak for this case where #$WhiteColor is one of the Zebra's main colors. COLOR-SCHEME could either be a set of colors formed using #$TheSet or it could be an instance of #$ColorScheme, which is itself a specialization of (#$SetOfTypeFn #$Color).") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab53c).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab53c,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
