x_comment(x_PublicTelephone,"The collection of all telephones situated to allow use by the general public for placing telephone calls.  Some public telephones can receive calls, while others cannot.  In the vast majority of the cases, the user must pay for placing a call.  A user does not have to pay for receiving a call on a public telephone (as of fall 2002).  Public telephones, often called ``pay phones'', normally have specific hardware for collecting money and as a result have structural features to prevent such money (and the phones themselves) from being stolen.  Some newer pay phones accept electronic money (e.g. using credit/debit cards, phone cards) as well, or instead of, accepting cash.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab56a).
