x_comment(x_WaitingList,"The collection of all waiting lists.  People, cars to be serviced, and jobs to be done can all be arranged in [be #$seriesMembers of] a waiting list.  Items on the waiting list in order to participate in some type of activity in the future which it cannot participate in at the present time due to other items of a similar time occupying limited resources.  On most waiting lists there is an assurance that the item on the list will participate in an instance of the activity type it is awaiting if it is left on the list long enough.  However, some waiting lists are for event types in which an absolute limit on the number of participants means that those waiting will only participate if others, further along in the process, drop out.  A waiting list changes over time with new things being placed on the list and old things being taken off.\n<p>\nSome instances of waiting list have criteria for the next type of item to be removed from the list to be serviced, which may mean that the next party that fits the criteria will be taken instead instead, for example, the next table to open for seating in a restaurant may not seat everyone who is in the next party on the restaurant's waiting list.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab56e).
