x_comment(x_toTheRightOf,"(#$toTheRightOf OBJ1 OBJ2) says that OBJ1 is located to OBJ2's right.  Thus the arg2 of #$toTheRightOf is restricted to instances of #$LeftAndRightSidedObject. The arg1 can be any instance of #$SpatialThing-Localized.  Because of this asymmetry in argument restrictions, #$toTheRightOf is not sufficient for representing all cases in which one object is to the left of another (see #$toTheLeftOf).  Note that this predicate cannot be used to state that an object is to the right of another, from the perspective of a third party, except as an argument in a #$perceivesThat assertion.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab5a6).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab5a6,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab5a6,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
