xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526ab5a7,[]).
x_comment(x_toTheLeftOf,"(#$toTheLeftOf OBJ1 OBJ2) says that OBJ1 is located to OBJ2's left.  Thus the arg2 of #$toTheLeftOf is restricted to instances of #$LeftAndRightSidedObject. The arg1 can be any instance of #$SpatialThing-Localized.  Because of this asymmetry in argument restrictions, #$toTheRightOf is not sufficient for representing all cases in which one object is to the right of another (see #$toTheRightOf).  Note that this predicate cannot be used to state that an object is to the left of another, from the perspective of a third party, except as an argument in a #$perceivesThat assertion.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab5a8).
