x_comment(x_expectedResponseToEventType,"(#$expectedResponseToEventType AGT TYPE RESPONSE-TYPE ROLE) says that in response to an instance of TYPE, AGT is expected to play the role ROLE in an instance of RESPONSE-TYPE.  More formally,  (#$expected-ToBe (#$thereExists ?RESPONSE-INS (#$and (#$isa ?RESPONSE-INS RESPONSE-TYPE) (ROLE ?RESPONSE-INS AGT)))).  This predicate is particularly useful in representing expectations to responses to executions of plans (See #$Plan-ExpectedSituationType).") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab5ac).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab5ac,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
