x_comment(x_UserAccountGroup,"A specialization of #$Group. Each instance of this collection is a 'group' as defined on a computer network as a named set of #$UserAccounts which share a given set of access permissions to certain network resources (see, for example #$groupAccountForFile). Groups may be defined along functional, departmental, or other lines, and users may belong to a number of groups. However, each user account will be a member of just one primary group, which will be associated by default with the files that that user creates. A group is related to its user accounts by the predicate #$groupMembers (q.v.). Note that instances of #$UserAccountGroup, being #$Groups, are not #$Collections.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab5c3).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab5c3,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
