x_comment('x_Packet-SYN',"#$Packet-SYN is a #$Packet-Internet.  When a computer wishes to establish a network connection to another computer, according to the #$InternetProtocol, a #$Packet-SYN (synchronization request packet) is sent from the originating computer to a specific port that is in a \"listen\" state on another computer.  The listening computer sends a SYN/ACK (synchronize/acknowledge) packet back to the first computer, which completes the handshake by sending an #$Packet-ACK (acknowledge packet).") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab5ff).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab5ff,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
