x_comment('x_Packet-ACK',"#$Packet-ACK is a #$Packet-Internet, and is the last part of the threeway handshake that occurs when a computer wishes to establish a network connection to another computer.  According to the #$InternetProtocol, a SYN (synchronization request) packet is sent from the originating computer to a specific port that is in a \"listen\" state on another computer.  The listening computer sends a SYN/ACK (synchronize/acknowledge) packet back to the first computer, which completes the handshake by sending an #$Packet-ACK (acknowledge packet).") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab600).
