x_comment(x_aggregateSituationType,"(#$aggregateSituationType SIT-TYPE AG-TYPE) means that AG-TYPE is the collection of situations whose instances are composed (a la #$subSituations) of multiple instances of SIT-TYPE.  AG-TYPE is agnostic as to whether its instances are composed of serially-occurring instances of SIT-TYPE, instances which occur in parallel, or some mix thereof.  The genls of AG-TYPE is determined by the value for AG-SIT-TYPE in (#$typeAggregatesIntoType SIT-TYPE AG-SIT-TYPE).") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab614).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab614,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab614,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526ab614,30460).
