xc_source_line(a65b16526ab617,30463).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526ab617,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526ab617,[]).
x_comment(x_aggregateRole,"(#$aggregateRole ROLE AG-ROLE) means that AG-ROLE is an instance of #$BinaryRolePredicate which is related to ROLE in that whenever both (ROLE ?SITUATION ?OBJ) and (AG-ROLE ?SITUATION ?GROUP) hold, ?OBJ is a member of ?GROUP.  In other words, AG-ROLE is a #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates a situation to the group consisting of all the situation participants which relate to it via ROLE.  For example, consider a dishwashing event Dishwashing001 in which many dishes are washed.  Each dish that is washed is an #$objectActedOn in Dishwashing001.  If (#$aggregateRole #$objectActedOn AG-ROLE), then each washed dish is also a member of a group, call it DishGroup001, such that (AG-ROLE Dishwashing001 DishGroup001).") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab618).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab618,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab618,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526ab618,30464).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526ab618,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526ab618,[]).
x_comment(x_AggregateRoleFn,"(#$AggregateRoleFn ROLE) denotes an instance of #$BinaryRolePredicate which is related to ROLE in that whenever both (ROLE ?SITUATION ?OBJ) and ((#$AggregateRoleFn ROLE) ?SITUATION ?GROUP) hold, ?OBJ is a member of ?GROUP.  In other words, (#$AggregateRoleFn ROLE) is a #$BinaryRolePredicate that relates a situation to the group consisting of all the situation participants which relate to it via ROLE.  For example, consider a dishwashing event Dishwashing001 in which many dishes are washed.  Each dish that is washed is an #$objectActedOn in Dishwashing001.  Each washed dish is also a member of a group, call it DishGroup001, such that ((#$AggregateRoleFn ROLE) Dishwashing001 DishGroup001).") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab619).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab619,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
