x_comment(x_Ketone,"Ketones are organic molecules consisting of a carbonyl radical (C = O) bonded to two other carbon radicals, wherein the two available carbon bonds of the carbonyl are used to attach the carbon atoms of the other radicals. One good example is acetone (a.k.a. dimethyl ketone), in which the carbon atom of the carbonyl is attached to the carbon atoms of two methyl radicals CH3- . The resulting formula is CO(CH3)2.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab654).
