x_comment(x_Trinitrotoluene,"A specialization of #$HighExplosive. Each instance of #$Trinitrotoluene is a yellow crystalline compound that is a flammable toxic derivative of #$Toluene, and is typically referred to as \"TNT\".  TNT is often  used as a high explosive, and it is a constituent of many explosives, such as #$Amatol, pentolite, tetrytol, torpex, #$Tritonal, picratol, ednatol, and #$CompositionB.  In a refined form, TNT is a very stable high explosive with a long shelf life.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab655).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab655,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
