x_comment('x_chemicalEquation-Balanced',"A quintary predicate used to describe the balanced chemical equation for a given type of #$ChemicalReaction. In a gaf of the form (#$chemicalEquation-Balanced R-TYPE LIST1 LIST2 LIST3  LIST4), LIST1 and LIST3 are lists of chemical substances, and LIST2 and LIST4 are list of numbers each of which is the balancing coefficient of the corresponding element in, respectively, LIST1 and LIST3. Thus, (#$chemicalEquation-Balanced R-TYPE (#$TheList COMPOUND-1 COMPOUND-2) (#$TheList 2 3) (#$TheList PRODUCT-1 PRODUCT-2) (#$TheList 1 4)) means that in the type of chemical reaction denoted by R-TYPE 2 units of COMPOUND-1 and 3 units of COMPOUND-2 result in 1 unit of PRODUCT-1 and 4 units of PRODUCT-2. Just as in the case of #$chemicalEquation-Balanced, one should not assume that the equilibrium of REACTION-TYPE lies entirely to the right of the equation.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab688).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab688,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
