x_comment(x_Protocol,"A spec of #$Instructions. A #$Protocol specifies how one or more agents should behave, in order to be considered to form part of, or to be participating in, some larger system.\n<p>\nExamples: there are certain rules about how a surrender should be negotiated in war. There are rules about a way a person should behave at a rave, or in the presence of the Queen of England.\nThere are rules about how one should behave in order to participate in a committee.\n<p>\nThere are also rules that specify how a device should behave electrically in order to be considered a node on a 10 base-T Ethernet network, and there are rules about what types of messages to send to interact with a SOAP-based service on a network.\n<p>\nProtocol is currently partitioned into #$HumanProtocol and #$MachineProtocol. Specializations of #$HumanProtocol include #$DiplomaticProtocol and #$SocialProtocol.\n<p>\nInstances of #$MachineProtocol include #$EthernetProtocol, #$IDEProtocol, #$SOAPProtocol.\n<p>\nSince the #$Protocol subcollections are called XProtocol (for some X), individual #$Protocols should be called Y-TheProtocol.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab6d4).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab6d4,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab6d4,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b16526ab6d4,30719).
xc_kb_names(a65b16526ab6d4,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b16526ab6d4,[]).
x_comment(x_MachineProtocol,"A specialization of #$Protocol and #$Specification. The collection of all protocols that specify how machines should behave in order to participate in some larger system or to be considered to be of a particular type. To be considered a #$Protocol, this interaction of system with system must involve communication, as opposed to direct action as gears perform on each other in a gearbox.\n<p>\nExamples: There are rules that specify how a device should behave electrically in order to be considered a node on a 10 base-T Ethernet network, and there are rules about what types of messages to send to interact with a SOAP-based service on a network.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab6d5).
