x_comment(x_FissileMaterial,"A specialization of #$FissionableMaterial.  Each instance of #$FissileMaterial is a portion of material that can undergo nuclear fission after capturing a neutron of any energy.  They are to be contrasted with \"fissionable isotopes\" (see #$FissionableMaterial), which fission only after the capture of neutrons with energies above some threshold value.  Many heavy isotopes are fissionable, but many fewer of them are also fissile, and almost all of these are isotopes of uranium or plutonium.  All fissile materials and some fissionable materials are usable in weapons.  It is the odd-numbered isotopes of uranium and plutonium that are fissile: U-233, U-235 and Pu-239, Pu-241. U-235 and Pu-239 are the most common and are the best weapon materials.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab77e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab77e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
