x_comment(x_MunsellBrightnessFn,"This function takes as an argument one or two #$SubLIntegers, from 0 to 100, and returns a #$MunsellBrightness as its value. For example, (MunsellBrightnessFn 75) is the #$MunsellBrightness of degree 75, which would be a fairly bright color. (#$MunsellBrightnessFn 25), on the other hand, would be the brightness of a dark color. Every color has a degree of brightness. Please see #$MunsellBrightness and #$colorHasBrightness for further explanation.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab7fe).
