x_comment(x_MunsellChromaFn,"This function takes as an argument one or two #$SubLIntegers and returns a \n#$MunsellChroma as its value. For example, (MunsellChromaFn 100) is the \n#$MunsellChroma of degree 100. Since the majority of colors (though not all) \nhave chromas ranging between 0 and 150, this is a relatively high chroma, and will \nmost likely apply to a moderately or highly saturated color. Also note that unlike \nother functions that express values related to the Munsell system of color \nclassification, there is no known upper limit on the domain of MunsellChromaFn. \nSome colors, such as flourescent colors, can have chromas of 300 or higher. Please \nsee #$MunsellChroma and #$colorHasChroma for further explanation.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab7ff).
