x_comment('x_completeChemicalComposition-List',"(#$completeChemicalComposition-List CHEM_SUBSTANCE_TYPE LIST_OF_GROUPS) means that molecules of CHEM_SUBSTANCE_TYPE, an instance of #$ChemicalSubstanceTypes, has a chemical formula expressed by the following list.  Elements of the list are collections of groups of a single cardinality of chemical objects of the same species [#$GroupOfCardinalityOfChemObjectTypeBySpecies], normally expressed using either #$AtomGroupingFn or #$ChemicalObjectGroupingFn.  The order of groups in the list is conventional and gives an idea of the structure of instances of the molecule type.\n<p>\nFor example:\n<p>\n(#$completeChemicalComposition-List #$AceticAcid\n(#$TheList\n(#$AtomGroupingFn #$Carbon 1)\n(#$AtomGroupingFn #$Hydrogen 3)\n(#$AtomGroupingFn #$Carbon 1)\n(#$AtomGroupingFn #$Oxygen 1)\n(#$ChemicalObjectGroupingFn #$HydroxideRadical 1)))\n<p>\nmeans what the chemical formula for #$AceticAcid being CH3COOH expresses.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab868).
