x_comment(x_MonadicMicrotheory,"A #$MonadicMicrotheory is a temporally and otherwise unqualified #$Microtheory; it is indivisible along all currently defined microtheory dimensions (see #$MtSpace and #$MtDim).  For example, #$PeopleDataMt is a #$MonadicMicrotheory, but (#$MtSpace #$PeopleDataMt) is not; nor is (#$MtSpace #$PeopleDataMt (#$MtDim #$mtTimeIndex (#$YearFn 1955))).  Note, however, that a #$MonadicMicrotheory need not be atomic: (#$MtOfBeliefSystemFn #$Buddhism) is a #$MonadicMicrotheory.  Together with #$PolyadicMicrotheory, this partitions #$Microtheory.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab87e).
