x_comment(x_cotemporalSubSituationTypes,"<code>(#$cotemporalSubSituationTypes SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2)</code> means that in any instance <code>SIT</code> of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> (a specialization of #$Situation), if instances <code>SIT1</code> and <code>SIT2</code> of <code>SUBSIT-TYPE1</code> and <code>SUBSIT-TYPE2</code> occur as subsituations, then <code>SIT1</code> and <code>SIT2</code> are cotemporal.\n<p>\nNote that <code>(#$cotemporalSubSituationTypes SIT-TYPE SUBSIT-TYPE1 SUBSIT-TYPE2)</code> does not imply that instances of <code>SUBSIT-TYPE1</code> or <code>SUBSIT-TYPE2</code> occur as subsituations of every instance of <code>SIT-TYPE</code>, since <code>SUBSIT-TYPE1</code> and <code>SUBSIT-TYPE2</code> may be merely candidate subsituation types of <code>SIT-TYPE</code> (see #$candidateProperSubSituationTypes).") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab8ce).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab8ce,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab8ce,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
