x_comment(x_solubilityValueOfSubstanceType,"(#$solubilityValueOfSubstanceType\nSOLUTE SOLVENT VALUE) means that VALUE is the solubility constant of the\nsubstance type SOLUTE in the substance type SOLVENT at 25C temperature. The\nsolubility constant of a substance type SOLUTE is the maximum amount of an\ninstance of SOLUTE that can be dissolved in a given quantity of the type\nSOLVENT. This constant can be expressed in a variety of inter-reducible\nways: here we use mass fraction of solute, a percentage measure: ie.,\nVALUE = m2 / (m1 + m2), where m1 is the mass of solvent and m2 is the mass\nof solute in a saturated solution. An example:\n(#$solubilityValueOfSubstanceType #$Salt-NaCl (#$LiquidFn Water) 0.265), meaning that a saturated solution of NaCl at 25C will contain 26.5 grams per 100 grams of water.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab93c).
