x_comment(x_objectHasColor,"(#$objectHasColor OBJECT COLOR-COLL) means that some visible part of OBJECT is \ncolored COLOR-COLL. This is the most general of the color predicates; for more specialized \npredicates see #$significantColorOfObject, #$mainColorOfObject, and \n#$uniformColorOfObject. Note that, unlike these latter three predicates, \n#$objectHasColor is not a specialization of #$isa. This is because an object's having \nsome part that's a certain color does not entail that the object itself, as a whole, is \ncharacterized by that color in the sense of belonging to that color collection.") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab975).
