x_comment(x_TemporalMicrotheory,"Each instance MT of #$TemporalMicrotheory is a microtheory that has the following characteristics. (i) MT has a time interval TIME as the value of `time index' (see #$MtTimeDimFn and #$mtTimeIndex), be it a time point, or an hour, or a day, or a stage in a plan or in a scenerio, or any other amount except the empty interval and `gappy' intervals.  (ii) MT has a time interval type PARA (an instance of #$TimeParameter) as the value of its `time parameter' (see #$MtTimeWithGranularityDimFn and #$mtTimeIndexWithParameter), be it #$CalendarDay, (#$SameLengthTimeIntervalTypeFn (#$DaysDuration 1)) or #$Null-TimeParameter (also see #$TimeInterval, #$TimeParameter and #$MtSpace). (iii) Each statement PROP in MT (either asserted or inferred) is understood in the following way: (1) PROP is true _at_ TIME, and (2) for each time interval T subsumed by TIME, if (#$temporallySubsumes-InsType T PARA) holds, PROP is true at T, and (3) other conditions specified in terms of the values of MT's other dimensions.  Note that if MT-1 and MT-2 are instances of #$TemporalMicrotheory such that MT-1 has `time index' T-1 and `time parameter' P-1 and such that MT-2 has `time index' T-2 and `time parameter' P-2 (and the rest of them are the same), then the following are (jointly) sufficient and necessary conditions for (#$genlMt MT-2 MT-1) to hold: (a) (#$temporallySubsumes T-1 T-2), (b) (#$temporallySubsumes-TypeType P-2 P-1) and (c) (#$temporallySubsumes-InsType T-2 P-1).") :- x_cid(a65b16526ab97e).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526ab97e,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526ab97e,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
