x_comment(x_MatrixSolutionFn,"#$MatrixSolutionFn is an #$EvaluatableFunction that calculates the solution to a set of linear equations.  (#$MatrixSolutionFn MATRIX) denotes the solution (should one exist) to the integer matrix MATRIX.  By 'integer matrix', we mean a #$List of #$Lists (of the same length) of #$Integers.  By 'the solution to the matrix', we mean the #$List of #$Integers that is the lowest whole-number solution to the set of linear equations that the matrix represents; each row of the matrix (#$TheList <a1> <a2> ... <an>) being interpreted as the linear equation <a1>*x1 + <a2>*x2 + ... + <an-1>*xn-1 = <an>*xn.  In other words, if (#$MatrixSolutionFn MATRIX) evaluates to (#$TheList <b1> <b2> ... <bn>), that means that <b1>, <b2>, ... , and <bn> are values of the variables x1, x2, ... , and xn, respectively, for which all of the equations represented by rows of the matrix are true.  If there is no solution to the matrix, or if there are infinitely many lowest whole-number solutions, then (#$MatrixSolutionFn MATRIX) denotes nothing.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aba07).
xc_microtheory(a65b16526aba07,x_UniversalVocabularyMt).
xc_source_file(a65b16526aba07,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/UniversalVocabularyMt.part05.krf').
