x_comment(x_contributesToSpeciesInSample,"(#$contributesToSpeciesInSample SAMPLE SUBSTANCE ION-TYPE INTERVAL) means that a certain (unspecified) amount of #$ChemicalSpeciesType SUBSTANCE contributes #$ScalarInterval INTERVAL amount of #$IonTypeByChemicalSpecies ION-TYPE to the #$PartiallyTangible SAMPLE.  (#$contributesToSpeciesInSample SAMPLE SUBSTANCE ION-TYPE INTERVAL) implies that SUBSTANCE is \"in\" SAMPLE (for the relevant sense of \"in\", see #$molarityOfSubstanceInSample). Also, if it is true that (#$contributesToSpeciesInSample SAMPLE SUBSTANCE ION-TYPE INTERVAL), it is possible for INTERVAL to be \"zero\" -- i.e, it is possible that SUBSTANCE contributes no amount of ION-TYPE to SAMPLE.  However, it is not possible for SUBSTANCE to contribute a \"negative amount\" of ION-TYPE to SAMPLE.") :- x_cid(a65b16526aba26).
